-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc1 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, Part I (ss 1 to 19B) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in
-- Great Britain, asking on facts they can state whether and how much they must pay in contributions.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the ssc1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here is
-- new law and no rule is restated: each question builds the modules' records from plain answers, in its WHERE, and calls the SAME module rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or one of the modules' own choices), one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- WHAT THE PERSON CANNOT STATE. The figures that regulations or orders set for a tax year (the earnings limits and thresholds of s 5(1), the
-- qualifying earnings factor of Schedule 3, the maximum number of Class 3A units) are asked as plain numbers: the person reads them from the
-- published rates. The percentages and sums the Act itself states (8% and 2% in s 8(2); 15% in s 9(2); GBP 7,105 in s 11(4)(b); GBP 3.65
-- in s 11(6); GBP 18.40 in s 13(1); GBP 12,570, GBP 50,270, 6% and 2% in ss 15(3) and (3ZA)) are taken as the Act states them (the modules'
-- own constants); the Act says they can be altered by order or regulations, so a later substitution would change these answers.
--
-- ANSWERS ARE THREE-VALUED. JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text answering in its own words; NOTHING means the text, or the facts given,
-- do not decide the question ("not covered"). A caller must never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- Not in this seat: Class 1B (s 10A(1): payable by a person accountable to the Inland Revenue under a PAYE settlement agreement) and
-- everything addressed to the Crown or the Treasury; they are in layer 1 for what they decide. The questions about what an employer pays (ss 6(1)(b), 9(1), 10(1), 10(4) and
-- 10ZA(3)) are here because a worker asks them, and they are phrased from the worker's side ("must my employer pay ...").

§ `Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, Part I -- the questions of a person who works, is self-employed or claims in Great Britain`

§§ `Who is an earner (ss 1 to 3)`

-- Everyone: the form can always show this group.

-- s 2(1)(a). An "employed earner" is a person gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service, or in an office
-- (including an elective office) with earnings.
@export Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner?
GIVEN `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2(1)(a), am I an employed earner` IS
    `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
    WHERE
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: s 2(1)(a) does not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a) reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 2(1)(b). A "self-employed earner" is a person gainfully employed in Great Britain otherwise than in employed earner's employment,
-- whether or not they are also employed in such employment.
@export Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner?
GIVEN `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2(1)(b), am I a self-employed earner` IS
    `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
    WHERE
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: s 2(1)(b) does not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(b) reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 2(5). A person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects any week during any part of which they are such an earner.
@export Under section 2(5), am I treated as a self-employed earner for a week?
GIVEN `I was a self-employed earner during some part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a self-employed earner during any part of the week?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 2(5), am I treated as a self-employed earner for a week` IS
    `s 2(5) the person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects the week` `I was a self-employed earner during some part of the week`

-- s 3(1)(a). "Earnings" includes any remuneration or profit derived from an employment.
@export Under section 3(1)(a), is what I receive earnings?
GIVEN `it is remuneration or profit derived from an employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment remuneration or profit that you derive from an employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 3(1)(a), is what I receive earnings` IS
    `s 3(1)(a) the payment is earnings` `it is remuneration or profit derived from an employment`

-- s 1(6)(a). No person is liable to pay a Class 1, 1A, 1B or 2 contribution unless they fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence
-- or presence in Great Britain. The conditions themselves are prescribed outside the Act, so whether you fulfil them is a plain fact.
@export Under section 1(6)(a), am I liable to pay a contribution of this class?
GIVEN `the class of contribution` IS A `Class of contribution` @desc Which class of contribution is it? (Class 1 primary, Class 1 secondary, Class 1A, Class 1B, Class 2, Class 3, Class 3A or Class 4)
      `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1(6)(a), am I liable to pay a contribution of this class` IS
    `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `the class of contribution` `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`

-- s 1(6)(b). No person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions unless they fulfil the same conditions.
@export Under section 1(6)(b), am I entitled to pay Class 3 contributions?
GIVEN `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 1(6)(b), am I entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` IS
    `s 1(6)(b) the person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain`

§§ `Payments treated as earnings (ss 4 to 4C)`

-- Only if the person receives a statutory payment (sick, maternity, paternity, adoption, shared parental, parental bereavement or neonatal care pay), or does
-- work for a client through an intermediary such as their own company: the form can ask "Do either of these apply to you?" before showing the group.

-- s 4(1)(a). A statutory payment (sick pay, maternity pay and the like) paid to or for your benefit in satisfaction of your entitlement is
-- treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment.
@export Under section 4(1)(a), is a statutory payment I receive treated as pay from employed earner's employment?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Statutory payment` @desc Which statutory payment is it? (statutory sick pay, statutory maternity pay, statutory paternity pay, statutory adoption pay, statutory shared parental pay, statutory parental bereavement pay or statutory neonatal care pay)
      `it is paid to me or for my benefit in satisfaction of my entitlement to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum paid to you, or for your benefit, in satisfaction (whole or part) of your entitlement to the payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4(1)(a), is a statutory payment I receive treated as pay from employed earner's employment` IS
    `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `the payment` `it is paid to me or for my benefit in satisfaction of my entitlement to it`

-- s 4A(7). A worker who is under an obligation personally to perform services is treated, for s 4A, as performing them.
@export Under section 4A(7), am I treated as performing the services?
GIVEN `I perform the services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform the services?
      `I am under an obligation personally to perform the services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under an obligation personally to perform the services?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 4A(7), am I treated as performing the services` IS
    `s 4A(7) the worker is treated as performing the services` `I perform the services` `I am under an obligation personally to perform the services`

§§ `Class 1 contributions (ss 5 to 9B)`

-- Only if the person is paid earnings from an employment (or office): the form can ask "Are you paid by an employer?" before showing the group.

-- s 6(1)(a), with ss 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3). A primary Class 1 contribution is payable by an employed earner over 16 on earnings paid in a tax
-- week in one employment if the amount paid exceeds the primary threshold, unless a Class 1B contribution is payable on them, or they are paid
-- after pensionable age (except as prescribed), or you do not fulfil the residence conditions. The thresholds are set for each tax year by
-- regulations: read them from the published rates.
@export Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings?
GIVEN `the amount I was paid in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you paid in the pay period, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were you paid? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the number of the tax week` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax week of that year were you paid? (1 to 53; tax week 1 begins on 6 April)
      `the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the primary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the primary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the secondary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
      `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
      `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a Class 1B contribution payable on these earnings (they are in a PAYE settlement agreement)?
      `I was paid after I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid after you attained pensionable age?
      `the regulations prescribe otherwise for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe otherwise for your case (for example, a prescribed exception to the pensionable-age rule)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6(1)(a), must I pay a primary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` IS
    `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)`
        `my earnings` `my limits` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
        `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings`
        `I was paid after I attained pensionable age` `the regulations prescribe otherwise for my case`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
            `the amount in pounds` IS `the amount I was paid in pounds`
            `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
                `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
                `number of the week in the year` IS `the number of the tax week`
        `my limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
            `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
            `lower earnings limit` IS `the lower earnings limit`
            `primary threshold` IS `the primary threshold`
            `upper earnings limit` IS `the upper earnings limit`
            `secondary threshold` IS `the secondary threshold`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: s 6(1) does not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a), called by s 6(1), reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 8(1). Where a primary Class 1 contribution is payable as in s 6(1)(a), you pay the main primary percentage (8% as the Act states it) of
-- the earnings above the primary threshold up to the upper earnings limit, and the additional primary percentage (2%) of those above it.
@export Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount I was paid in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you paid in the pay period, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were you paid? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the number of the tax week` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax week of that year were you paid? (1 to 53; tax week 1 begins on 6 April)
      `the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the primary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the primary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the secondary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
      `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
      `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a Class 1B contribution payable on these earnings (they are in a PAYE settlement agreement)?
      `I was paid after I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid after you attained pensionable age?
      `the regulations prescribe otherwise for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe otherwise for your case (for example, a prescribed exception to the pensionable-age rule)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 8(1), how much primary Class 1 contribution must I pay on these earnings` IS
    `s 8(1) the amount of the primary Class 1 contribution` `my primary contribution is payable` `the amount I was paid in pounds` `my limits`
        `s 8(2)(a) the main primary percentage as the Act states it` `s 8(2)(b) the additional primary percentage as the Act states it`
    WHERE
        `my primary contribution is payable` MEANS
            `s 6 a primary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a), 6(2) and 6(3)`
                `my earnings` `my limits` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
                `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings`
                `I was paid after I attained pensionable age` `the regulations prescribe otherwise for my case`
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
            `the amount in pounds` IS `the amount I was paid in pounds`
            `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
                `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
                `number of the week in the year` IS `the number of the tax week`
        `my limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
            `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
            `lower earnings limit` IS `the lower earnings limit`
            `primary threshold` IS `the primary threshold`
            `upper earnings limit` IS `the upper earnings limit`
            `secondary threshold` IS `the secondary threshold`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a), called by s 6(1), reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 6(1)(b), with ss 1(6)(a) and 6(2). A secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, by the employer or other secondary contributor, on
-- earnings paid to an employed earner over 16 if the amount paid exceeds the secondary threshold. It is not reduced by your age at payment.
@export Under section 6(1)(b), must my employer pay a secondary Class 1 contribution on these earnings?
GIVEN `the amount I was paid in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you paid in the pay period, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were you paid? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the number of the tax week` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax week of that year were you paid? (1 to 53; tax week 1 begins on 6 April)
      `the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the primary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the primary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the secondary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
      `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
      `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a Class 1B contribution payable on these earnings (they are in a PAYE settlement agreement)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6(1)(b), must my employer pay a secondary Class 1 contribution on these earnings` IS
    `s 6 a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a) and 6(2)`
        `my earnings` `my limits` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
        `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
            `the amount in pounds` IS `the amount I was paid in pounds`
            `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
                `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
                `number of the week in the year` IS `the number of the tax week`
        `my limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
            `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
            `lower earnings limit` IS `the lower earnings limit`
            `primary threshold` IS `the primary threshold`
            `upper earnings limit` IS `the upper earnings limit`
            `secondary threshold` IS `the secondary threshold`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a), called by s 6(1), reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 9(1). Where a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable as in s 6(1)(b), the employer pays the relevant percentage of the earnings
-- above the secondary threshold: 15% as the Act states it, or the age-related percentage (s 9A) or 0% (s 9B, a relevant apprentice). The
-- table of s 9A(3) is omitted from the text, so the age-related percentage is read from the published rates. Where regulations provide an
-- upper secondary threshold (ss 9A(7), 9B(4)), the earnings above it carry the 15% rate.
@export Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount I was paid in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you paid in the pay period, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were you paid? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the number of the tax week` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax week of that year were you paid? (1 to 53; tax week 1 begins on 6 April)
      `the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the primary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the primary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the secondary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
      `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain?
      `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a Class 1B contribution payable on these earnings (they are in a PAYE settlement agreement)?
      `I fall within an age group specified in column 1 of the table in section 9A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within an age group for which a lower age-related secondary percentage is specified (the table in section 9A(3))?
      `the age-related secondary percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the age-related secondary percentage for your age group, as a decimal (0.1 for 10%; 0 if no age group applies)?
      `I am under 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under the age of 25?
      `I am employed as an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in this employment as an apprentice?
      `regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for my age group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for your age group?
      `the upper secondary threshold for my age group` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that upper secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices?
      `the upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that upper secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 9(1), how much secondary Class 1 contribution must my employer pay on these earnings` IS
    `s 9(1) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution` `my secondary contribution is payable` `the amount I was paid in pounds` `my limits`
        `section 9A applies` `section 9B applies` `the age-related secondary percentage` `s 9(2) the secondary percentage as the Act states it`
        `my upper threshold for my age group` `my upper threshold as a relevant apprentice`
    WHERE
        `my secondary contribution is payable` MEANS
            `s 6 a secondary Class 1 contribution is payable, having regard to sections 1(6)(a) and 6(2)`
                `my earnings` `my limits` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`
                `I fulfil the prescribed conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` `a Class 1B contribution is payable on the earnings`
        `my relevant apprentice status` MEANS `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` (JUST `I am under 25`) `I am employed as an apprentice`
        `section 9B applies` MEANS `s 9B(1) section 9B applies to the earnings` `my secondary contribution is payable` `my relevant apprentice status`
        `section 9A applies` MEANS `s 9A(1) section 9A applies to the earnings` `my secondary contribution is payable` `I fall within an age group specified in column 1 of the table in section 9A(3)` `section 9B applies`
        `my upper threshold for my age group` MEANS
            IF `regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for my age group` THEN JUST `the upper secondary threshold for my age group` ELSE NOTHING    -- no value given: an input left out, not an answer of the text
        `my upper threshold as a relevant apprentice` MEANS
            IF `regulations provide an upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` THEN JUST `the upper secondary threshold for relevant apprentices` ELSE NOTHING    -- no value given: an input left out, not an answer of the text
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
            `the amount in pounds` IS `the amount I was paid in pounds`
            `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
                `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
                `number of the week in the year` IS `the number of the tax week`
        `my limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
            `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
            `lower earnings limit` IS `the lower earnings limit`
            `primary threshold` IS `the primary threshold`
            `upper earnings limit` IS `the upper earnings limit`
            `secondary threshold` IS `the secondary threshold`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a), called by s 6(1), reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

-- s 9B(2). A "relevant apprentice" is an earner under 25 who is employed, in the employment, as an apprentice (the employer then pays a
-- 0% secondary percentage below the upper secondary threshold). The section applies where a secondary contribution is payable.
@export Under section 9B(2), am I a relevant apprentice?
GIVEN `I am under 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under the age of 25?
      `I am employed as an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed, in this employment, as an apprentice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 9B(2), am I a relevant apprentice` IS
    `s 9B(2) the earner is a relevant apprentice` (JUST `I am under 25`) `I am employed as an apprentice`

-- s 6A(2) and (3). Where your earnings in a tax week are not less than the lower earnings limit but do not exceed the primary threshold,
-- you are treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for that week, for the purposes of the benefits the section lists.
@export Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week?
GIVEN `the amount I was paid in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you paid in the pay period, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were you paid? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the number of the tax week` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax week of that year were you paid? (1 to 53; tax week 1 begins on 6 April)
      `the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the primary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the primary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for your pay period, in pounds?
      `the secondary threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the secondary threshold for your pay period, in pounds?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed (do you work for gain)?
      `my job is carried on in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job carried on in Great Britain?
      `my job is under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service (a contract of employment)?
      `my job is an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my office carries earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you hold an office, does it carry earnings? (answer no if you hold no office)
      `the purpose` IS A `s 6A(3) Purpose` @desc For which purpose are you asking? (section 14(1)(a); the provisions in section 21(5A)(a) to (c); other contributory benefits; jobseeker's allowance; employment and support allowance; or any other purpose)
      `the provision is one mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the purpose is the provisions in section 21(5A)(a) to (c), is the provision you are asking about one of those listed there?
      `a prescribed exception or modification applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a prescribed exception or modification apply to your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 6A(2), am I treated as having paid a primary Class 1 contribution for this week` IS
    `s 6A(2) the earner is treated as having actually paid a primary Class 1 contribution for the week`
        (`s 6A(1) section 6A applies to the earnings` `my earnings` `my limits` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my employment` `I am gainfully employed` `my office carries earnings`)
        `the purpose` `the provision is one mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` `a prescribed exception or modification applies`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`
        `my earnings` MEANS `Earnings paid` WITH
            `the amount in pounds` IS `the amount I was paid in pounds`
            `the tax week they were paid in` IS `Tax week` WITH
                `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
                `number of the week in the year` IS `the number of the tax week`
        `my limits` MEANS `Earnings limits` WITH
            `the tax year` IS `my tax year`
            `lower earnings limit` IS `the lower earnings limit`
            `primary threshold` IS `the primary threshold`
            `upper earnings limit` IS `the upper earnings limit`
            `secondary threshold` IS `the secondary threshold`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `the employee` IS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2066
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2000
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            -- The fields s 2(1)(a), called by s 6(1), reads.
            `held under a contract of service` IS `my job is under a contract of service`
            `held in an office` IS `my job is an office`
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS `my job is carried on in Great Britain`

§§ `Class 1A contributions on benefits in kind (ss 10 to 10ZB)`

-- Only if the person receives benefits in kind from a job (a company car, say): the form can ask "Do you get benefits in kind from your job?" first.

-- s 10(1). A Class 1A contribution is payable for a tax year, by the employer, on benefits in kind (general earnings) that the earner is
-- chargeable to income tax on, where the employment is employed earner's employment (other than lower-paid employment as a minister of
-- religion) and the benefits fall to be left out of account in computing earnings for Class 1.
@export Under section 10(1), is a Class 1A contribution payable on the benefits I get from my job?
GIVEN `I am chargeable to income tax on general earnings (benefits) received from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you chargeable to income tax on the benefits in kind you receive from the employment?
      `the employment is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment employed earner's employment?
      `the employment is not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment other than lower-paid employment as a minister of religion?
      `the benefits fall to be left out of account for Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the benefits fall to be left out of account in working out your earnings for Class 1 contributions (they are not earnings paid to you)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10(1), is a Class 1A contribution payable on the benefits I get from my job` IS
    `s 10(1) a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year`
        `I am chargeable to income tax on general earnings (benefits) received from the employment`
        `the employment is employed earner's employment`
        `the employment is not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion`
        `the benefits fall to be left out of account for Class 1 contributions`

-- s 10(4) and (5). The Class 1A contribution is the Class 1A percentage (the secondary percentage, 15% as the Act states it) of the benefits
-- that fall to be left out of account.
@export Under section 10(4), how much Class 1A contribution is payable on these benefits, in pounds?
GIVEN `I am chargeable to income tax on general earnings (benefits) received from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you chargeable to income tax on the benefits in kind you receive from the employment?
      `the employment is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment employed earner's employment?
      `the employment is not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment other than lower-paid employment as a minister of religion?
      `the benefits fall to be left out of account for Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the benefits fall to be left out of account in working out your earnings for Class 1 contributions (they are not earnings paid to you)?
      `the value of the benefits that fall to be left out of account` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of those benefits, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 10(4), how much Class 1A contribution is payable on these benefits` IS
    `s 10(4) the amount of the Class 1A contribution payable under subsection (1)`
        (`s 10(1) a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year`
            `I am chargeable to income tax on general earnings (benefits) received from the employment`
            `the employment is employed earner's employment`
            `the employment is not lower-paid employment as a minister of religion`
            `the benefits fall to be left out of account for Class 1 contributions`)
        `the value of the benefits that fall to be left out of account`
        (`s 10(5) the Class 1A percentage` `s 9(2) the secondary percentage as the Act states it`)

-- s 10ZA(1) and (3). Where someone other than your employer provides the benefit, without your employer arranging or facilitating it, that
-- person (not your employer) pays the Class 1A contribution -- in the case of the tax year beginning 6 April 2000 only if they gave written notice.
@export Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit, rather than my employer, owe the Class 1A contribution?
GIVEN `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year on the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a Class 1A contribution payable for the tax year on the benefit you received?
      `the benefit is provided for me or a member of my family or household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit provided for you or a member of your family or household?
      `the person providing it is not my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person providing the benefit someone other than your employer?
      `my employer did not arrange or facilitate it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer not arrange or facilitate the provision of the benefit?
      `the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit a sporting testimonial payment?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year began` IS A NUMBER @desc For which tax year is the contribution? (the calendar year in which it began: 2025 for 2025-26)
      `the provider gave written notice to the Inland Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the provider give written notice to the Inland Revenue (this matters only for the tax year beginning 6 April 2000)?
      `the day the provider gave written notice` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the provider give that written notice? (any date if there was none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 10ZA(3), does the person who provides the benefit rather than my employer owe the Class 1A contribution` IS
    `s 10ZA(3) the liability falls on the person providing the benefit`
        (`s 10ZA(1) section 10ZA applies`
            `a Class 1A contribution is payable for the tax year on the benefit`
            `the benefit is provided for me or a member of my family or household`
            `the person providing it is not my employer`
            `my employer did not arrange or facilitate it`
            `the benefit is a sporting testimonial payment`)
        (`s 10ZA(4) subsection (3) applies in the case of a Class 1A contribution for the tax year`
            (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year began`)
            `the notice date`)
    WHERE
        `the notice date` MEANS
            IF `the provider gave written notice to the Inland Revenue` THEN JUST `the day the provider gave written notice` ELSE NOTHING    -- no value given: an input left out, not an answer of the text

§§ `Class 2 contributions of the self-employed (ss 11 to 12)`

-- Only if the person is self-employed: the form can ask "Are you self-employed?" first.

-- s 11(5A), (5B), (7). A self-employed earner with relevant profits of, or exceeding, the small profits threshold (GBP 7,105 as the Act states
-- it) is treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution for each week in the tax year that they are in the employment, but not for a
-- week before the one in which they attain 16 or after the one in which they attain pensionable age.
@export Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week?
GIVEN `I am in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year?
      `I am in the employment in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the employment in the week you are asking about?
      `my relevant profits for the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your relevant profits (profits from the employment on which Class 4 contributions are payable) for the tax year, in pounds?
      `the week is before the week in which I attained 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week before the week in which you attained the age of 16?
      `the week is after the week in which I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week after the week in which you attained pensionable age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 11(5B), am I treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution for this week` IS
    `s 11(5B) the earner is treated for relevant purposes as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution in respect of the week`
        (`s 11(1) section 11 applies` `I am in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year`)
        `I am in the employment in the week`
        `my relevant profits for the tax year`
        `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold as the Act states it`
        (`s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` `the week is before the week in which I attained 16` `the week is after the week in which I attained pensionable age`)

-- s 11(6) and (7). If your relevant profits are below the small profits threshold, you may pay a Class 2 contribution of GBP 3.65 (as the Act
-- states it) for any week in the tax year that you are in the employment, unless regulations under s 11(9)(b) bar it.
@export Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week?
GIVEN `I am in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year?
      `I am in the employment in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the employment in the week you are asking about?
      `my relevant profits for the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your relevant profits (profits from the employment on which Class 4 contributions are payable) for the tax year, in pounds?
      `the week is before the week in which I attained 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week before the week in which you attained the age of 16?
      `the week is after the week in which I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week after the week in which you attained pensionable age?
      `regulations bar payment in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 11(9)(b) provide that you may not pay (because of your employment, or a prescribed circumstance)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 11(6), may I pay a Class 2 contribution for this week` IS
    `s 11(6) the earner may pay a Class 2 contribution in respect of the week`
        (`s 11(1) section 11 applies` `I am in employment as a self-employed earner in the tax year`)
        `I am in the employment in the week`
        `my relevant profits for the tax year`
        `s 11(4)(b) the small profits threshold as the Act states it`
        (`s 11(7) a Class 2 contribution is to be paid or treated as paid in respect of the week` `the week is before the week in which I attained 16` `the week is after the week in which I attained pensionable age`)
        `regulations bar payment in my case`

-- s 12(1), (2), (3), (8). A Class 2 contribution under s 11(6) paid after the tax year of the week it is for costs what it would have cost in
-- that year, unless it is an ordinary contribution paid after the end of the following tax year while the weekly rate has changed, when it is
-- computed by the highest weekly rate in the period from the week to the day of payment. The person states that highest rate.
@export Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution, in pounds?
GIVEN `it is a Class 2 contribution under section 11(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Class 2 contribution of the kind you may pay under section 11(6)?
      `the calendar year in which the tax year of the week began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year is the week the contribution is for? (the calendar year in which it began: 2020 for 2020-21)
      `the calendar year in which the tax year of payment began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year do you pay it? (the calendar year in which it began)
      `it is of the amount specified in section 11(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a contribution of the amount specified in section 11(6) (rather than a higher-rate contribution)?
      `the weekly rate in the contribution year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly rate of the contribution for the week in the tax year of the week, in pounds?
      `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate applicable at the time you pay, in pounds?
      `the highest weekly rate in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the highest weekly rate of ordinary contributions in the period from the week you pay for to the day you pay, in pounds?
      `regulations under section 12(4) or (6) apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 12(4) or (6) apply to your contribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 12(2), how much must I pay for a late paid Class 2 contribution` IS
    `s 12(2) the amount of the late paid Class 2 contribution`
        (`s 12(1) section 12 applies to the contribution` `it is a Class 2 contribution under section 11(6)` `my contribution year` `my payment year`)
        (`s 12(8) the contribution is an ordinary contribution` `it is of the amount specified in section 11(6)`)
        `my contribution year` `my payment year`
        `the weekly rate in the contribution year`
        `the weekly rate applicable at the time of payment`
        (LIST `the highest weekly rate in the period`)    -- the module takes the list of rates in the period and answers its highest; the person states that highest rate
        `regulations under section 12(4) or (6) apply`
    WHERE
        `my contribution year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year of the week began`
        `my payment year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year of payment began`

§§ `Class 3 contributions that anyone may pay (ss 13 to 14)`

-- Only if the person pays, or is thinking of paying, voluntary Class 3 contributions (for example to fill a gap in their record): the form can ask "Do you want to pay voluntary contributions?" first.

-- s 13(1) and 1(6)(b). Earners and others over 16 are entitled, if they so wish and subject to prescribed conditions, to pay Class 3
-- contributions, which are GBP 18.40 a week as the Act states it. The regulations that grant the entitlement are outside this text.
@export Under section 13(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution?
GIVEN `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over the age of 16?
      `the regulations, subject to the prescribed conditions, entitle me to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations, with their prescribed conditions satisfied in your case, entitle you to pay a Class 3 contribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` IS
    `s 13(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution` (JUST `I am over 16`) `the regulations, subject to the prescribed conditions, entitle me to pay`

-- s 13(4), (5), (6). A Class 3 contribution paid for an earlier tax year costs what it would have cost in that year, unless it is paid after
-- the end of the next tax year but one following that year and the two amounts differ, when it is the highest of the amounts in the period.
@export Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year, in pounds?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the tax year it is for began` IS A NUMBER @desc For which tax year is the contribution? (the calendar year in which it began: 2020 for 2020-21)
      `the calendar year in which the tax year of payment began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year do you pay it? (the calendar year in which it began)
      `the amount applicable had it been paid in the earlier year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of Class 3 contribution would have applied had you paid it in the earlier year, in pounds?
      `the amount applicable at the time of payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of Class 3 contribution applies at the time you pay, in pounds?
      `the highest other amount in the period between` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the highest other amount of a Class 3 contribution in the period between the two years, in pounds? (the larger of the two amounts above if there was no other)
      `regulations under section 13(7) apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 13(7) apply to your contribution?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 13(4), how much must I pay for a Class 3 contribution for an earlier tax year` IS
    `s 13(4) the amount of the Class 3 contribution for the earlier tax year`
        `my contribution year` `my payment year`
        `the amount applicable had it been paid in the earlier year`
        `the amount applicable at the time of payment`
        (LIST `the highest other amount in the period between`)    -- the module takes the list of other amounts and answers the highest of all; the person states the highest other amount
        `regulations under section 13(7) apply`
    WHERE
        `my contribution year` MEANS `s 13(5) the contribution year` (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year it is for began`)
        `my payment year` MEANS `s 13(5) the payment year` (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year of payment began`)

-- s 13A(1) to (12). An eligible person (reached pensionable age from 6 April 2008 to 5 April 2015, with at least 20 qualifying years, and, if
-- they reached it before 6 April 2010, a year of paying contributions with an earnings factor at the qualifying level) may pay Class 3
-- contributions for a missing year, for not more than 6 tax years and not after 6 years from attaining pensionable age.
@export Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year?
GIVEN `the day I attained or will attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you attain, or will you attain, pensionable age?
      `the number of tax years that count towards my 20` IS A NUMBER @desc How many tax years are there each of which counts under section 13A(8) or (10) (contributions paid or credited with an earnings factor at the qualifying level, or years precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home)?
      `I paid contributions in one tax year before attaining pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you attained pensionable age before 6 April 2010: did you actually pay contributions of a relevant class for the purposes of paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 in respect of any one tax year before the year you attained it?
      `my earnings factor for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year (derived as section 13A(13) says), in pounds?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the qualifying earnings factor for that year, in pounds?
      `the calendar year in which the missing year began` IS A NUMBER @desc Which tax year do you want to pay for? (the calendar year in which it began: 1990 for 1990-91)
      `a limit on the time is the only reason I may not pay for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled under the regulations made under section 13 to pay Class 3 contributions for that year but for a limit on the time within which they may be paid?
      `the number of tax years I would pay for under this section` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting this one, for how many tax years would you pay contributions under this section?
      `the day I pay` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you pay?
      `the prescribed conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury satisfied in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 13A(1), may I pay a Class 3 contribution for a missing year` IS
    `s 13A(1) an eligible person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution in respect of the missing year, having regard to subsections (3) and (4)`
        `I am an eligible person`
        `the year is a missing year`
        (`s 13A(3) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A for the tax year` `the number of tax years I would pay for under this section`)
        (`s 13A(4) the person is entitled to pay a contribution under section 13A on the day` `the day I attained or will attain pensionable age` `the day I pay`)
        `the prescribed conditions are satisfied`
    WHERE
        `the first condition` MEANS `s 13A(6) the first condition is satisfied` `the day I attained or will attain pensionable age`
        `the second condition` MEANS `s 13A(7) the second condition is satisfied` `the number of tax years that count towards my 20`
        `the third condition applies` MEANS `s 13A(11) the third condition applies` `the day I attained or will attain pensionable age`
        `the third condition` MEANS `s 13A(12) the third condition is satisfied` `I paid contributions in one tax year before attaining pensionable age` `my earnings factor for that year` `the qualifying earnings factor for that year`
        `I am an eligible person` MEANS `s 13A(5) the person is an eligible person` `the first condition` `the second condition` `the third condition applies` `the third condition`
        `the year is a missing year` MEANS
            `s 13A(2) the tax year is a missing year`
                (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the missing year began`)
                `a limit on the time is the only reason I may not pay for that year`

-- s 14(1). No one is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for a tax year if their earnings factor for the year equals or exceeds the
-- qualifying earnings factor for it; the regulations may preclude payment in other cases. So JUST FALSE here means NOT entitled (barred), and
-- NOTHING means the subsection does not decide: the question is asked in the rule's own sense, and only s 14(1)'s no is an answer.
@export Under section 14(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year?
GIVEN `my earnings factor, or the aggregate of my earnings factors, for the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your earnings factor for the tax year (or the total of your earnings factors, derived from earnings on which Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid and from Class 2 contributions actually paid), in pounds?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14(1), am I entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year` IS
    `s 14(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3 contribution for the tax year`
        `my earnings factor, or the aggregate of my earnings factors, for the tax year` `the qualifying earnings factor for the tax year`

§§ `Class 3A contributions for units of additional pension (ss 14A to 14B)`

-- Only if the person draws, or has deferred, a state retirement pension and is thinking of buying units of additional pension: the form can ask "Do you draw or defer a state pension?" first.
-- The option to pay ends at the cut-off date of s 14A(1A) (5 April 2017 at the earliest).

-- s 14A(1), (1A), (2). A person who is entitled to a Category A, B or D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit, or has deferred
-- entitlement to a Category A or B pension or graduated retirement benefit, is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution before the cut-off date:
-- 5 April 2017, or, if later, the end of the 30-day period beginning with the day HMRC sent them information in response to a request made
-- before 6 April 2017.
@export Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or to graduated retirement benefit?
      `my retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred (section 55(3))?
      `my graduated retirement benefit is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your graduated retirement benefit deferred within the meaning of section 36(4A) of the National Insurance Act 1965?
      `the day I pay` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you pay?
      `HMRC sent me information in response to a request I made before 6 April 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs send you information about Class 3A contributions in response to a request you made before 6 April 2017?
      `the day HMRC sent me that information` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they send it? (any date if they did not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14A(1), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this day` IS
    `s 14A(1) the person is entitled to pay a Class 3A contribution on the day`
        (`s 14A(2) the person is eligible to pay a Class 3A contribution`
            `I am entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category D retirement pension or graduated retirement benefit`
            (JUST `my retirement pension is deferred`)
            `my graduated retirement benefit is deferred`)
        `the day I pay`
        (`s 14A(1A) the cut-off date` `the day HMRC sent me information`)
    WHERE
        `the day HMRC sent me information` MEANS
            IF `HMRC sent me information in response to a request I made before 6 April 2017` THEN JUST `the day HMRC sent me that information` ELSE NOTHING    -- no value given: an input left out, not an answer of the text

-- s 14A(5). A person may pay Class 3A contributions on more than one occasion but may not obtain more than the maximum number of units of
-- additional pension, which the Treasury specifies in regulations.
@export Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion?
GIVEN `I have already paid a Class 3A contribution on an earlier occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already paid a Class 3A contribution on an earlier occasion?
      `the units of additional pension I have already obtained` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension have you already obtained?
      `the units of additional pension I would obtain by this payment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension would you obtain by this payment?
      `the maximum number of units specified in regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of units of additional pension that the Treasury has specified in regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14A(5), may I pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion` IS
    `s 14A(5) the person may pay a Class 3A contribution on this occasion`
        `I have already paid a Class 3A contribution on an earlier occasion`
        `the units of additional pension I have already obtained`
        `the units of additional pension I would obtain by this payment`
        `the maximum number of units specified in regulations`

-- s 14B(3). A person is treated as never having had a unit of additional pension if the Class 3A contribution paid for it is repaid.
@export Under section 14B(3), am I treated as never having had the unit of additional pension?
GIVEN `the Class 3A contribution I paid for the unit was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Class 3A contribution you paid in respect of the unit repaid to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 14B(3), am I treated as never having had the unit of additional pension` IS
    `s 14B(3) the person is treated as never having had the unit of additional pension` `the Class 3A contribution I paid for the unit was repaid`

§§ `Class 4 contributions on profits (ss 15 to 18A)`

-- Only if the person has profits from a trade, profession or vocation, or is a member of a limited liability partnership: the form can ask "Do you have trading profits?" first.

-- s 15(1). Class 4 contributions are payable for a tax year on all profits that (a) are immediately derived from a trade, profession or
-- vocation, (b) are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005 for the corresponding year of assessment, and (c) are not
-- profits of a trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom.
@export Under section 15(1), are Class 4 contributions payable on my profits for the tax year?
GIVEN `my profits are immediately derived from a trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your profits immediately derived from the carrying on or exercise of a trade, profession or vocation?
      `my profits are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 for the year of assessment corresponding to the tax year?
      `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(1), are Class 4 contributions payable on my profits for the tax year` IS
    `s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable for the tax year in respect of the profits`
        `my profits are immediately derived from a trade, profession or vocation`
        `my profits are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`
        `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`

-- s 15(2) and (3). Class 4 contributions are payable by the person on whom the income tax is (or would be) charged: 6% of the profits above
-- GBP 12,570 up to GBP 50,270 and 2% of those above GBP 50,270 (the Act's own figures; they can be altered under s 141 of the Administration
-- Act, and the main percentage under s 143, and a later alteration would change this answer).
@export Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year, in pounds?
GIVEN `my profits are immediately derived from a trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your profits immediately derived from the carrying on or exercise of a trade, profession or vocation?
      `my profits are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they profits chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 for the year of assessment corresponding to the tax year?
      `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `my profits for the tax year, computed in accordance with Schedule 2` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your profits for the tax year, computed in accordance with Schedule 2 to the Act, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 15(3), how much Class 4 contribution must I pay on my profits for the tax year` IS
    `s 15(3) the amount of the Class 4 contribution for the tax year`
        (`s 15(1) Class 4 contributions are payable for the tax year in respect of the profits`
            `my profits are immediately derived from a trade, profession or vocation`
            `my profits are chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`
            `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`)
        `my profits for the tax year, computed in accordance with Schedule 2`
        `s 15(3)(a) the lower profits limit as the Act states it`
        `s 15(3)(b) the upper profits limit as the Act states it`
        `s 15(3ZA)(a) the main Class 4 percentage as the Act states it`
        `s 15(3ZA)(b) the additional Class 4 percentage as the Act states it`

-- s 15(3A). A member of a limited liability partnership on whom income tax is (or would be) charged in respect of the partnership's trading
-- profits pays Class 4 contributions if they would be payable were the trade carried on in partnership by the members.
@export Under section 15(3A), am I, as a member of a limited liability partnership, liable to Class 4 contributions?
GIVEN `income tax is or would be charged on me in respect of the partnership's profits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is income tax (or would it be) charged on you in respect of profits arising from the trade or profession carried on by the limited liability partnership?
      `Class 4 contributions would be payable were it carried on in partnership by the members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Class 4 contributions be payable if the trade or profession were carried on in partnership by the members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 15(3A), am I as a member of a limited liability partnership liable to Class 4 contributions` IS
    `s 15(3A) Class 4 contributions are payable by the member of the limited liability partnership`
        `income tax is or would be charged on me in respect of the partnership's profits`
        `Class 4 contributions would be payable were it carried on in partnership by the members`

§§ `Contributions paid in error (s 19A)`

-- Only if Class 1, 1A or 1B contributions were paid for the person in error, because the work was not employed earner's employment: the form can ask "Were contributions paid for you in error?" first.

-- s 19A(1) and (2). Where Class 1, 1A or 1B contributions were paid in error for 1998-99 or a later tax year ("year 1") because the work was
-- not employed earner's employment, and the payer was not told of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year after year 1,
-- then after the end of that following year ("year 2") you are treated, except as prescribed, as if the earnings came from employed earner's
-- employment for contributions and contributory benefits, and for statutory sick pay and maternity pay.
@export Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which year 1 began` IS A NUMBER @desc In which tax year were the contributions paid in error? (the calendar year in which year 1 began: 2010 for 2010-11)
      `contributions were paid in respect of earnings or a benefit in year 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were Class 1, Class 1A or Class 1B contributions paid in respect of earnings paid to you (or a benefit made available to you) in year 1?
      `they were paid in error because the work was not employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they paid in error, in that the work was not employed earner's employment?
      `the payer was notified of the error before the end of the next tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who made the payments notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking? (the section works after the end of year 2)
      `the circumstances are those prescribed as excepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those that regulations prescribe as excepted from the section?
      `the purpose` IS A `s 19A(2) Purpose` @desc For which purpose are you asking? (contributions and contributory benefits; statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay; or another purpose)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 19A(2), am I treated as having been in employed earner's employment despite the error` IS
    `s 19A(2) the earner is treated as if the earnings were derived from employed earner's employment`
        (`s 19A(1) section 19A applies`
            `year 1`
            `contributions were paid in respect of earnings or a benefit in year 1`
            `they were paid in error because the work was not employed earner's employment`
            `the payer was notified of the error before the end of the next tax year`)
        (`s 19A(1)(c) the last day of year 2` `year 1`)
        `the day`
        `the circumstances are those prescribed as excepted`
        `the purpose`
    WHERE
        `year 1` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which year 1 began`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc2 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (UK), 1992 c. 4, Part II, ss 20 to 42 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- The text is a converter rendering, not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit,
-- statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great Britain, asking on facts they can state whether and how much
-- they must pay in contributions, whether they are entitled to a benefit or to statutory pay, how much,
-- for how long, and what ends or reduces it.
--
-- This layer asks the questions that person would ask about the contributory benefits of Part II, ss 20 to
-- 42: how the Act counts their contributions, whether they are entitled to incapacity benefit, maternity
-- allowance or the benefits for a widow, widower or surviving partner, and how much. Nothing here is new
-- law: every question calls a rule from the layer-1 modules imported above, never restating one.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, numbers, dates, or the Act's own list of
-- benefits), one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- The records and the "maybe" values the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE,
-- from those answers. A fact the person cannot state, because the Act sends it to a regulation, an order or
-- another Part, is either asked as a plain figure the person looks up (a rate, a limit) or left unanswered
-- (NOTHING) with a comment.
--
-- READING A RESULT. A "false" answer means the text itself says no. A NOTHING answer means "not covered":
-- the text is silent, or limits itself in its own words, or sends the answer to something outside Part II.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into false (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ssc2)").
--
-- The questions are named "Under section N, ..." with the Act's own numbering, so that no two parts of the
-- Act can ever share a name. There is never a seat for an official: s 24(2), s 35(6B) to (6D) and s 39A(3D)(d)
-- speak to the Secretary of State, and appear here only for what they mean to the person.

§ `Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, Part II -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `Which benefits count, and how the benefit year runs (ss 20 and 21)`

-- s 20(1). The Act lists the contributory benefits under Part II; the list is open (fork F1 in NOTES.md),
-- so a benefit that is not on it is not answered.
@export Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part?
GIVEN `the benefit I claim` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit do you claim?
      `I am an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance (someone who was already receiving it when the Act took effect)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(1), is the benefit I claim a contributory benefit under this Part` IS
    `s 20(1) the benefit is a contributory benefit under this Part` `the benefit I claim` `I am an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance`

-- s 20(2). A long-term benefit is one of the Act's named list (it includes the Category A and B retirement
-- pensions, the widow's benefits and long-term incapacity benefit).
@export Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit?
GIVEN `the benefit I claim` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit do you claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a long-term benefit` IS
    `s 20(2) the benefit is a long-term benefit` `the benefit I claim`

-- s 20(2). A short-term benefit is one of the Act's named list (it includes short-term incapacity benefit
-- and maternity allowance).
@export Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a short-term benefit?
GIVEN `the benefit I claim` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit do you claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 20(2), is the benefit I claim a short-term benefit` IS
    `s 20(2) the benefit is a short-term benefit` `the benefit I claim`

-- s 21(1). Entitlement to the benefits of s 20(1) depends on contribution conditions being satisfied, except
-- for the routes the section carves out: short-term incapacity benefit under s 30A(1)(b), long-term
-- incapacity benefit under s 30A(5), maternity allowance under s 35 or 35B, incapacity benefit under s 40 or
-- 41, and a shared additional pension under s 55A or 55AA.
@export Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim?
GIVEN `the benefit I claim` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit do you claim?
      `I am an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance (someone who was already receiving it when the Act took effect)?
      `the route by which I claim` IS A `s 21(1) Route of entitlement` @desc By which route do you claim it: one of the routes section 21(1) names, or any other route?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 21(1), does the requirement of contribution conditions apply to the benefit I claim` IS
    `s 21(1) the requirement of contribution conditions applies to the entitlement` `the benefit I claim` `I am an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance` `the route by which I claim`

-- s 21(6). The benefit year that begins in a calendar year starts on the first Sunday in January and ends on
-- the Saturday before the first Sunday of the next January (the text's own definition).
@export Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end?
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the benefit year begin (for example 2025)?
GIVETH A Period
DECIDE `Under section 21(6), when does the benefit year that begins in this calendar year start and end` IS
    `s 21(6) the benefit year that begins in the calendar year` `the calendar year`
        NOTHING   -- no other period is asked about: the regulations' "other period for the prescribed purpose" is not stated by the person

§§ `Earnings factors and credits (ss 22 to 24)`

-- s 22(1)(b). For a tax year before 1987-88 the earnings factor is derived from the person's contributions of
-- Classes 1, 2 and 3.
@export Under section 22(1)(b), what is my earnings factor for a tax year before 1987-88?
GIVEN `my earnings factor from Class 1 contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings factor do your Class 1 contributions for the year give (0 if you paid none)?
      `my earnings factor from Class 2 contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings factor do your Class 2 contributions for the year give (0 if you paid none)?
      `my earnings factor from Class 3 contributions` IS A NUMBER @desc What earnings factor do your Class 3 contributions for the year give (0 if you paid none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 22(1)(b), what is my earnings factor for a tax year before 1987-88` IS
    `s 22(1)(b) the annual earnings factor for an earlier tax year` `my earnings factor from Class 1 contributions` `my earnings factor from Class 2 contributions` `my earnings factor from Class 3 contributions`

-- s 22(4). Subject to regulations under s 19(4) to (6), no earnings factor is derived (a) for 1987-88 or any
-- later tax year, from earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions are paid at the reduced rate, or (b) for
-- any earlier tax year, from primary Class 1 contributions paid at the reduced rate or from secondary Class 1
-- contributions.
@export Under section 22(4), is an earnings factor derived from my contributions for this tax year?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the tax year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the tax year begin (the year 2024-25 begins in 2024)?
      `I paid primary Class 1 contributions at the reduced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the contributions you paid primary Class 1 contributions at the reduced rate (for example the married woman's rate)?
      `the contributions are secondary Class 1 contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the contributions secondary Class 1 contributions (paid by an employer for you)?
      `regulations provide otherwise for my contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 19(4) to (6) provide that an earnings factor is derived from your contributions anyway?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 22(4), is an earnings factor derived from my contributions for this tax year` IS
    `s 22(4) an earnings factor is derived from the earnings or contributions` `my tax year` `I paid primary Class 1 contributions at the reduced rate` `the contributions are secondary Class 1 contributions` `regulations provide otherwise for my contributions`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year begins`

-- s 23(3)(b). Class 2 and Class 3 contributions give, for each contribution paid, an earnings factor equal or
-- approximating to the lower earnings limit for the year.
@export Under section 23(3)(b), what earnings factor do my Class 2 or Class 3 contributions give for the tax year?
GIVEN `the lower earnings limit for the tax year, in pounds a week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit for the tax year, in pounds a week (it is set each year by regulations: look it up)?
      `the number of my Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Class 2 or Class 3 contributions did you pay for the tax year?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 23(3)(b), what earnings factor do my Class 2 or Class 3 contributions give for the tax year` IS
    `s 23(3)(b) the amount to which the earnings factor from Class 2 or Class 3 contributions equals or approximates` `the lower earnings limit for the tax year, in pounds a week` `the number of my Class 2 or Class 3 contributions for the tax year`

-- s 23A(3). A person is a "relevant carer" for a week if Child Benefit is awarded to them for any part of the
-- week for a child under 12, or they are a foster parent, or are engaged in caring as the regulations define.
@export Under section 23A(3), was I a relevant carer in respect of this week?
GIVEN `child benefit was awarded to me for any part of the week for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was Child Benefit awarded to you for any part of the week for a child?
      `that child is under 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that child under 12 (if you were awarded Child Benefit for no child, answer no)?
      `I was a foster parent for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a foster parent for any part of the week, as the regulations define a foster parent?
      `I was engaged in caring in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged in caring in the week, as the regulations define caring?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 23A(3), was I a relevant carer in respect of this week` IS
    `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` `child benefit was awarded to me for any part of the week for a child` (JUST `that child is under 12`) `I was a foster parent for any part of the week` `I was engaged in caring in the week`

-- s 23A(2). For each week after 6 April 2010 in which the person was a relevant carer, one Class 3
-- contribution is treated as paid.
@export Under section 23A(2), how many Class 3 contributions am I credited with for this week?
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the week (a week of Part II begins on a Sunday)?
      `child benefit was awarded to me for any part of the week for a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was Child Benefit awarded to you for any part of the week for a child?
      `that child is under 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that child under 12 (if you were awarded Child Benefit for no child, answer no)?
      `I was a foster parent for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a foster parent for any part of the week, as the regulations define a foster parent?
      `I was engaged in caring in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged in caring in the week, as the regulations define caring?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 23A(2), how many Class 3 contributions am I credited with for this week` IS
    `s 23A(2) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the week` `the first day of the week` `the relevant carer answer`
    WHERE
        `the relevant carer answer` MEANS `s 23A(3) the person was a relevant carer in respect of the week` `child benefit was awarded to me for any part of the week for a child` (JUST `that child is under 12`) `I was a foster parent for any part of the week` `I was engaged in caring in the week`

-- s 23A(5). The contributor is credited with 52 Class 3 contributions for each tax year ending before 6 April
-- 2010 in which they were precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home (subsection (6) limits
-- the number of tax years).
@export Under section 23A(5), how many Class 3 contributions am I credited with for this tax year?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the tax year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the tax year begin (the year 2024-25 begins in 2024)?
      `I was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you precluded from regular employment in that tax year by responsibilities at home?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 23A(5), how many Class 3 contributions am I credited with for this tax year` IS
    `s 23A(5) the number of Class 3 contributions credited for the tax year` `my tax year` `I was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year begins`

-- s 24(2). Where records of earnings are unobtainable, the Secretary of State may compute them or take a
-- specified sum. To the person this is a liberty of the Secretary of State and a liability of the person.
@export Under section 24(2), may the Secretary of State work out my earnings for this tax year by computation or by taking a specified sum?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the tax year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the tax year begin (the year 2024-25 begins in 2024)?
      `the records of my earnings have not been kept or kept long enough or are otherwise unobtainable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State been satisfied that records of your earnings have not been maintained or retained, or are otherwise unobtainable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 24(2), may the Secretary of State work out my earnings for this tax year by computation or by taking a specified sum` IS
    `s 24(2) the Secretary of State may determine the earnings by computation or by specifying a sum` `my tax year` `the records of my earnings have not been kept or kept long enough or are otherwise unobtainable`
    WHERE
        `my tax year` MEANS `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the calendar year in which the tax year begins`

§§ `Incapacity benefit: whether, how much, and what reduces it (ss 30A to 30E)`

-- s 30A(1). Short-term incapacity benefit is paid for a day of incapacity for work that forms part of a
-- period of incapacity for work, to a person who satisfies either of the conditions in subsection (2) (age
-- and contributions) or, if neither, each of the conditions in subsection (2A) (age, incapacity, residence
-- and education). Subsections (3) and (4) take away the first 3 days and any day after 364 days of
-- entitlement; the number of days already counted is the answer to the section 30D question below.
@export Under section 30A(1), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `I satisfy the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the contribution conditions in Schedule 3 for short-term incapacity benefit?
      `the first day of my period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your period of incapacity for work?
      `I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension but for deferment or an election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if your entitlement had not been deferred or you had not made an election under section 54(1)?
      `I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension but for deferment or an election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category B retirement pension, on the contributions of a deceased spouse or civil partner, if your entitlement had not been deferred or you had not made an election under section 54(1)?
      `I am over 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 16 (that is, have you reached 16)?
      `my case is a prescribed case with an age limit of 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is yours a prescribed case in which the age limit is 25 rather than 20?
      `I am under 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 20?
      `I am under 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 25?
      `I am incapable of work on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of work on this day, under the test in section 171A?
      `the number of consecutive days I was incapable of work` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive days immediately before this day (or before the earlier day you were 16 or over) were you incapable of work?
      `I satisfy the conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the prescribed conditions as to residence in Great Britain, or presence there, on this day?
      `I am receiving full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving full-time education on this day?
      `this day forms part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this day form part of a period of incapacity for work (a run of days of incapacity, with gaps of no more than 8 weeks joined)?
      `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first day of the period as 1, what number is this day in the period?
      `the number of days of entitlement before this day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of entitlement are counted before this day (the answer to the question on section 30D)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30A(1), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for this day` IS
    `s 30A(1) the person is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for the relevant day`
        `condition (1)(a)` `condition (1)(b)` `day of incapacity in a period` `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` `the number of days of entitlement before this day`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called here read only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`
        `condition (2)(a)` MEANS `s 30A(2)(a) the person is under pensionable age on the relevant day and satisfies the contribution conditions` `the day` `me` (JUST `I satisfy the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit`)
        `condition (2)(b)` MEANS `s 30A(2)(b) the person is not more than 5 years over pensionable age on the relevant day, the period began before that age, and a retirement pension would be payable but for deferment or election` `the day` `me` `the first day of my period of incapacity for work` (JUST `I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension but for deferment or an election`) (JUST `I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension but for deferment or an election`)
        `condition (1)(a)` MEANS `s 30A(2) the person satisfies either of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(a)` `condition (2)(a)` `condition (2)(b)`
        `condition (1)(b)` MEANS `s 30A(2A) the person satisfies each of the conditions mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` (JUST `I am over 16`) `my case is a prescribed case with an age limit of 25` (JUST `I am under 20`) (JUST `I am under 25`) (JUST `I am incapable of work on this day`) `the number of consecutive days I was incapable of work` `I satisfy the conditions as to residence or presence in Great Britain` `I am receiving full-time education`
        `the maternity allowance route` MEANS NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 30C(2) route (a day in the maternity allowance period) is not asked here; a woman in that period who is not incapable of work gets NOTHING from this question
        `day of incapacity in a period` MEANS `s 30C(1) the relevant day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` (`s 30C(1)(a) the day is a day of incapacity for work` (JUST `I am incapable of work on this day`)) `the maternity allowance route` (JUST `this day forms part of a period of incapacity for work`)

-- s 30A(5). A person who ceases, by virtue of subsection (4), to be entitled to short-term incapacity benefit
-- is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for each later day of incapacity for work in the same period of
-- incapacity for work, subject to the condition the subsection adds about pensionable age.
@export Under section 30A(5), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for this day?
GIVEN `I ceased to be entitled to short-term incapacity benefit by virtue of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be entitled to short-term incapacity benefit because you had had 196 days of entitlement (section 30A(4))?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `this day is a later day of incapacity in the same period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a later day of incapacity for work in the same period of incapacity for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30A(5), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for this day` IS
    `s 30A(5) the person is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for the relevant day` `I ceased to be entitled to short-term incapacity benefit by virtue of subsection (4)` `the day` `me` `this day is a later day of incapacity in the same period`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`

-- s 30B(1). The amount payable for any day is 1/7th of the appropriate weekly rate.
@export Under section 30B(1), how much am I paid for one day of incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly rate, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your appropriate weekly rate of incapacity benefit, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30B(1), how much am I paid for one day of incapacity benefit` IS
    `s 30B(1) the amount payable by way of incapacity benefit for a day` `the appropriate weekly rate, in pounds`

-- s 30B(2). The weekly rate of short-term incapacity benefit is the lower rate for the first 196 days of
-- entitlement and the higher rate after that. The two rates are in Schedule 4, which this text omits: the
-- person looks them up.
@export Under section 30B(2), what is the weekly rate of my short-term incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `the lower weekly rate in Schedule 4, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower weekly rate of short-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds (look it up)?
      `the higher weekly rate in Schedule 4, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the higher weekly rate of short-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds (look it up)?
      `the number of days of entitlement before this day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of entitlement are counted before this day (the answer to the question on section 30D)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30B(2), what is the weekly rate of my short-term incapacity benefit` IS
    `s 30B(2) the weekly rate of short-term incapacity benefit` (JUST `the lower weekly rate in Schedule 4, in pounds`) (JUST `the higher weekly rate in Schedule 4, in pounds`) `the number of days of entitlement before this day`

-- s 30B(4). A person who has been entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for 196 days or more and is
-- terminally ill, or is entitled to the highest rate of the care component of disability living allowance, is
-- paid the long-term rate if that is greater than the rate otherwise payable.
@export Under section 30B(4), what is the weekly rate of my short-term incapacity benefit if I am terminally ill?
GIVEN `the number of days of entitlement before this day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of entitlement are counted before this day (the answer to the question on section 30D)?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected within 6 months?
      `I am entitled to the highest rate of the care component of disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the highest rate of the care component of disability living allowance?
      `the rate otherwise payable under subsection (2) or (3), in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate would otherwise be payable to you under subsection (2) or (3), in pounds?
      `the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds (look it up)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30B(4), what is the weekly rate of my short-term incapacity benefit if I am terminally ill` IS
    `s 30B(4) the weekly rate of short-term incapacity benefit for a terminally ill person` `the number of days of entitlement before this day`
        (`s 30B(4) the person is terminally ill` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months`)
        `I am entitled to the highest rate of the care component of disability living allowance`
        (JUST `the rate otherwise payable under subsection (2) or (3), in pounds`)
        (JUST `the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds`)

-- s 30B(8). The weekly amount payable is the weekly rate less the reduction for pension payments (s 30DD) and
-- the deduction for a councillor's allowance (s 30E).
@export Under section 30B(8), what weekly amount of incapacity benefit am I paid after the reductions?
GIVEN `my weekly rate before reduction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of incapacity benefit before any reduction, in pounds?
      `the reduction for a pension payment, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the reduction under section 30DD, in pounds (0 if none)?
      `the deduction for a councillor's allowance, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the deduction under section 30E, in pounds (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30B(8), what weekly amount of incapacity benefit am I paid after the reductions` IS
    `s 30B(8) the weekly amount payable after the reductions in sections 30DD and 30E` `my weekly rate before reduction, in pounds` `the reduction for a pension payment, in pounds` `the deduction for a councillor's allowance, in pounds`

-- s 30C(1)(c). Two periods of incapacity for work not separated by a period of more than 8 weeks are treated
-- as one period (fork F9: the days strictly between them; a gap of 56 days is not more than 8 weeks).
@export Under section 30C(1)(c), are my two periods of incapacity for work treated as one period?
GIVEN `the first day of my first period of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your first period of incapacity for work?
      `the last day of my first period of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your first period of incapacity for work?
      `the first day of my second period of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your second period of incapacity for work?
      `the last day of my second period of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your second period of incapacity for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30C(1)(c), are my two periods of incapacity for work treated as one period` IS
    `s 30C(1)(c) the two periods are treated as one period of incapacity for work` `my first period` `my second period`
    WHERE
        `my first period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my first period of incapacity`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of my first period of incapacity`
        `my second period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my second period of incapacity`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of my second period of incapacity`

-- s 30C(5). A person who returns to claim after leaving qualifying remunerative work may have the days of the
-- claim treated as days of incapacity for work, if (a) the day after they left was a day of incapacity, (b)
-- they were entitled to the higher rate or long-term benefit within the two years ending with that day, and
-- (c) they met the tax credit conditions on the day before they left.
@export Under section 30C(5), is this day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim after I stopped qualifying remunerative work?
GIVEN `my claim is for the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit or for long-term incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit, or for long-term incapacity benefit?
      `the first day of the period for which I claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you claim?
      `the last day of the period for which I claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for which you claim?
      `the day I stopped qualifying remunerative work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to be in qualifying remunerative work?
      `the day after I stopped was a day of incapacity for work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the day after you ceased work a day of incapacity for work for you?
      `I was entitled to the higher rate or long-term benefit within the two years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit or to long-term incapacity benefit within the two years ending with that day of incapacity?
      `the latest day I was so entitled` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you last so entitled (any date if you answered no)?
      `I met the tax credit conditions on the day before I stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions (section 30C(5A)) on the day before you ceased work?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day of your claim do you ask?
      `I meet the tax credit conditions on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions (section 30C(5A)) on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30C(5), is this day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim after I stopped qualifying remunerative work` IS
    `s 30C(5) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the claim`
        `my claim is for the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit or for long-term incapacity benefit`
        `my claim period`
        `the day I stopped qualifying remunerative work`
        (JUST `the day after I stopped was a day of incapacity for work for me`)
        `the latest day of entitlement`
        (JUST `I met the tax credit conditions on the day before I stopped`)
        `the day`
        (JUST `I meet the tax credit conditions on this day`)
    WHERE
        `my claim period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of the period for which I claim`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of the period for which I claim`
        `the latest day of entitlement` MEANS IF `I was entitled to the higher rate or long-term benefit within the two years` THEN JUST `the latest day I was so entitled` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 30C(5A). The relevant tax credit conditions on a day: (a) entitled to the disability element of working
-- tax credit (or would be but for the relevant income), and (b) either working tax credit or a child tax credit
-- element other than the family element is paid for the day.
@export Under section 30C(5A), do I satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions on this day?
GIVEN `I am entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit (on your own claim or a joint claim)?
      `I would be so entitled but for the relevant income in my or our case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be so entitled but for the relevant income in your or your joint case?
      `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit, or any element of child tax credit other than the family element, paid for the day on such a claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30C(5A), do I satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions on this day` IS
    `s 30C(5A) the person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on the day` `I am entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` `I would be so entitled but for the relevant income in my or our case` `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid for the day`

-- s 30C(6). A person on a training-for-work course who was on the higher rate or long-term benefit within the
-- 56 days before it, and who is incapable on the first day after it ends within two years, has the training
-- days treated as days of incapacity for work.
@export Under section 30C(6), is this training day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim?
GIVEN `the first day I was engaged in training for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day you were engaged in training for work?
      `I was entitled to the higher rate or long-term benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to the higher rate of short-term incapacity benefit or to long-term incapacity benefit for one or more of the 56 days before you began training?
      `the last day I was so entitled` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you last so entitled (any date if you answered no)?
      `the first day after my training ended` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day after you ceased to be engaged in training for work?
      `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that first day a day of incapacity for work for you?
      `the training day` IS A DATE @desc For which training day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 30C(6), is this training day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim` IS
    `s 30C(6) the training day is treated as a day of incapacity for work` `the first day I was engaged in training for work` `the last day of entitlement` `the first day after my training ended` `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for me` `the training day`
    WHERE
        `the last day of entitlement` MEANS IF `I was entitled to the higher rate or long-term benefit` THEN JUST `the last day I was so entitled` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 30D. In counting the days of entitlement to short-term incapacity benefit (for ss 30A(4), 30B(2), 30B(4)
-- and 30B(5)), the first three days of the period of incapacity are included, so are a woman's days of
-- maternity allowance, so are prescribed days of statutory sick pay if the contribution conditions were met on
-- the first of them, and days of disqualification are excluded.
@export Under section 30D, how many days of entitlement count before this day?
GIVEN `the number of days I was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in the period of incapacity were you entitled to short-term incapacity benefit, not counting the first three days of the period (section 30D(2)(a) adds those three days itself, even if you were entitled for them)?
      `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `the number of days I was entitled to maternity allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days were you entitled to maternity allowance (0 if you are not a woman or had none)?
      `the number of prescribed days of statutory sick pay` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many of the days prescribed by regulations were you entitled to statutory sick pay?
      `I satisfied the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit on the first of those days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you satisfy the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit on the first of those days?
      `the number of days I was disqualified for receiving incapacity benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days were you disqualified for receiving incapacity benefit?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30D, how many days of entitlement count before this day` IS
    `s 30D the number of days of entitlement before the relevant day` `the number of days I was entitled to short-term incapacity benefit in the period` `I am a woman` `the number of days I was entitled to maternity allowance` `the number of prescribed days of statutory sick pay` `I satisfied the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit on the first of those days` `the number of days I was disqualified for receiving incapacity benefit`

-- s 30DD(1). Where a pension payment, or a Pension Protection Fund periodic payment, is payable for the same
-- period and the payments together exceed the threshold, the incapacity benefit is reduced by 50 per cent of the
-- excess.
@export Under section 30DD(1), by how much is my incapacity benefit reduced because of a pension payment?
GIVEN `I am entitled to incapacity benefit for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to incapacity benefit for the period?
      `a pension payment or a PPF periodic payment is payable to me for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a pension payment, or a Pension Protection Fund periodic payment, or both, payable to you for the period?
      `the amount of the payments taken together, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of those payments taken together, in pounds (or the amount the regulations treat as payable)?
      `the threshold, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the threshold for the period, in pounds (the greater amount the regulations prescribe, or its proportion for a part-week)?
      `regulations secure that a person of my description suffers no reduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 30DD(3) secure that a person of your description does not suffer any reduction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30DD(1), by how much is my incapacity benefit reduced because of a pension payment` IS
    `s 30DD(1) the reduction in the amount of incapacity benefit` `I am entitled to incapacity benefit for the period` `a pension payment or a PPF periodic payment is payable to me for the period` `the amount of the payments taken together, in pounds` `the threshold, in pounds` `regulations secure that a person of my description suffers no reduction`

-- s 30E(1). Where the net amount of councillor's allowance for the week (the allowances less the expenses
-- incurred) exceeds the amount the regulations prescribe, the excess is deducted from the incapacity benefit
-- for that week.
@export Under section 30E(1), by how much is my incapacity benefit for this week reduced because of a councillor's allowance?
GIVEN `the councillor's allowances I am entitled to for the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the councillor's allowances to which you are entitled for the week, in pounds?
      `the expenses I incurred in the week as a councillor, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What expenses did you incur in the week in connection with your membership of the council or councils, in pounds?
      `the amount the regulations prescribe, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do the regulations prescribe for the purposes of section 30E(1), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 30E(1), by how much is my incapacity benefit for this week reduced because of a councillor's allowance` IS
    `s 30E(1) the deduction from the incapacity benefit for the week` (`s 30E(3) the net amount of councillor's allowance` `the councillor's allowances I am entitled to for the week, in pounds` `the expenses I incurred in the week as a councillor, in pounds`) `the amount the regulations prescribe, in pounds`

§§ `Maternity allowance (ss 35 to 35B)`

-- s 35(1). A woman is entitled to a maternity allowance if (a) she is pregnant and has reached (or been
-- confined before reaching) the 11th week before the expected week of confinement, (b) she has been engaged
-- in employment for part of at least 26 of the 66 weeks before that week, (c) her average weekly earnings are
-- not less than the threshold, and (d) she is not entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week.
-- The expected week of confinement is a week of Part II, so it begins on a Sunday.
@export Under section 35(1), am I entitled to a maternity allowance?
GIVEN `I have become pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become pregnant?
      `the first day of my expected week of confinement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day (a Sunday) of the week in which your baby is expected?
      `the day for which I ask` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `I have been confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been confined (given birth)?
      `the day I was confined` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you confined (any date if you answered no)?
      `the number of those 66 weeks in which I was employed` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 66 weeks immediately before the expected week of confinement were you employed, as an employee or self-employed, for any part of the week?
      `my average weekly earnings, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your average weekly earnings, in pounds (worked out as section 35A(4) says)?
      `the maternity allowance threshold, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maternity allowance threshold for the tax year in which the 66 weeks began, in pounds (set by order: look it up)?
      `I am entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 35(1), am I entitled to a maternity allowance` IS
    `s 35(1) the woman is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section`
        (`s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` `I have become pregnant` `my expected week of confinement` `the day for which I ask` `the day of my confinement`)
        (`s 35(1)(b) the woman has been engaged in employment for any part of the week in the case of at least 26 of the 66 weeks` `the number of those 66 weeks in which I was employed`)
        (`s 35(1)(c) her average weekly earnings are not less than the maternity allowance threshold` (JUST `my average weekly earnings, in pounds`) `the maternity allowance threshold, in pounds`)
        (`s 35(1)(d) she is not entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy` (JUST `I am entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week`))
    WHERE
        `my expected week of confinement` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement`
            `the last day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement` PLUS 6
        `the day of my confinement` MEANS IF `I have been confined` THEN JUST `the day I was confined` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 35(2). The maternity allowance period is the period that would be the maternity pay period if she were
-- entitled to statutory maternity pay (s 165(1), in another Part).
@export Under section 35(2), when is my maternity allowance period?
GIVEN `the first day of the maternity pay period I would have` IS A DATE @desc What would be the first day of your maternity pay period, if you were entitled to statutory maternity pay (section 165(1))?
      `the last day of the maternity pay period I would have` IS A DATE @desc What would be the last day of that maternity pay period?
GIVETH A Period
DECIDE `Under section 35(2), when is my maternity allowance period` IS
    `s 35(2) the maternity allowance period` `that maternity pay period`
    WHERE
        `that maternity pay period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of the maternity pay period I would have`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of the maternity pay period I would have`

-- s 35(5). The amount payable by way of maternity allowance for a day is 1/7th of the weekly rate.
@export Under section 35(5), how much maternity allowance am I paid for one day?
GIVEN `my weekly rate of maternity allowance, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of maternity allowance, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 35(5), how much maternity allowance am I paid for one day` IS
    `s 35(5) the amount payable by way of maternity allowance for a day` `my weekly rate of maternity allowance, in pounds`

-- s 35(6). A woman is confined by labour resulting in the issue of a living child, or after 24 weeks of
-- pregnancy resulting in the issue of a child whether alive or dead; she is confined on the day of the issue of
-- the child (the last of them, for twins or more).
@export Under section 35(6), am I confined by this labour?
GIVEN `the weeks of pregnancy when my labour began` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many completed weeks of pregnancy did your labour begin?
      `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your labour result in the issue of a living child?
      `the day the child, or the last of the children, was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the child (or the last of the children) issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 35(6), am I confined by this labour` IS
    `s 35(6) the woman is confined by the labour` `my labour`
    WHERE
        `my labour` MEANS Labour WITH
            `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS `the weeks of pregnancy when my labour began`
            `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child`
            `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS `the day the child, or the last of the children, was issued`

@export Under section 35(6), on what day am I confined by this labour?
GIVEN `the weeks of pregnancy when my labour began` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many completed weeks of pregnancy did your labour begin?
      `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your labour result in the issue of a living child?
      `the day the child, or the last of the children, was issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the child (or the last of the children) issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 35(6), on what day am I confined by this labour` IS
    `s 35(6) the day on which the woman is confined` `my labour`
    WHERE
        `my labour` MEANS Labour WITH
            `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS `the weeks of pregnancy when my labour began`
            `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child`
            `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS `the day the child, or the last of the children, was issued`

-- s 35A(1). The weekly rate is the lower of the prescribed rate and 90% of average weekly earnings, or the
-- prescribed rate where subsection (5B) applies.
@export Under section 35A(1), what is my weekly rate of maternity allowance?
GIVEN `I am treated by regulations as having received the payment in each week of the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated, by regulations under section 35A(5)(c)(i), as having received a payment in each week of the specified period equal to the amount that sub-paragraph mentions?
      `my average weekly earnings, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your average weekly earnings, in pounds (worked out as section 35A(4) says)?
      `the weekly rate prescribed, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate do the regulations prescribe under section 166(1)(b), in pounds (look it up)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 35A(1), what is my weekly rate of maternity allowance` IS
    `s 35A(1) the appropriate weekly rate of maternity allowance`
        (`s 35A(5B) subsection (5B) applies` `I am treated by regulations as having received the payment in each week of the specified period`)
        (JUST `my average weekly earnings, in pounds`)
        `the weekly rate prescribed, in pounds`

-- s 35B(1). A woman who works with her self-employed spouse or civil partner is entitled to a maternity
-- allowance if (a) she is pregnant as in s 35(1)(a), (b) she worked with him or her for part of at least 26 of
-- the 66 weeks, (c) he or she paid a Class 2 contribution for those weeks, and (d) she is not entitled to a
-- maternity allowance under section 35 or to statutory maternity pay for the same week.
@export Under section 35B(1), am I entitled to a maternity allowance for working with my self-employed spouse or civil partner?
GIVEN `I have become pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become pregnant?
      `the first day of my expected week of confinement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day (a Sunday) of the week in which your baby is expected?
      `the day for which I ask` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `I have been confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already been confined (given birth)?
      `the day I was confined` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you confined (any date if you answered no)?
      `the number of those 66 weeks in which I worked with my spouse or civil partner` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 66 weeks immediately before the expected week of confinement did you work with your spouse or civil partner, who was then self-employed, for any part of the week?
      `my spouse or civil partner has paid a Class 2 contribution for the 26 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your spouse or civil partner paid a Class 2 contribution in respect of those 26 weeks?
      `I am entitled to a maternity allowance under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a maternity allowance under section 35 for the same week?
      `I am entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week in respect of the same pregnancy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 35B(1), am I entitled to a maternity allowance for working with my self-employed spouse or civil partner` IS
    `s 35B(1) W is entitled to a maternity allowance under this section`
        (`s 35(1)(a) the woman has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week before the expected week of confinement` `I have become pregnant` `my expected week of confinement` `the day for which I ask` `the day of my confinement`)
        (`s 35B(1)(b) W has worked with S for any part of the week in the case of at least 26 of the 66 weeks` `the number of those 66 weeks in which I worked with my spouse or civil partner`)
        (`s 35B(1)(c) S has paid a Class 2 contribution in respect of the 26 weeks` `my spouse or civil partner has paid a Class 2 contribution for the 26 weeks`)
        (`s 35B(1)(d) W is not entitled to a maternity allowance under section 35 or to statutory maternity pay for the same week` (JUST `I am entitled to a maternity allowance under section 35`) (JUST `I am entitled to statutory maternity pay for the same week`))
    WHERE
        `my expected week of confinement` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement`
            `the last day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement` PLUS 6
        `the day of my confinement` MEANS IF `I have been confined` THEN JUST `the day I was confined` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 35B(8). The 14-week period begins on the day after the date of confinement unless one of s 35B(5) to (7)
-- applies (the earliest of the days she ceased, or refrained from, working with her spouse or civil partner).
@export Under section 35B(8), on what day does my 14-week maternity allowance period begin?
GIVEN `the first day of my expected week of confinement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day (a Sunday) of the week in which your baby was expected?
      `the date of my confinement` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you confined (given birth)?
      `I ceased to work with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to work with your spouse or civil partner (who is self-employed)?
      `the day I ceased to work with my spouse or civil partner` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease (any date if you answered no)?
      `I refrained from working with my spouse or civil partner wholly or partly because of my pregnancy or confinement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refrain from working with your spouse or civil partner, wholly or partly because of your pregnancy or confinement?
      `the first day I so refrained` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first so refrain (any date if you answered no)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 35B(8), on what day does my 14-week maternity allowance period begin` IS
    `s 35B(8) the first day of the 14-week period` `my expected week of confinement` `the date of my confinement` `the day I ceased, if I did` `the first day I refrained, if I did`
    WHERE
        `my expected week of confinement` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement`
            `the last day` IS `the first day of my expected week of confinement` PLUS 6
        `the day I ceased, if I did` MEANS IF `I ceased to work with my spouse or civil partner` THEN JUST `the day I ceased to work with my spouse or civil partner` ELSE NOTHING
        `the first day I refrained, if I did` MEANS IF `I refrained from working with my spouse or civil partner wholly or partly because of my pregnancy or confinement` THEN JUST `the first day I so refrained` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Widowed mother's allowance and widow's pension (ss 37 to 39)`
-- These questions arise only for a person whose husband has died. A form should first ask "Has your husband died?".

-- s 37(2). A child or qualifying young person falls within the subsection if the child is a son or daughter of
-- the woman and her late husband, or he was entitled to child benefit for the child immediately before his
-- death, or the woman and he were residing together and she was then entitled to child benefit for the child.
@export Under section 37(2), does this child or qualifying young person fall within the subsection for my widowed mother's allowance?
GIVEN `the child is a son or daughter of me and my late husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child a son or daughter of you and your late husband?
      `my late husband was entitled to child benefit for the child immediately before his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late husband, immediately before his death, entitled to child benefit for the child?
      `my late husband and I were residing together immediately before his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you and your late husband residing together immediately before his death?
      `I was then entitled to child benefit for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you then entitled to child benefit for the child?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(2), does this child or qualifying young person fall within the subsection for my widowed mother's allowance` IS
    `s 37(2) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` `the child is a son or daughter of me and my late husband` `my late husband was entitled to child benefit for the child immediately before his death` `my late husband and I were residing together immediately before his death` `I was then entitled to child benefit for the child`

-- s 37(1). A woman who has been widowed is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance if her late husband
-- satisfied the contribution conditions and she (a) is entitled to child benefit for a child within (2), or (b)
-- is pregnant by him, or (c) is pregnant in the circumstances (c) describes. Only for a husband who died
-- before 9 April 2001 (s 37(A1)).
@export Under section 37(1), am I entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
GIVEN `the day my husband died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die?
      `I have been widowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been widowed?
      `my late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your late husband satisfy the contribution conditions in Schedule 3 for a widowed mother's allowance?
      `I am entitled to child benefit for a child who falls within section 37(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child benefit for a child or qualifying young person who falls within section 37(2) (see the question on that subsection)?
      `I am pregnant by my late husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant by your late husband?
      `my late husband and I were residing together immediately before his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you and your late husband residing together immediately before his death?
      `I am pregnant after artificial insemination or the placing of an embryo before his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before his death with the semen of some person other than your husband, or as the result of the placing in you before his death of an embryo, an egg in the process of fertilisation, or sperm and eggs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(1), am I entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS
    `s 37(1) the woman is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
        (`s 37(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` `the day my husband died`)
        `I have been widowed`
        (JUST `my late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed mother's allowance`)
        `I am entitled to child benefit for a child who falls within section 37(2)`
        `I am pregnant by my late husband`
        (`s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described` `my late husband and I were residing together immediately before his death` `I am pregnant after artificial insemination or the placing of an embryo before his death`)

-- s 37(3). A widow continues to be entitled to the allowance while she satisfies the requirements of
-- subsection (1), but not for any period after she remarries or forms a civil partnership.
@export Under section 37(3), am I entitled to a widowed mother's allowance on this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you remarried or formed a civil partnership?
      `the day I remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you do so (any date if you answered no)?
      `I satisfy the requirements of section 37(1)(a), (b) or (c) on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, do you satisfy the requirements of section 37(1)(a), (b) or (c) (see the question on section 37(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(3), am I entitled to a widowed mother's allowance on this day` IS
    `s 37(3) the widow is entitled to the allowance on the day` `the day` `the day of my remarriage` (JUST `I satisfy the requirements of section 37(1)(a), (b) or (c) on this day`)
    WHERE
        `the day of my remarriage` MEANS IF `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` THEN JUST `the day I remarried or formed a civil partnership` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 37(4). The allowance is not payable (a) for any period before the day on which her entitlement is regarded
-- as commencing under s 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act, nor (b) for any period during which she and a
-- person she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married
-- couple or civil partners.
@export Under section 37(4), is my widowed mother's allowance payable for this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a day on which your entitlement is regarded as commencing for payment purposes, by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act?
      `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` IS A DATE @desc What is that day (any date if you answered no)?
      `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, are you and a person you are not married to, or in a civil partnership with, living together as if you were a married couple or civil partners?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 37(4), is my widowed mother's allowance payable for this day` IS
    `s 37(4) the allowance is payable for the day` `the day` `the commencement day` `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement day` MEANS IF `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` THEN JUST `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38(1). A woman who has been widowed is entitled to a widow's pension if her late husband satisfied the
-- contribution conditions and she was over the age the section reads (45, or 40 in the 1988 case of s 38(4))
-- but under 65 when he died, or when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance. Only for a
-- husband who died before 9 April 2001 (s 38(A1)).
@export Under section 38(1), am I entitled to a widow's pension?
GIVEN `the day my husband died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die?
      `I have been widowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been widowed?
      `my late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widow's pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your late husband satisfy the contribution conditions in Schedule 3 for a widow's pension?
      `my age in completed years when my husband died` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you, in completed years, when your husband died?
      `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `my age in completed years when I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you, in completed years, when you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance (any age if you answered no)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 38(1), am I entitled to a widow's pension` IS
    `s 38(1) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension`
        (`s 38(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` `the day my husband died`)
        `I have been widowed`
        (JUST `my late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widow's pension`)
        (`s 38(4) the lower age read in subsection (1)` `my case`)
        `my age in completed years when my husband died`
        `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
        `my age in completed years when I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)` `the day my husband died` `my age in completed years when my husband died` `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` `my age in completed years when I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`

-- s 38(2). The widow is not entitled to the pension for any period after she remarries or forms a civil
-- partnership, but, subject to that, she continues to be entitled to it until she attains pensionable age.
@export Under section 38(2), am I entitled to my widow's pension on this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you remarried or formed a civil partnership?
      `the day I remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you do so (any date if you answered no)?
      `I am entitled to a widow's pension under section 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a widow's pension under section 38(1) (see the question on that subsection)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 38(2), am I entitled to my widow's pension on this day` IS
    `s 38(2) the widow is entitled to the pension on the day` `the day` `me` `the day of my remarriage` (JUST `I am entitled to a widow's pension under section 38(1)`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`
        `the day of my remarriage` MEANS IF `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` THEN JUST `the day I remarried or formed a civil partnership` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 38(3). The pension is not payable (a) for any period before the day her entitlement is regarded as
-- commencing under s 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act, (b) for any period for which she is entitled to a
-- widowed mother's allowance, or (c) for any period during which she and a person she is not married to, or in a
-- civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@export Under section 38(3), is my widow's pension payable for this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a day on which your entitlement is regarded as commencing for payment purposes, by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act?
      `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` IS A DATE @desc What is that day (any date if you answered no)?
      `I am entitled to a widowed mother's allowance for this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a widowed mother's allowance for this day?
      `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, are you and a person you are not married to, or in a civil partnership with, living together as if you were a married couple or civil partners?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 38(3), is my widow's pension payable for this day` IS
    `s 38(3) the pension is payable for the day` `the day` `the commencement day` `I am entitled to a widowed mother's allowance for this day` `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement day` MEANS IF `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` THEN JUST `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 39(4). A widow's pension is reduced by 7 per cent for each year, or part of a year, by which her age when
-- the qualifying condition was fulfilled falls short of the age subsection (6) reads (55, or 50 in the 1988 case).
@export Under section 39(4), what is the weekly rate of my widow's pension after any reduction for my age?
GIVEN `the day my husband died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die?
      `my age in completed years when my husband died` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you, in completed years, when your husband died?
      `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `my age in completed years when I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you, in completed years, when you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance (any age if you answered no)?
      `my age in completed years when the qualifying condition was fulfilled` IS A NUMBER @desc How old were you, in completed years, at the time the qualifying condition for the pension was fulfilled (section 39(5))?
      `the weekly rate of my widow's pension apart from subsection (4), in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your widow's pension before any reduction under subsection (4), in pounds (worked out under sections 44 to 45B)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 39(4), what is the weekly rate of my widow's pension after any reduction for my age` IS
    `s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of my widow's pension apart from subsection (4), in pounds`) (`s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` `my case`) `my age in completed years when the qualifying condition was fulfilled`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)` `the day my husband died` `my age in completed years when my husband died` `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` `my age in completed years when I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`

§§ `Widowed parent's allowance (ss 39A to 39C)`
-- These questions arise only for a person whose spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner has died.

-- s 39A(1), (1A) and (2). The section applies where the person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner
-- died before the day s 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force, the person has not since married or
-- formed a civil partnership or cohabiting partnership before that day, and is under pensionable age on that
-- day; it does not apply where a woman's husband died before 9 April 2001. The survivor is then entitled to a
-- widowed parent's allowance if the deceased satisfied the contribution conditions and (a) the survivor is
-- entitled to child benefit for a child within s 39A(3), or (b) a surviving spouse or cohabiting partner who is
-- a woman is pregnant by the deceased (or as s 37(1)(c) describes), or (c) a surviving civil partner or
-- cohabiting partner who is a woman is pregnant after artificial insemination while residing with the deceased.
@export Under section 39A(2), am I entitled to a widowed parent's allowance?
GIVEN `the day my spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner die?
      `the day section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day does section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 come into force (look it up)?
      `I have married or formed a civil or cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you married, or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership, after the death but before that day?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `I am a woman whose husband has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman whose husband has died?
      `the deceased satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed parent's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the deceased satisfy the contribution conditions in Schedule 3 for a widowed parent's allowance?
      `I am the` IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor` @desc Are you the surviving spouse, the surviving civil partner, or the surviving cohabiting partner?
      `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `I am entitled to child benefit for a child who falls within section 39A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child benefit for a child or qualifying young person who falls within section 39A(3)?
      `I am pregnant by the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant by the deceased?
      `we were residing together immediately before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you and the deceased residing together immediately before the time of the death?
      `I am pregnant after artificial insemination or the placing of an embryo before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before the death, or of the placing in you before the death of an embryo, an egg in the process of fertilisation, or sperm and eggs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39A(2), am I entitled to a widowed parent's allowance` IS
    `s 39A(2) the survivor is entitled to a widowed parent's allowance`
        (`s 39A(1) the section applies` `the day my spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` `the day section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force` `I have married or formed a civil or cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day` `me`)
        `the answer for a woman whose husband has died`
        (JUST `the deceased satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed parent's allowance`)
        (`s 39A(2) the survivor satisfies the requirements of paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` `I am the` `I am a woman` `I am entitled to child benefit for a child who falls within section 39A(3)` `I am pregnant by the deceased` `the pregnancy answer` `we were residing together immediately before the death` `I am pregnant after artificial insemination or the placing of an embryo before the death`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`
        `the answer for a woman whose husband has died` MEANS IF `I am a woman whose husband has died` THEN `s 39A(1A) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` `the day my spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` ELSE NOTHING
        `the pregnancy answer` MEANS `s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described` `we were residing together immediately before the death` `I am pregnant after artificial insemination or the placing of an embryo before the death`

-- s 39A(4), (4A), (4B). The survivor is not entitled to the allowance for any period after they marry, or form a
-- civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership (the kinds depend on who they are); subject to that they
-- continue to be entitled for any period throughout which they satisfy the requirements of s 39A(2) named for
-- their kind of survivor and are under pensionable age.
@export Under section 39A(4), am I entitled to my widowed parent's allowance on this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `I am the` IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor` @desc Are you the surviving spouse, the surviving civil partner, or the surviving cohabiting partner?
      `I have since married or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since married, or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership?
      `the day I did so` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you do so (any date if you answered no)?
      `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(a) on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, do you satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(a) (entitled to child benefit for a child within subsection (3))?
      `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(b) on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, do you satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(b) (a woman, surviving spouse or cohabiting partner, pregnant as that paragraph describes)?
      `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(c) on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, do you satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(c) (a woman, surviving civil partner or cohabiting partner, who resided with the deceased and is pregnant after artificial insemination)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39A(4), am I entitled to my widowed parent's allowance on this day` IS
    `s 39A(4) the survivor is entitled to the allowance on the day` `the day` `me` `the day I formed a later relationship` (`s 39A(4) the survivor satisfies the requirements named for the kind of survivor` `I am the` (JUST `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(a) on this day`) (JUST `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(b) on this day`) (JUST `I satisfy the requirements of section 39A(2)(c) on this day`))
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`
        `the day I formed a later relationship` MEANS IF `I have since married or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership` THEN JUST `the day I did so` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 39A(5). The allowance is not payable (a) for any period before the day the survivor's entitlement is
-- regarded as commencing under s 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act, nor (b) for any period during which the
-- survivor and a person they are not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they
-- were a married couple or civil partners.
@export Under section 39A(5), is my widowed parent's allowance payable for this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a day on which your entitlement is regarded as commencing for payment purposes, by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act?
      `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` IS A DATE @desc What is that day (any date if you answered no)?
      `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On this day, are you and a person you are not married to, or in a civil partnership with, living together as if you were a married couple or civil partners?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 39A(5), is my widowed parent's allowance payable for this day` IS
    `s 39A(5) the allowance is payable for the day` `the day` `the commencement day` `I am living together with a person as if we were a married couple or civil partners on this day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement day` MEANS IF `my entitlement is treated as commencing on a day under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` THEN JUST `the day my entitlement is treated as commencing` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Long-term incapacity benefit for a widow or widower (ss 40 to 42)`
-- These questions arise only for a person whose spouse has died and who is incapable of work. A form should
-- first ask "Has your husband (or wife) died, and are you incapable of work?".

-- s 40(1) and (2). Section 40 applies to a woman who (a) on her husband's death is not entitled to a widowed
-- mother's allowance, or later ceases to be, (b) is incapable of work then, (c) would have been entitled to a
-- widow's pension had she been over 45, or is entitled to one with a reduction under s 39(4), and (d) is not
-- otherwise entitled to incapacity benefit. It does not apply unless her husband died after 5 April 1979 or she
-- ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance after that date.
@export Under section 40(1), does section 40 (long-term incapacity benefit for a widow) apply to me?
GIVEN `the day my husband died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die?
      `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `the day I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to be entitled to it (any date if you answered no)?
      `I was not entitled to a widowed mother's allowance when my husband died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you not entitled to a widowed mother's allowance on your husband's death?
      `I was incapable of work at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you incapable of work at the time your husband died, or at the time you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `I would have been entitled to a widow's pension if I had been over 45` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to a widow's pension if you had been over the age of 45 when your husband died or when you ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `I am entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction because of my age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under section 39(4)?
      `I am entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 40` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 40?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(1), does section 40 (long-term incapacity benefit for a widow) apply to me` IS
    `s 40(1) the section applies to the woman`
        `the exclusion in subsection (2)`
        `I was not entitled to a widowed mother's allowance when my husband died`
        `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
        (JUST `I was incapable of work at that time`)
        (JUST `I would have been entitled to a widow's pension if I had been over 45`)
        (JUST `I am entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction because of my age`)
        `I am entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 40`
    WHERE
        `the exclusion in subsection (2)` MEANS `s 40(2) the section is not excluded by subsection (2)` `the day my husband died` `the day I ceased, if I did`
        `the day I ceased, if I did` MEANS IF `I have ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` THEN JUST `the day I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 40(3). A woman to whom section 40 applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for any day of
-- incapacity for work which falls in a period of incapacity that began before the time her husband died or
-- she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, and is after that time and after the first 364
-- days of incapacity in that period.
@export Under section 40(3), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit as a widow for this day?
GIVEN `section 40 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 40 apply to you (see the question on section 40(1))?
      `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this day a day of incapacity for work that forms part of a period of incapacity for work?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the day my husband died or I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die, or (if it applies to you) did you cease to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `the first day of my period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your period of incapacity for work?
      `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first day of the period as 1, what number is this day in the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(3), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit as a widow for this day` IS
    `s 40(3) the woman is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
        (JUST `section 40 applies to me`)
        (JUST `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`)
        `the day`
        `the day my husband died or I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
        `the first day of my period of incapacity for work`
        `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work`

-- s 40(4). A woman to whom section 40 applies who is not entitled to long-term benefit under subsection (3), but
-- who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for any day of incapacity which falls in
-- a period that began before the time and is after that time and after the first 196 days of the period.
@export Under section 40(4), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit as a terminally ill widow for this day?
GIVEN `section 40 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 40 apply to you (see the question on section 40(1))?
      `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 40(3) for this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 40(3) for this day (see the question on that subsection)?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected within 6 months?
      `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this day a day of incapacity for work that forms part of a period of incapacity for work?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the day my husband died or I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your husband die, or (if it applies to you) did you cease to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance?
      `the first day of my period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your period of incapacity for work?
      `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first day of the period as 1, what number is this day in the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(4), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit as a terminally ill widow for this day` IS
    `s 40(4) the woman is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
        (JUST `section 40 applies to me`)
        (`s 40(4) the woman is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (3)` `my entitlement under subsection (3)`)
        (`s 40(4) the woman is terminally ill` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months`)
        (JUST `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`)
        `the day`
        `the day my husband died or I ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`
        `the first day of my period of incapacity for work`
        `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work`
    WHERE
        `my entitlement under subsection (3)` MEANS IF `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 40(3) for this day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 40(5). The weekly rate is (a) the long-term rate under s 30A if she is not entitled to a widow's pension,
-- and (b) if she is entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under s 39(4), the difference between the
-- weekly rate of that pension and the rate in (a).
@export Under section 40(5), what is the weekly rate of my incapacity benefit as a widow?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a widow's pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a widow's pension?
      `I am entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction because of my age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction under section 39(4)?
      `the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds (look it up)?
      `the weekly rate of my widow's pension, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your widow's pension, in pounds (the answer to the question on section 39(4))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 40(5), what is the weekly rate of my incapacity benefit as a widow` IS
    `s 40(5) the weekly rate of incapacity benefit payable under this section` `I am entitled to a widow's pension` `I am entitled to a widow's pension with a reduction because of my age` (`s 30B(6) the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit` (JUST `the weekly rate of long-term incapacity benefit in Schedule 4, in pounds`)) (`s 38 the weekly rate of that pension in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of my widow's pension, in pounds`))

-- s 40(6). A woman is not entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 if she is over pensionable age. If she
-- has attained pensionable age and the period of incapacity did not end before then, she is entitled to a
-- Category A retirement pension instead.
@export Under section 40(6), am I entitled to incapacity benefit as a widow on this day, or to a Category A retirement pension instead?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(6), am I entitled to incapacity benefit as a widow on this day, or to a Category A retirement pension instead` IS
    `s 40(6) the woman is entitled to incapacity benefit under this section on the day` `the day` `me`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`

-- s 40(6)(a). A woman who has attained pensionable age, and whose period of incapacity did not end before then,
-- is entitled, if not otherwise entitled, to a Category A retirement pension.
@export Under section 40(6)(a), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension on this day because my period of incapacity continued to pensionable age?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `my period of incapacity did not end before I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the period of incapacity for work mentioned in section 40(3)(a) or (4)(a) not terminate before you attained pensionable age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 40(6)(a), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension on this day because my period of incapacity continued to pensionable age` IS
    `s 40(6)(a) the woman is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `the day` `me` `my period of incapacity did not end before I attained pensionable age`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`

-- s 41(1). Section 41 applies to a man whose wife died on or after 6 April 1979 and who was incapable of work
-- when she died, or becomes incapable within the prescribed period after that, and is not otherwise entitled
-- to incapacity benefit.
@export Under section 41(1), does section 41 (long-term incapacity benefit for a widower) apply to me?
GIVEN `the day my wife died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your wife die?
      `I was incapable of work when she died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you incapable of work at the time she died?
      `I became incapable of work within the prescribed period after her death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become incapable of work within the prescribed period after her death?
      `I am entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 41?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(1), does section 41 (long-term incapacity benefit for a widower) apply to me` IS
    `s 41(1) the section applies to the man` `the day my wife died` (JUST `I was incapable of work when she died`) `I became incapable of work within the prescribed period after her death` `I am entitled to incapacity benefit apart from section 41`

-- s 41(2). A man to whom section 41 applies is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit for any day of incapacity
-- which falls in a period that began before the time his wife died or within the prescribed period after it, and
-- is after that time and after the first 364 days of incapacity in that period.
@export Under section 41(2), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit as a widower for this day?
GIVEN `section 41 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 41 apply to you (see the question on section 41(1))?
      `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this day a day of incapacity for work that forms part of a period of incapacity for work?
      `my period began before my wife died or within the prescribed period after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your period of incapacity for work begin before your wife died or within the prescribed period after that time?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the day my wife died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your wife die?
      `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first day of the period as 1, what number is this day in the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(2), am I entitled to long-term incapacity benefit as a widower for this day` IS
    `s 41(2) the man is entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
        (JUST `section 41 applies to me`)
        (JUST `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`)
        `my period began before my wife died or within the prescribed period after`
        `the day`
        `the day my wife died`
        `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work`

-- s 41(3). A man to whom section 41 applies who is not entitled to long-term benefit under subsection (2), but
-- who is terminally ill, is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit for any day after the first 196 days of
-- incapacity in a period that began before the time his wife died or within the prescribed period after it.
@export Under section 41(3), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit as a terminally ill widower for this day?
GIVEN `section 41 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 41 apply to you (see the question on section 41(1))?
      `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 41(2) for this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 41(2) for this day (see the question on that subsection)?
      `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected within 6 months?
      `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this day a day of incapacity for work that forms part of a period of incapacity for work?
      `my period began before my wife died or within the prescribed period after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your period of incapacity for work begin before your wife died or within the prescribed period after that time?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the day my wife died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your wife die?
      `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first day of the period as 1, what number is this day in the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(3), am I entitled to short-term incapacity benefit as a terminally ill widower for this day` IS
    `s 41(3) the man is entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under this section for the day`
        (JUST `section 41 applies to me`)
        (`s 41(3) the man is not entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (2)` `my entitlement under subsection (2)`)
        (`s 41(3) the man is terminally ill` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `my death in consequence of that disease can reasonably be expected within 6 months`)
        (JUST `this day is a day of incapacity for work forming part of a period of incapacity for work`)
        `my period began before my wife died or within the prescribed period after`
        `the day`
        `the day my wife died`
        `the number of this day in my period of incapacity for work`
    WHERE
        `my entitlement under subsection (2)` MEANS IF `I am entitled to long-term incapacity benefit under section 41(2) for this day` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 41(5). A man is not entitled to incapacity benefit under section 41 if he is over pensionable age. If he has
-- attained pensionable age and the period did not end before then, he is entitled to a Category A retirement
-- pension instead (unless he is entitled to a Category B pension on his wife's contributions).
@export Under section 41(5), am I entitled to incapacity benefit as a widower on this day?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(5), am I entitled to incapacity benefit as a widower on this day` IS
    `s 41(5) the man is entitled to incapacity benefit under this section on the day` `the day` `me`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Man
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`

-- s 41(5)(a). A man who has attained pensionable age, and whose period of incapacity did not end before then,
-- is entitled, if not otherwise entitled to a Category A pension and also not entitled to a Category B pension on
-- his wife's contributions, to a Category A retirement pension.
@export Under section 41(5)(a), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension on this day because my period of incapacity continued to pensionable age?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask?
      `the date I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you attain (or did you attain) pensionable age?
      `my period of incapacity did not end before I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the period of incapacity for work mentioned in section 41(2)(a) or (3)(a) not terminate before you attained pensionable age?
      `I am entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my wife's contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of your wife's contributions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 41(5)(a), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension on this day because my period of incapacity continued to pensionable age` IS
    `s 41(5)(a) the man is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` `the day` `me` `my period of incapacity did not end before I attained pensionable age` `I am entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my wife's contributions`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule called here reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900
            `sex` IS Man
            `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the date I attain pensionable age`

-- s 42(1A). The relevant tax credit conditions on a day: (a) entitled to the disability element of working tax
-- credit (or would be but for the relevant income), and (b) either working tax credit or a child tax credit
-- element other than the family element is paid for the day.
@export Under section 42(1A), do I satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions on this day?
GIVEN `I am entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit (on your own claim or a joint claim)?
      `I would be so entitled but for the relevant income in my or our case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be so entitled but for the relevant income in your or your joint case?
      `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is working tax credit, or any element of child tax credit other than the family element, paid for the day on such a claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(1A), do I satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions on this day` IS
    `s 42(1A) the person satisfies the relevant tax credit conditions on the day` `I am entitled for the day to the disability element of working tax credit` `I would be so entitled but for the relevant income in my or our case` `working tax credit or an element of child tax credit other than the family element is paid for the day`

-- s 42(1). A person who claims incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 for a period starting after they ceased
-- to be in qualifying remunerative work, and (a) the day after was a day of incapacity, (b) they were entitled to
-- incapacity benefit under that section within the two years ending with that day, and (c) they met the tax
-- credit conditions the day before they ceased, has every day in the claim on which they meet those conditions
-- treated as a day of incapacity for work. Section 42 grants no benefit itself: s 40 or s 41 then applies.
@export Under section 42(1), is this day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim under section 40 or 41 after I stopped qualifying remunerative work?
GIVEN `my claim is for incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41?
      `the first day of the period for which I claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you claim?
      `the last day of the period for which I claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period for which you claim?
      `the day I stopped qualifying remunerative work` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease to be in qualifying remunerative work?
      `the day after I stopped was a day of incapacity for work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the day after you ceased work a day of incapacity for work for you?
      `I was entitled to incapacity benefit under that section within the two years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 within the two years ending with that day of incapacity?
      `the latest day I was so entitled` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you last so entitled (any date if you answered no)?
      `I met the tax credit conditions on the day before I stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions (section 42(1A)) on the day before you ceased work?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc For which day of your claim do you ask?
      `I meet the tax credit conditions on this day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the relevant tax credit conditions (section 42(1A)) on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(1), is this day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim under section 40 or 41 after I stopped qualifying remunerative work` IS
    `s 42(1) the day is treated as a day of incapacity for work for the claim`
        `my claim is for incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41`
        `my claim period`
        `the day I stopped qualifying remunerative work`
        (JUST `the day after I stopped was a day of incapacity for work for me`)
        `the latest day of entitlement`
        (JUST `I met the tax credit conditions on the day before I stopped`)
        `the day`
        (JUST `I meet the tax credit conditions on this day`)
    WHERE
        `my claim period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of the period for which I claim`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of the period for which I claim`
        `the latest day of entitlement` MEANS IF `I was entitled to incapacity benefit under that section within the two years` THEN JUST `the latest day I was so entitled` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 42(2). A person who becomes engaged in training for work, was entitled to incapacity benefit under section
-- 40 or 41 for one or more of the 56 days before, and for whom the first day after the training ends is a day of
-- incapacity within two years of the last day of entitlement, has each training day after that last day treated
-- as a day of incapacity for work for a claim for a period starting after the training ends.
@export Under section 42(2), is this training day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim under section 40 or 41?
GIVEN `the first day I was engaged in training for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day you were engaged in training for work?
      `I was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 within the 56 days before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 for one or more of the 56 days immediately before you began training?
      `the last day I was so entitled` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you last so entitled (any date if you answered no)?
      `the first day after my training ended` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day after you ceased to be engaged in training for work?
      `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that first day a day of incapacity for work for you?
      `the training day` IS A DATE @desc For which training day do you ask?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 42(2), is this training day treated as a day of incapacity for work for my claim under section 40 or 41` IS
    `s 42(2) the training day is treated as a day of incapacity for work` `the first day I was engaged in training for work` `the last day of entitlement` `the first day after my training ended` `that first day is a day of incapacity for work for me` `the training day`
    WHERE
        `the last day of entitlement` MEANS IF `I was entitled to incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 within the 56 days before` THEN JUST `the last day I was so entitled` ELSE NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc3 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4, sections 43 to 62
-- (retirement pensions, additional pension, shared additional pension, child's special allowance,
-- contribution failures and deferment) -- THE SEAT LAYER of part ssc3.
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit,
-- statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great Britain, asking on facts they can state whether they are
-- entitled to a retirement pension (or to a shared additional pension, or to a child's special
-- allowance), how much it is worth, and what ends, reduces or increases it.
--
-- Nothing here is new law. Each question builds the records the layer-1 modules expect (a Person, a
-- list of pensions) from plain answers and calls the rule that already exists in ssc3-a-s43-s44.l4
-- to ssc3-g-s60-s62.l4. No rule is restated here.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, numbers, dates and the core's own choices, one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A fact that the
-- Act hands to a rule in another part (a contribution condition in Schedule 3, the meaning of
-- "relevant carer" in section 23A, whether two people are a couple under section 137) is asked of the
-- person as a plain yes/no, and the answer is passed to the layer-1 rule as JUST of that answer. The
-- person never states NOTHING: a question the person cannot answer is left to the layer-1 rule, which
-- answers NOTHING ("not covered") where the text does not decide.
--
-- WHAT THE SEAT FIXES (stated once, so a later reader can find it):
--   * Wherever a rule takes a Person, the seat builds one from: whether the person is a woman (the Act
--     says "woman" and "man" and defines neither except in s 140A(5); the person states which applies),
--     the date of birth, and the date the person attains (or attained) pensionable age. That date is
--     borrowed from the Pensions Act 1995 (s 122(1)) and is a fact the person states.
--   * The field `marital status` of a Person is read by no rule in sections 43 to 62. The seat sets it to
--     the status that the question itself presupposes (a widow's question says `widowed or a surviving civil
--     partner`), a placeholder that no rule reads, and says so at each use.
--   * The contribution conditions of Schedule 3 Part I (paragraphs 5, 5A, 6) are another part's answer.
--     The person states one yes/no for them. Where the layer-1 rule has a slot for paragraph 5 and a slot
--     for paragraph 5A, the same answer goes to both, because the layer-1 rule itself picks the slot
--     that applies by the date of attaining pensionable age (s 44(1A)).
--   * Amounts that regulations, orders or the Secretary of State set (the specified amount per unit of
--     additional pension, revaluation percentages, rates under Schedule 4) are asked in pounds or
--     per cent; the seat never supplies one. A later substitution of the Act's own figures (for
--     instance the weekly rate in s 44(4)) changes the layer-1 constants, not the seat.

§ `Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, ss 43 to 62 -- the pensioner's questions`

§§ `Section 43: when I qualify for more than one retirement pension`

-- s 43(1) to (5). A person who, apart from s 43(1), would be entitled to both a Category A and a
-- Category B retirement pension for the same period is entitled to one only: the one named in a
-- notice given to the Secretary of State that has effect for the week, or else the most favourable.
-- The answer is the name of the pension that the person is entitled to for the week; NOTHING where
-- the text does not decide (two notices with effect for the same week).
@export Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension?
GIVEN `I qualify for a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify for a Category A retirement pension for the week?
      `the weekly rate of my Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the weekly rate of your Category A retirement pension be, in pounds? (0 if you do not qualify)
      `I qualify for a Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify for a Category B retirement pension for the week, through your spouse, civil partner or former spouse or civil partner?
      `the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the weekly rate of your Category B retirement pension be, in pounds? (0 if you do not qualify)
      `I have given notice saying which pension I want` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Secretary of State written notice saying which of the two pensions you want to receive?
      `my notice asks for the Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice ask for the Category A pension? (answer no if it asks for the Category B pension, or if you gave no notice)
      `the date of my notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give your notice? (any date if you gave none)
      `the week begins on` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the week begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
DECIDE `Under section 43, which retirement pension am I entitled to for a week when I qualify for both a Category A and a Category B pension` IS
    `s 43(1) the pensions the person is entitled to for the week` pensions notices `the week begins on`
    WHERE
        pensions MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `I qualify for a Category A retirement pension` AND `I qualify for a Category B retirement pension` THEN LIST `my Category A pension`, `my Category B pension`
                IF `I qualify for a Category A retirement pension` THEN LIST `my Category A pension`
                IF `I qualify for a Category B retirement pension` THEN LIST `my Category B pension`
                OTHERWISE EMPTY
        -- Placeholders: the two last fields of a pension in contention ("awarded because of section 61ZA" and "because of section 61ZB")
        -- are FALSE here. A pension awarded because of units of additional pension has its own questions (ss 61ZA to 61ZC below),
        -- and the combinations s 61ZC(1) and (2) lift are asked there, not in this question.
        `my Category A pension` MEANS
            `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category A retirement pension`, "my Category A pension", `the weekly rate of my Category A retirement pension in pounds`, FALSE, FALSE
        `my Category B pension` MEANS
            `s 43 Pension in contention` OF `Category B retirement pension`, "my Category B pension", `the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds`, FALSE, FALSE
        notices MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `I have given notice saying which pension I want` AND `my notice asks for the Category A retirement pension` THEN LIST `s 43 Notice` OF "my Category A pension", `the date of my notice`
                IF `I have given notice saying which pension I want` THEN LIST `s 43 Notice` OF "my Category B pension", `the date of my notice`
                OTHERWISE EMPTY

§§ `Section 44: Category A retirement pension`

-- s 44(1). A person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension if they attained pensionable age
-- before 6 April 2016 and satisfy the contribution conditions (Schedule 3 Part I, paragraph 5 for
-- those who attained it before 6 April 2010, paragraph 5A for the rest). The layer-1 rule picks the
-- paragraph by the date of attaining pensionable age; the person states one yes/no for whichever
-- paragraph applies to them (see the header). The Act's "woman"/"man" is not read by this rule, and
-- neither is the date of birth or the marital status: fixed placeholders below.
@export Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you (or will you) reach State Pension age?
      `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your National Insurance contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(1), am I entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS
    `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` me (JUST `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`) (JUST `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 44(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 44(1), closing words: the person becomes entitled on the day they attain pensionable age.
@export Under section 44(1), on what day do I become entitled to a Category A retirement pension?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you (or will you) reach State Pension age?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 44(1), on what day do I become entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS
    `s 44(1) the day on which the person becomes entitled` me
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: the rule reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 44(1), closing words: the entitlement continues throughout the person's life.
-- The answer is JUST TRUE for a day on or after the day of becoming entitled while the person is alive,
-- JUST FALSE for a day after their death, and NOTHING for a day before they became entitled.
@export Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you (or will you) reach State Pension age?
      `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your National Insurance contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who held the pension died? (answer no if you are asking about your own pension while you are alive)
      `the day I died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did they die? (any date if no one has died)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(1), is my Category A retirement pension running on a given day` IS
    `s 44(1) the entitlement is running on the day` me entitled `the day I ask about` `the date of death`
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 44(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        entitled MEANS
            `s 44(1) the person is entitled to a Category A retirement pension` me (JUST `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`) (JUST `my contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        `the date of death` MEANS
            IF `I have died` THEN JUST `the day I died` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 44(2). The pension is payable in respect of a day from the day on which the entitlement is to be
-- regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act (not among the sources: stated by the person).
@export Under section 44(2), is my Category A retirement pension payable in respect of a given day?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `the day my entitlement is regarded as commencing` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your entitlement regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k) of the Social Security Administration Act 1992? (the date the Department for Work and Pensions gives you)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 44(2), is my Category A retirement pension payable in respect of a given day` IS
    `s 44(2) the Category A retirement pension is payable in respect of the day` `the day I ask about` `the day my entitlement is regarded as commencing`

-- s 44(4). The weekly rate of the basic pension is the Act's figure, or the lower figure where the
-- sum is relevant for working out the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit under s 30B(3).
@export Under section 44(4), what is the weekly rate of my basic pension, in pounds?
GIVEN `the sum is to work out the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you need the figure to work out the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit (section 30B(3))? (answer no if you want the basic pension itself)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 44(4), what is the weekly rate of my basic pension` IS
    `s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` `the sum is to work out the lower rate of short-term incapacity benefit`

§§ `Sections 44A to 44C: earnings factors the Act gives me for a year or a week`

-- s 44A(1) and (2). For a tax year in which the person's earnings factor is low but one of four
-- conditions holds (a low earnings factor; carer's allowance; responsibility for a young child; long-term
-- incapacity), the person is treated as having an earnings factor equal to the low earnings threshold,
-- which counts toward the Category A pension. The first condition is arithmetic on the person's
-- earnings; the second to fourth are facts. Section 44A(4) counts the working life the fourth condition
-- measures against. The figures of the year (the qualifying earnings factor, the low earnings
-- threshold) are set by regulations and orders, so the person states them.
@export Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low?
GIVEN `my earnings factor for the year apart from section 44A` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for the year, in pounds, without counting section 44A?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the low earnings threshold for the year, in pounds?
      `carer's allowance was payable to me throughout the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was carer's allowance payable to you throughout the year?
      `carer's allowance would have been payable but for a reduction to nil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would carer's allowance have been payable throughout the year but for being reduced to nil because you receive other benefits?
      `child benefit was payable to me throughout the year in respect of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was child benefit payable to you throughout the year in respect of a child?
      `that child was under 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that child under 6 years old?
      `I satisfy another condition prescribed for responsibilities at home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy another condition that regulations prescribe for people with responsibilities at home?
      `long-term incapacity benefit was payable to me throughout the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was long-term incapacity benefit (or qualifying employment and support allowance) payable to you throughout the year?
      `I did not satisfy the contribution conditions for that benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to satisfy the contribution conditions for that benefit?
      `the amount was reduced to nil because of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under regulations, was the amount payable reduced to nil because you receive other benefits?
      `the amount was reduced to nil because of payments from a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under regulations, was the amount payable reduced to nil because you receive payments from a pension scheme?
      `the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme an occupational pension scheme?
      `the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme a personal pension scheme?
      `years in my working life before the exclusions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many tax years are in your working life, before section 44A(4) takes any out?
      `of which before 1978-79` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, how many are before the tax year 1978-79?
      `of which I am treated under section 44A as having a factor because of carer's allowance or responsibilities at home` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, how many are years in which you are treated under section 44A, because of carer's allowance or responsibilities at home, as having an earnings factor?
      `years in which my factor is at least the qualifying earnings factor` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many relevant years is your earnings factor equal to or greater than the qualifying earnings factor?
      `my other earnings factors for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What other earnings factors are taken into account for the year under section 44(6), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 44A, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year in which my own earnings factor was low` IS
    `s 44A(1) the deemed earnings factor in pounds`
        (`s 44A(2) any of the conditions in subsection (2) is satisfied` conditionA conditionB conditionC conditionD)
        `the low earnings threshold for the year`
        `my other earnings factors for the year`
    WHERE
        conditionA MEANS
            `s 44A(2)(a) the earnings factor lies from the qualifying earnings factor up to the low earnings threshold`
                `my earnings factor for the year apart from section 44A`
                `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
                `the low earnings threshold for the year`
        conditionB MEANS
            `s 44A(2)(b) carer's allowance condition`
                `carer's allowance was payable to me throughout the year`
                `carer's allowance would have been payable but for a reduction to nil`
        conditionC MEANS
            `s 44A(2)(c) responsibilities at home condition`
                `child benefit was payable to me throughout the year in respect of a child`
                (JUST `that child was under 6`)
                `I satisfy another condition prescribed for responsibilities at home`
        conditionD MEANS
            `s 44A(2)(d) incapacity benefit condition`
                (JUST (`s 44A(3) the requirement referred to in subsection (2)(d) is satisfied` `years in which my factor is at least the qualifying earnings factor` `one tenth of my working life`))
                `long-term incapacity benefit was payable to me throughout the year`
                `I did not satisfy the contribution conditions for that benefit`
                `the amount was reduced to nil because of other benefits`
                `the amount was reduced to nil because of payments from a scheme`
                (JUST `the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`)
                (JUST `the scheme is a personal pension scheme`)
        `one tenth of my working life` MEANS
            `s 44A(4)(b) one tenth of the working life rounded to the nearest whole year` `my working life`
        `my working life` MEANS
            `s 44A(4)(a) the pensioner's working life in years`
                `years in my working life before the exclusions`
                `of which before 1978-79`
                `of which I am treated under section 44A as having a factor because of carer's allowance or responsibilities at home`

-- s 44B(2). For a tax year from the flat rate introduction year, a person with a low earnings factor
-- is treated as having an earnings factor equal to the low earnings threshold in three cases (Conditions A,
-- B and C), the third measured in earnings factor credits under s 44C. The conditions are arithmetic on
-- figures the person states. Whether the year is the flat rate introduction year or later is a fact the
-- person states (the layer-1 rule takes it as an input).
@export Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year?
GIVEN `my earnings factor for the year apart from section 44B` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for the year, in pounds, without counting section 44B?
      `my earnings factor for the year apart from sections 44B and 44C` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for the year, in pounds, without counting sections 44B and 44C?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `the low earnings threshold for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the low earnings threshold for the year, in pounds?
      `the aggregate of my earnings factor credits for the year under section 44C` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of earnings factor credits you are entitled to for the year under section 44C, in pounds?
      `the number of my earnings factor credits for the year under section 44C` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earnings factor credits are you entitled to for the year under section 44C?
      `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the year the flat rate introduction year, or a later year?
      `my other earnings factors for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What other earnings factors are taken into account for the year under section 44(6)(za), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 44B, what earnings factor am I treated as having for a tax year from the flat rate introduction year` IS
    `s 44B(2) the deemed earnings factor in pounds`
        conditionA conditionB conditionC
        `the year is the flat rate introduction year or a later year`
        `the low earnings threshold for the year`
        `my other earnings factors for the year`
    WHERE
        conditionA MEANS
            `s 44B(3) Condition A is satisfied`
                `my earnings factor for the year apart from section 44B`
                `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
                `the low earnings threshold for the year`
        conditionB MEANS
            `s 44B(4) Condition B is satisfied`
                `my earnings factor for the year apart from sections 44B and 44C`
                `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
                `the aggregate of my earnings factor credits for the year under section 44C`
        conditionC MEANS
            `s 44B(5) Condition C is satisfied` `the number of my earnings factor credits for the year under section 44C`

-- s 44C(2) and (3). For a week in a relevant year in which the person was a carer, or received a long-term
-- incapacity or severe disablement benefit (and meets the other conditions of s 44C(3)), the person is
-- entitled to an earnings factor credit equal to 1/52 of the qualifying earnings factor for the year (s 44C(2)).
@export Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week?
GIVEN `the week falls in a relevant year to which section 44C applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in a relevant year to which section 44C applies?
      `I was a relevant carer in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a "relevant carer" (section 23A(3)) in respect of the week?
      `carer's allowance was payable to me for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was carer's allowance payable to you for any part of the week?
      `carer's allowance would have been payable but for a reduction to nil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would carer's allowance have been payable for any part of the week but for being reduced to nil because you receive other benefits?
      `severe disablement allowance was payable to me for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was severe disablement allowance payable to you for any part of the week?
      `long-term incapacity benefit was payable to me for any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was long-term incapacity benefit payable to you for any part of the week?
      `I did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3?
      `the amount was reduced to nil because of other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under regulations, was the amount payable reduced to nil because you receive other benefits?
      `the amount was reduced to nil because of payments from a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under regulations, was the amount payable reduced to nil because you receive payments from a pension scheme?
      `the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme an occupational pension scheme?
      `the scheme is a personal pension scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that scheme a personal pension scheme?
      `I satisfy another condition prescribed for paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy another condition that regulations prescribe for section 44C(3)(e)?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 44C, what earnings factor credit do I get for a week` IS
    `s 44C(2) the earnings factor credit for the week in pounds`
        `the week falls in a relevant year to which section 44C applies`
        eligible
        `the qualifying earnings factor for the year`
    WHERE
        eligible MEANS
            `s 44C(3) the pensioner is eligible for earnings factor enhancement in respect of the week`
                (JUST `I was a relevant carer in respect of the week`)
                `carer's allowance was payable to me for any part of the week`
                `carer's allowance would have been payable but for a reduction to nil`
                `severe disablement allowance was payable to me for any part of the week`
                `long-term incapacity benefit was payable to me for any part of the week`
                `I did not satisfy the contribution conditions in paragraph 2 of Schedule 3`
                `the amount was reduced to nil because of other benefits`
                `the amount was reduced to nil because of payments from a scheme`
                (JUST `the scheme is an occupational pension scheme`)
                (JUST `the scheme is a personal pension scheme`)
                `I satisfy another condition prescribed for paragraph (e)`

§§ `Sections 45 to 45B: additional pension`

-- s 45(1). Where the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 1999: the weekly rate of additional
-- pension is the weekly equivalent of 1.25 per cent of the adjusted surpluses, plus the units of additional
-- pension at the specified amount for each unit. The specified amount is set by regulations: stated by the person.
@export Under section 45(1), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension, in pounds, if I reached pensionable age before 6 April 1999?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `the adjusted amount of my surpluses in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjusted amount of the surpluses in your earnings factors that section 44(3)(b) mentions, in pounds?
      `the number of units of additional pension I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension do you have?
      `the specified amount for each unit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do regulations specify for each unit of additional pension, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 45(1), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age before 6 April 1999` IS
    `s 45(1) the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds`
        me
        `the adjusted amount of my surpluses in pounds`
        `the number of units of additional pension I have`
        (`s 45(2A) the specified amount for each unit in pounds` (JUST `the specified amount for each unit in pounds`))
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 45(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 45(2). Where the person attained pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999: the sum of the weekly
-- equivalents of four amounts (25/N per cent of the early surpluses; the relevant percentage of the later
-- surpluses; the Schedule 4A amount; the Schedule 4B amount), plus the units. Paragraph (d) is omitted
-- where section 46(4)(a) so provides: for a pension calculated under section 45 by virtue of section 39C(1)
-- where the person who died was under pensionable age. The person states those two facts and s 46(4) is called.
-- SEAT READING (reading (b), listed in NOTES.md): s 46(4) answers JUST TRUE inside its case and NOTHING outside it
-- ("limited by its own wording"). The seat passes `s 46(4) ... EQUALS JUST TRUE` as the fact "paragraph (d) is
-- omitted", so outside the bereavement case paragraph (d) stays as enacted; the other reading would make every
-- ordinary pension NOTHING.
@export Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension, in pounds, if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or will) you reach State Pension age?
      `the adjusted amount of my surpluses for the tax years 1978-79 to 1987-88 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjusted amount of your surpluses for the tax years 1978-79 to 1987-88, in pounds?
      `the adjusted amount of my surpluses for the tax years after 1987-88 and before the first appointed year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the adjusted amount of your surpluses for the tax years after 1987-88 and before the first appointed year, in pounds?
      `N, the number of tax years in my working life after 5 April 1978` IS A NUMBER @desc How many tax years in your working life fall after 5 April 1978?
      `the Schedule 4A amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount calculated in accordance with Schedule 4A, in pounds?
      `the Schedule 4B amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount calculated in accordance with Schedule 4B, in pounds?
      `my additional pension is calculated by virtue of the bereavement provision in section 39C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your additional pension one that falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of section 39C (bereavement)?
      `the person who died was under pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died (spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner) under pensionable age when they died? (answer no if nobody died)
      `the number of units of additional pension I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension do you have?
      `the specified amount for each unit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do regulations specify for each unit of additional pension, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 45(2), what is the weekly rate of my additional pension if I reached pensionable age on or after 6 April 1999` IS
    `s 45(2) the weekly rate of the additional pension in pounds`
        me
        `the adjusted amount of my surpluses for the tax years 1978-79 to 1987-88 in pounds`
        `the adjusted amount of my surpluses for the tax years after 1987-88 and before the first appointed year in pounds`
        `N, the number of tax years in my working life after 5 April 1978`
        (JUST `the Schedule 4A amount in pounds`)
        (JUST `the Schedule 4B amount in pounds`)
        omitted
        `the number of units of additional pension I have`
        (`s 45(2A) the specified amount for each unit in pounds` (JUST `the specified amount for each unit in pounds`))
    WHERE
        omitted MEANS
            `s 46(4) section 45 has effect subject to the additional modifications` (JUST `my additional pension is calculated by virtue of the bereavement provision in section 39C`) `the person who died was under pensionable age` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 45(2) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 45AA. For a year in which a working families' tax credit or a disabled person's tax credit is paid in respect of an employed earner,
-- the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid are treated as increased by the credit (AG), or, if they were below the
-- qualifying earnings factor, as AG plus that factor; the result is never more than the upper earnings limit times 53. Subsection (4)
-- takes the rule away from a woman with an unrevoked reduced-rate election. The qualifying earnings factor, the credit and the upper
-- earnings limit are set outside the sources: the person states them.
@export Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid, in pounds?
GIVEN `a working families' tax credit or a disabled person's tax credit was paid in respect of me as an employed earner for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For this tax year, was a working families' tax credit paid in respect of you as an employed earner, or a disabled person's tax credit paid to you as one?
      `I am a woman who has made, or is treated as having made, an unrevoked election to pay primary Class 1 contributions at a reduced rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a woman: have you made, or are you treated as having made, an election to pay primary Class 1 contributions at a reduced rate, which has not been revoked? (No, if you are a man.)
      `the earnings on which I paid, or was treated as paying, primary Class 1 contributions for the year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the earnings on which primary Class 1 contributions were paid, or treated as paid, for the year, in pounds?
      `the qualifying earnings factor for the year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the qualifying earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `the aggregate amount of the credit paid for the year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount of the tax credit paid for the year, in pounds?
      `the upper earnings limit for the year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the upper earnings limit for the year, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 45AA, what are my qualifying earnings for a year in which a tax credit was paid` IS
    `s 45AA(1) the qualifying earnings treated as paid in pounds`
        `a working families' tax credit or a disabled person's tax credit was paid in respect of me as an employed earner for the year`
        (`s 45AA(4) subsection (1) applies to the woman` `I am a woman who has made, or is treated as having made, an unrevoked election to pay primary Class 1 contributions at a reduced rate`)
        `the earnings on which I paid, or was treated as paying, primary Class 1 contributions for the year in pounds`
        `the qualifying earnings factor for the year in pounds`
        `the aggregate amount of the credit paid for the year in pounds`
        `the upper earnings limit for the year in pounds`

-- s 45B. If the person has become subject to a state scheme pension debit (a pension-sharing order on
-- divorce), the weekly rate of their additional pension is reduced by the appropriate weekly amount, and
-- revalued by the relevant percentage where the debit came in or after the final relevant year. The
-- appropriate weekly amount and the percentage are set outside the sources: the person states them.
@export Under section 45B, what is the weekly rate of my additional pension, in pounds, after a pension debit?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of my additional pension before the reduction in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your additional pension before the reduction, in pounds?
      `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate weekly amount of the pension debit, in pounds?
      `I became subject to the debit in or after the final relevant year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become subject to the pension debit in or after the last tax year before the one in which you reached pensionable age?
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant revaluation percentage, as a percentage? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 45B, what is the weekly rate of my additional pension after a pension debit` IS
    `s 45B(2) the weekly rate of the additional pension after the reduction in pounds`
        `the weekly rate of my additional pension before the reduction in pounds`
        (JUST `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`)
        `I became subject to the debit in or after the final relevant year`
        (JUST `the relevant revaluation percentage`)

§§ `Section 47: increase of a Category A pension for a long-term incapacity age addition`

-- s 47(1). The weekly rate of a Category A pension is increased by the age addition to long-term
-- incapacity benefit the person was getting on a day in the 8 weeks before pensionable age, or on the
-- last day before those weeks. Section 61(1) takes the increase away where the pension has no basic
-- pension because a contribution condition failed (or is payable only by virtue of s 60(1)).
@export Under section 47(1), by how much, in pounds a week, is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `I was entitled to an age addition on a day in the 8 weeks before I attain pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit on any day in the 8 weeks ending immediately before the day you reached pensionable age?
      `I was entitled to an age addition on the last day before those 8 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to an age addition on the last day before those 8 weeks began?
      `the weekly rate of my age addition in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly rate of your age addition, in pounds?
      `my pension is payable only by virtue of section 60(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pension payable only because regulations under section 60(1) give you entitlement despite a contribution failure?
      `my pension contains no basic pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your pension contain no basic pension because you failed to satisfy a contribution condition?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 47(1), by how much is my Category A pension increased because I got an age addition to long-term incapacity benefit` IS
    `s 47(1) the increase of the weekly rate in pounds`
        (`s 61(1) the increase under section 47(1) is excluded` `Category A retirement pension` (JUST `my pension is payable only by virtue of section 60(1)`) (JUST `my pension contains no basic pension`))
        (JUST `I was entitled to an age addition on a day in the 8 weeks before I attain pensionable age`)
        (JUST `I was entitled to an age addition on the last day before those 8 weeks`)
        (JUST `the weekly rate of my age addition in pounds`)

§§ `Section 48: Category A pension from a former spouse's or civil partner's contributions`

-- s 48(1) to (3). A person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has been in a marriage or civil
-- partnership that ended may have the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions treated as their own
-- for a claim to a Category A retirement pension, if their own contributions do not satisfy the contribution
-- conditions up to the year the relationship ended. Subsection (2) switches it off for early cases, and
-- subsection (3) limits it to the last relevant relationship.
@export Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I have been in a relevant relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been married, or in a civil partnership, that has ended?
      `the day that relationship ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that marriage or civil partnership end?
      `it is the last relevant relationship I have had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the last marriage or civil partnership you have had?
      `my own contributions satisfy the contribution conditions up to that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your own contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension, counting up to the tax year in which that relationship ended?
      `my claim is for a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim a claim for a Category A retirement pension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48(1), can my former spouse's or civil partner's contributions be treated as my own for a Category A retirement pension` IS
    `s 48(1) the former spouse's or civil partner's contributions may be treated as the person's own`
        me
        `I have been in a relevant relationship`
        (JUST `my own contributions satisfy the contribution conditions up to that year`)
        `my claim is for a Category A retirement pension`
        (`s 48(2) subsection (1) is disapplied for the person` me `the day that relationship ended`)
        (`s 48(3) the relationship is not excluded by subsection (3)` `it is the last relevant relationship I have had`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: ss 48(1) and 48(2) read only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

§§ `Section 48A: Category B pension for a married person or civil partner`

-- s 48A(1), (2) and (6). A married person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 is entitled to a
-- Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions if the spouse has attained pensionable
-- age and satisfies the relevant contribution condition. Subsection (2) bars a man whose spouse was born before
-- 6 April 1950 and a woman whose wife was born before that date (s 51ZA(1) lifts the bar for a woman in a marriage
-- that predates her spouse's gender recognition certificate).
@export Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I am married to my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you married to your spouse?
      `my spouse is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse a woman?
      `my spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your spouse's date of birth?
      `the day my spouse attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or will) your spouse reach State Pension age?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `my spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004? (answer no if she is not)
      `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your marriage subsist before that certificate was issued? (answer no if there is no certificate)
      `my spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48A(1), am I, as a married person, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my spouse's contributions` IS
    `s 48A(1) the married person is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions`
        me spouse
        `I am married to my spouse`
        `the day I ask about`
        (JUST (`s 51ZA(1) section 48A(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` me `my spouse is a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued`))
        (JUST `my spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        (JUST `my spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: ss 48A(1) and (2) read the sex and the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant, not the date of birth.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS (IF `I am a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `married`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        spouse MEANS
            Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS `my spouse's date of birth`
                `sex` IS (IF `my spouse is a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `married`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my spouse attains pensionable age`

-- s 48A(3). A civil partner who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 is entitled to a Category B
-- retirement pension by virtue of the contributing civil partner's contributions if that partner was born on or
-- after 6 April 1950, has attained pensionable age, and satisfies the condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3.
@export Under section 48A(3), am I, as a civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my civil partner's contributions?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I am the civil partner of the contributing civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in a civil partnership with them?
      `my civil partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your civil partner's date of birth?
      `the day my civil partner attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or will) your civil partner reach State Pension age?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
      `my civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48A(3), am I, as a civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my civil partner's contributions` IS
    `s 48A(3) the civil partner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the contributing civil partner`
        me partner
        `I am the civil partner of the contributing civil partner`
        `the day I ask about`
        (JUST `my civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution condition`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 48A(3) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        partner MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholder: s 48A(3) does not read the sex of the contributing civil partner.
                `date of birth` IS `my civil partner's date of birth`
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `in a civil partnership`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my civil partner attains pensionable age`

§§ `Section 48AA: Category B pension after a divorce or the dissolution of a civil partnership`

-- s 48AA(1) and (2). A person whose marriage has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement
-- pension by virtue of the former spouse's contributions on terms parallel to s 48A(1); subsection (2) bars a
-- man whose former spouse was born before 6 April 1950 and a woman whose former wife was (s 51ZA(2) lifts the bar
-- for a woman in a marriage that predates her former spouse's gender recognition certificate).
@export Under section 48AA(1), am I, after a divorce, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my former spouse's contributions?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `my former spouse is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your former spouse a woman?
      `my former spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your former spouse's date of birth?
      `the day my former spouse attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or will) your former spouse reach State Pension age?
      `the day my marriage was dissolved` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your marriage dissolved?
      `my former spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your former spouse, when the marriage was dissolved, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004? (answer no if she was not)
      `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your marriage subsist before that certificate was issued? (answer no if there is no certificate)
      `my former spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your former spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48AA(1), am I, after a divorce, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my former spouse's contributions` IS
    `s 48AA(1) the person whose marriage has been dissolved is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the former spouse's contributions`
        me spouse
        `the day my marriage was dissolved`
        (JUST (`s 51ZA(2) section 48AA(2)(b) does not prevent the woman from being entitled` me `my former spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued`))
        (JUST `my former spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        (JUST `my former spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: ss 48AA(1) and (2) read the sex and the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant, not the date of birth.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS (IF `I am a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        spouse MEANS
            Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS `my former spouse's date of birth`
                `sex` IS (IF `my former spouse is a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my former spouse attains pensionable age`

§§ `Section 48B: Category B pension for a widow, widower or surviving civil partner`

-- s 48B(1), (1ZA) and (1ZB). A person whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B
-- retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions if the person attained pensionable age before 6 April
-- 2016 and before the death, and the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition; subsection (1ZA) bars
-- the claim on terms parallel to s 48A(2) (s 51ZA(3) lifts the bar in the gender-change case).
@export Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `my late spouse was a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse a woman?
      `my late spouse's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What was your late spouse's date of birth?
      `the day my late spouse attained or would have attained pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or would) your late spouse reach State Pension age?
      `the day my spouse died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse die?
      `my spouse died while we were married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse die while you were married to each other?
      `my late spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse, at the time of death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004? (answer no if she was not)
      `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your marriage subsist before that certificate was issued? (answer no if there is no certificate)
      `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48B(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` IS
    `s 48B(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the spouse's contributions`
        me spouse
        `the day my spouse died`
        `my spouse died while we were married`
        (JUST (`s 51ZA(3) the case of a woman whose dead spouse changed gender applies` me `my late spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued`))
        (JUST `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        (JUST `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: ss 48B(1) and (1ZA) read the sex and the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant, not the date of birth.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS (IF `I am a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        spouse MEANS
            Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS `my late spouse's date of birth`
                `sex` IS (IF `my late spouse was a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my late spouse attained or would have attained pensionable age`

-- s 48B(1A) and (1B). A person whose civil partner died while they were civil partners of each other is entitled to a
-- Category B retirement pension by virtue of the deceased civil partner's contributions on terms parallel to s 48B(1).
@export Under section 48B(1A), am I, as a surviving civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late civil partner's contributions?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `my late civil partner's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What was your late civil partner's date of birth?
      `the day my late civil partner attained or would have attained pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did (or would) your late civil partner reach State Pension age?
      `the day my civil partner died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your civil partner die?
      `my civil partner died while we were civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your civil partner die while you were civil partners of each other?
      `my late civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your late civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48B(1A), am I, as a surviving civil partner, entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late civil partner's contributions` IS
    `s 48B(1A) the person whose civil partner died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the civil partner's contributions`
        me partner
        `the day my civil partner died`
        `my civil partner died while we were civil partners of each other`
        (JUST `my late civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        (JUST `my late civil partner's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 48B(1A) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        partner MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholder: s 48B(1A) does not read the deceased civil partner's sex.
                `date of birth` IS `my late civil partner's date of birth`
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my late civil partner attained or would have attained pensionable age`

-- s 48B(2). The weekly rate of the Category B pension is the basic pension (as for a Category A pension)
-- plus the additional pension determined as for a Category A pension, halved unless s 48C(3) omits "half of".
-- The basic pension is the section 44(4) rate for a retirement pension (not the lower rate of short-term
-- incapacity benefit), so the seat calls s 44(4) with "no".
@export Under section 48B(2), what is the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension, in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the additional pension, worked out as for a Category A retirement pension, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the weekly rate of the additional pension be, in pounds, if worked out as for a Category A retirement pension (section 45)?
      `the day my spouse died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse die?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 48B(2), what is the weekly rate of my Category B retirement pension` IS
    `s 48B(2) the weekly rate of the Category B retirement pension in pounds`
        (`s 44(4) the weekly rate of the basic pension in pounds` FALSE)
        (JUST `the weekly rate of the additional pension, worked out as for a Category A retirement pension, in pounds`)
        (`s 48C(3) the words "half of" are omitted from section 48B(2)(b)` `the day my spouse died`)

§§ `Section 48BB: Category B pension for someone who was getting a widowed parent's allowance or bereavement allowance`

-- s 48BB(4) and (2). A person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 is entitled to a Category B retirement pension
-- by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner who died if they were entitled to a bereavement
-- allowance before pensionable age, or to a widowed parent's allowance (when over 45 and not still getting it at
-- pensionable age), and have not since married or formed a civil partnership.
@export Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I was entitled to a bereavement allowance before I attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a bereavement allowance (section 39B) at some time before you reached pensionable age?
      `I was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at some time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at some time?
      `I was over 45 at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you over 45 at that time?
      `I was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance immediately before pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a widowed parent's allowance immediately before you reached pensionable age?
      `I have not since married or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since that death, have you stayed unmarried and out of any civil partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 48BB(4), am I entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the contributions of my late spouse or civil partner after getting bereavement allowance or widowed parent's allowance` IS
    `s 48BB(4) the pensioner is entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the contributions of the spouse or civil partner`
        me
        `I was entitled to a bereavement allowance before I attained pensionable age`
        `I was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance at some time`
        (JUST `I was over 45 at that time`)
        `I was entitled to a widowed parent's allowance immediately before pensionable age`
        `I have not since married or formed a civil partnership`
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 48BB(4) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

§§ `Sections 51 and 52: Category B pension for a widow or widower, and the increase to a Category A pension`

-- s 51(1), (2) and 51ZA(4). A person whose spouse died while they were married is entitled to a Category B
-- retirement pension if both attained pensionable age by the death, the person attained it before 6 April 2010,
-- the spouse satisfied the relevant contribution condition, and subsection (2) (a man whose wife died, or a
-- woman whose husband died, as the subsection describes) does not bar the claim.
@export Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `my late spouse was a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse a woman?
      `the day my late spouse attained pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your late spouse reach State Pension age?
      `the day my spouse died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse die?
      `my spouse died while we were married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your spouse die while you were married to each other?
      `my late spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late spouse, at the time of death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004? (answer no if she was not)
      `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your marriage subsist before that certificate was issued? (answer no if there is no certificate)
      `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions for a Category A retirement pension (Schedule 3, Part I)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 51(1), am I, as a widow or widower, entitled to a Category B retirement pension` IS
    `s 51(1) the person whose spouse died is entitled to a Category B retirement pension`
        me spouse
        `the day my spouse died`
        `my spouse died while we were married`
        `my late spouse was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate`
        `the marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued`
        (JUST `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
        (JUST `my late spouse's contributions satisfy the contribution conditions`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholder: s 51(1) reads the sex and the date of attaining pensionable age of the claimant, not the date of birth.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS (IF `I am a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        spouse MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholder: s 51(1) does not read the late spouse's date of birth.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS (IF `my late spouse was a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man)
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day my late spouse attained pensionable age`

-- s 51A(1) to (3). Where, apart from s 43(1), a person would be entitled both to a Category A pension and to a Category B pension on the
-- contributions of the other party to their marriage or civil partnership, and the basic pension in the Category A pension falls short
-- through a deficiency of contributions, it is increased by the lesser of the shortfall and the basic pension in the Category B rate.
-- Subsection (3) disapplies the section where both parties attained pensionable age before 6 April 1979. The full rate is the
-- Schedule 4 Part I paragraph 5 rate, which the person states.
@export Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions, in pounds?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `the day the other party attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse or civil partner reach State Pension age?
      `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category A retirement pension, if section 43(1) (only one pension at a time) did not stop it?
      `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the other party's contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on your spouse's or civil partner's contributions, if section 43(1) did not stop it?
      `my Category A basic pension falls short by a deficiency of contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the basic pension in your Category A retirement pension fall short because your own contributions are deficient?
      `the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly basic pension in your Category A retirement pension, in pounds?
      `the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 5 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 5, in pounds?
      `the basic pension in the rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly basic pension in the rate of your Category B retirement pension, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 51A, by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because of my spouse's or civil partner's contributions` IS
    `s 51A(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds`
        me other
        `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension`
        `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on the other party's contributions`
        `my Category A basic pension falls short by a deficiency of contributions`
        `the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension in pounds`
        (JUST `the weekly rate of a Category B retirement pension under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 5 in pounds`)
        `the basic pension in the rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds`
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: ss 51A(2) and (3) read only the date of attaining pensionable age of each party.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `married`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`
        other MEANS
            Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `married`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day the other party attains pensionable age`

-- s 52(2). A surviving spouse who, apart from s 43(1), would be entitled to both a Category A pension and a
-- Category B pension on the late spouse's contributions, and whose Category A basic pension falls short through a
-- deficiency of contributions, gets the basic pension increased to the amount in the Category B rate
-- (the "full amount" is the section 44(4) rate); subsection (4) disapplies the section for early deaths.
@export Under section 52(2), by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because I am a surviving spouse, in pounds?
GIVEN `the day my spouse died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your spouse die?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category A retirement pension, if section 43(1) (only one pension at a time) did not stop it?
      `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on your late spouse's contributions, if section 43(1) did not stop it?
      `my Category A basic pension falls short by a deficiency of contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the basic pension in your Category A retirement pension fall short because your own contributions are deficient?
      `the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly basic pension in your Category A retirement pension, in pounds?
      `the basic pension in the rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly basic pension in the rate of your Category B retirement pension, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 52(2), by how much is the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension increased because I am a surviving spouse` IS
    `s 52(2) the increase of the basic pension in the Category A retirement pension in pounds`
        `the day my spouse died`
        me
        `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension`
        `apart from section 43(1) I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension on my late spouse's contributions`
        `my Category A basic pension falls short by a deficiency of contributions`
        `the basic pension in my Category A retirement pension in pounds`
        `the basic pension in the rate of my Category B retirement pension in pounds`
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 52(2) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age of the surviving spouse.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

§§ `Section 55: deferment of retirement pension`

-- s 55(3). A person's retirement pension is deferred if they do not become entitled to it only because they have
-- not made the claim section 1 of the Administration Act requires, or because an election under s 54(1) treats
-- them as not having become entitled. (Schedule 5, which then governs, is not among the sources: layer 1 stops here.)
@export Under section 55(3), is my retirement pension deferred?
GIVEN `I do not become entitled only because I have not made a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason you are not yet entitled that you have not claimed (section 1 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992)?
      `I elected under section 54(1) to be treated as not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect, under section 54(1), to be treated as not having become entitled to the pension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 55(3), is my retirement pension deferred` IS
    `s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred`
        (JUST `I do not become entitled only because I have not made a claim`)
        (JUST `I elected under section 54(1) to be treated as not entitled`)

§§ `Sections 55A to 55C: shared additional pension`

-- s 55A(1). A person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and is entitled to an old state scheme
-- pension credit (a pension share on divorce under section 49(1)(b) of the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999)
-- is entitled to a shared additional pension.
@export Under section 55A(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I am entitled to an old state scheme pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an old state scheme pension credit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 55A(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit` IS
    `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` me (JUST `I am entitled to an old state scheme pension credit`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 55A(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 55A(3) to (5). The weekly rate of the shared additional pension is the appropriate weekly amount, revalued by the
-- relevant revaluation percentage where entitlement arose before the final relevant year ends. The appropriate weekly
-- amount and the percentage are fixed outside the sources, so the person states them.
@export Under section 55A(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension, in pounds?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `the day my entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arise?
      `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate weekly amount, in pounds?
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant revaluation percentage, as a percentage? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 55A(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension` IS
    `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds`
        me
        `the day my entitlement to the old state scheme pension credit arose`
        (JUST `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`)
        (JUST `the relevant revaluation percentage`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 55A(3) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 55AA(1) and (3). A person who attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and is entitled to a new state scheme
-- pension credit (section 49A(2)(b) of the 1999 Act) is entitled to a shared additional pension equal to the credit.
@export Under section 55AA(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I am entitled to a new state scheme pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a new state scheme pension credit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 55AA(1), am I entitled to a shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit` IS
    `s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` me (JUST `I am entitled to a new state scheme pension credit`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 55AA(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

@export Under section 55AA(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension, in pounds?
GIVEN `the amount of my new state scheme pension credit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your new state scheme pension credit, in pounds a week?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 55AA(3), what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension` IS
    `s 55AA(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (JUST `the amount of my new state scheme pension credit in pounds`)

-- s 55B(1) to (6). Where the person has become subject to an old state scheme pension debit referable to the shared
-- additional pension, the weekly rate is reduced by the appropriate weekly amount, revalued where the debit came
-- before the final relevant year ends. Both figures are fixed outside the sources, so the person states them.
@export Under section 55B, what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension, in pounds, after a pension debit?
GIVEN `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach State Pension age?
      `I have become subject to an old state scheme pension debit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become subject to an old state scheme pension debit (a pension share on divorce)?
      `the debit is referable to my shared additional pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debit, to any extent, referable to your shared additional pension?
      `the day I became subject to the debit` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become subject to the debit?
      `the weekly rate of my shared additional pension before the reduction in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your shared additional pension before the reduction, in pounds?
      `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate weekly amount, in pounds?
      `the relevant revaluation percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the relevant revaluation percentage, as a percentage? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 55B, what is the weekly rate of my shared additional pension after a pension debit` IS
    `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds`
        me
        `I have become subject to an old state scheme pension debit`
        `the debit is referable to my shared additional pension`
        `the day I became subject to the debit`
        `the weekly rate of my shared additional pension before the reduction in pounds`
        (JUST `the appropriate weekly amount in pounds`)
        (JUST `the relevant revaluation percentage`)
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 55B(1) reads only the date of attaining pensionable age.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I attain pensionable age`

-- s 55C(3). A shared additional pension is deferred if the person would be entitled to a Category A or B
-- retirement pension but for its deferral, and does not become entitled to the shared additional pension only
-- because of the claim requirement. The deferral of the retirement pension is section 55(3)'s answer.
@export Under section 55C(3), is my shared additional pension deferred?
GIVEN `I would be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for its deferral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for the fact that your entitlement is deferred?
      `I do not become entitled to my retirement pension only because I have not made a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason you are not yet entitled to your retirement pension that you have not claimed?
      `I elected under section 54(1) to be treated as not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you elect, under section 54(1), to be treated as not having become entitled to the retirement pension?
      `I do not become entitled to the shared additional pension only because I have not made a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason you are not yet entitled to the shared additional pension that you have not claimed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 55C(3), is my shared additional pension deferred` IS
    `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred`
        `I would be entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension but for its deferral`
        (`s 55(3) the retirement pension is deferred`
            (JUST `I do not become entitled to my retirement pension only because I have not made a claim`)
            (JUST `I elected under section 54(1) to be treated as not entitled`))
        (JUST `I do not become entitled to the shared additional pension only because I have not made a claim`)

§§ `Section 56: child's special allowance`

-- s 56(1), (2), (3), (6). A woman whose marriage ended in divorce, and whose former husband is dead, is entitled to a
-- child's special allowance if she is entitled to child benefit for a child (and was immediately before his death,
-- or the circumstances in the Act's other alternatives hold) and the husband satisfied the contribution condition;
-- it is not payable for a period after she remarries or lives with a man as husband and wife, nor where the
-- subsection (3) cap applies (the child is counted as living with her, or the contributions test is met), subject to
-- the subsection (6) saving for those who qualified immediately before 6 April 1987.
@export Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day?
GIVEN `my marriage has been terminated by divorce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your marriage been ended by divorce?
      `my former husband is dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the husband of that marriage dead?
      `my former husband satisfied the contribution condition for a child's special allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your former husband satisfy the contribution condition for a child's special allowance (Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 6)?
      `I am entitled to child benefit in respect of a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child benefit in respect of a child?
      `I was so entitled immediately before my husband's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you so entitled immediately before your husband's death?
      `in the prescribed circumstances he was then so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the circumstances prescribed by regulations, was he then so entitled to child benefit?
      `he had been contributing at the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your husband, before his death, been contributing at not less than the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child?
      `I was entitled to maintenance for that child under a court order, trust or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the date of your husband's death, were you entitled under a court order, trust or agreement (which you have taken reasonable steps to enforce) to receive payments for that child at not less than that rate?
      `the period is after my remarriage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period you ask about after your remarriage?
      `during the period I live with a man I am not married to as husband and wife` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period you ask about, do you and a man to whom you are not married live together as husband and wife?
      `apart from subsection (3) I am entitled to receive payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the cap in section 56(3), are you entitled to receive payment of the allowance for the child?
      `I would be treated under Part IX as having the child living with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be treated, for the purposes of Part IX, as having the child living with you?
      `the weekly rate of the contributions I make in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of the contributions you make to the child's maintenance, in pounds?
      `I am one of two spouses residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of two spouses residing together?
      `the weekly rate of the contributions the two of us make together in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of the contributions you and your spouse make together, in pounds?
      `the amount referred to in subsection (3) in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount referred to in section 56(3), in pounds a week?
      `this is a prescribed case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is yours a case that regulations prescribe for section 56(5)?
      `the contributions are over and above those needed for section 143(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your contributions over and above those required to satisfy section 143(1)(b)?
      `immediately before 6 April 1987 I satisfied the conditions in section 56(1)(a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before 6 April 1987, did you satisfy conditions (a) to (c) of section 56(1)?
      `immediately before 6 April 1987 I was not barred for either reason in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before 6 April 1987, were you free of both bars in section 56(2) (remarriage; living with a man as husband and wife)?
      `I have so continued since 6 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you continued in that position since 6 April 1987?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to know about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 56(1), is the child's special allowance payable to me for a day` IS
    `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)`
        entitled
        (`s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period`
            `the period is after my remarriage`
            `during the period I live with a man I am not married to as husband and wife`)
        barredBy3
        barredBy6
    WHERE
        me MEANS
            Person WITH
                -- Placeholders: s 56(1) reads only the sex of the woman.
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1950
                `sex` IS Woman
                `marital status` IS `divorced or a former civil partner`
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2010
        entitled MEANS
            `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance`
                me
                `my marriage has been terminated by divorce`
                `my former husband is dead`
                (JUST `my former husband satisfied the contribution condition for a child's special allowance`)
                (JUST `I am entitled to child benefit in respect of a child`)
                (JUST `I was so entitled immediately before my husband's death`)
                (JUST `in the prescribed circumstances he was then so entitled`)
                (JUST `he had been contributing at the prescribed weekly rate to the cost of providing for that child`)
                (JUST `I was entitled to maintenance for that child under a court order, trust or agreement`)
        barredBy3 MEANS
            `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)`
                `apart from subsection (3) I am entitled to receive payment`
                (`s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied`
                    (JUST `I would be treated under Part IX as having the child living with me`)
                    (`s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied`
                        `the weekly rate of the contributions I make in pounds`
                        `I am one of two spouses residing together`
                        `the weekly rate of the contributions the two of us make together in pounds`
                        `the amount referred to in subsection (3) in pounds`
                        (JUST `this is a prescribed case`)
                        (JUST `the contributions are over and above those needed for section 143(1)(b)`)))
        barredBy6 MEANS
            `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)`
                `the day I ask about`
                (JUST `immediately before 6 April 1987 I satisfied the conditions in section 56(1)(a) to (c)`)
                `immediately before 6 April 1987 I was not barred for either reason in subsection (2)`
                `I have so continued since 6 April 1987`

@export Under section 56(1), what is the weekly rate of my child's special allowance, in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of a child's special allowance under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of a child's special allowance under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 56(1), what is the weekly rate of my child's special allowance` IS
    `s 56(1) the weekly rate of the child's special allowance in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of a child's special allowance under Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6 in pounds`)

§§ `Sections 60 to 62: contribution failures, units of additional pension, and gender change`

-- s 60(2) and (3). Where the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied for an employed earner who died of an
-- industrial injury or disease, they are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or
-- surviving civil partner to the benefits subsection (3) names (here, a Category B retirement pension payable
-- under section 48B or 48BB). Subsection (8) applies the rule only to deaths on or after the date it names.
@export Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease?
GIVEN `the employed earner died on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the employed earner (your late spouse or civil partner) die?
      `the employed earner was married or a civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employed earner married or in a civil partnership with you?
      `the injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused by a personal injury of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)?
      `the disease or injury is one mentioned in section 108(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death caused by a disease or injury of a kind mentioned in section 108(1)?
      `the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied for the employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the contribution conditions not wholly satisfied in respect of the employed earner?
      `my pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pension a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB?
      `paragraph 5A of Schedule 3, Part I applies to my pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 5A of Schedule 3, Part I apply to your pension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 60(2), are the contribution conditions taken to be satisfied for my Category B retirement pension, because my spouse or civil partner died of an industrial injury or disease` IS
    `s 60(2) the contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied for the entitlement of the widow, widower or surviving civil partner`
        `the employed earner died on`
        `the employed earner was married or a civil partner`
        (JUST `the injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)`)
        (JUST `the disease or injury is one mentioned in section 108(1)`)
        `the contribution conditions are not wholly satisfied for the employed earner`
        (`s 60(3) the benefit is one of those referred to in subsection (2)`
            `Category B retirement pension`
            `my pension is a Category B retirement pension payable by virtue of section 48B or 48BB`
            `paragraph 5A of Schedule 3, Part I applies to my pension`)

-- s 60A(1) to (3) and (6). If the contribution condition in paragraph 5A of Schedule 3 is not satisfied for a benefit to which
-- that paragraph applies, a person who would have been entitled had it been satisfied is entitled to a prescribed proportion of
-- the benefit for each year of the contributor's working life that satisfies the paragraph's requirements (a) and (b).
-- Subsection (6): the condition includes the condition as modified by paragraph 5A(4). The prescribed proportion is set by
-- regulations, so the person states it, and the number of qualifying years is stated as a count.
@export Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied?
GIVEN `paragraph 5A(4) modifies the condition for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 5A(4) of Schedule 3 modify the contribution condition in your case?
      `the condition as modified is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition, as modified by paragraph 5A(4), satisfied?
      `the condition as unmodified is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition, as it reads without that modification, satisfied?
      `the benefit is one to which paragraph 5A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one to which paragraph 5A of Schedule 3, Part I applies?
      `I would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied?
      `the number of years of the contributor's working life that satisfy paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years of the contributor's working life are the requirements in paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b) satisfied?
      `the prescribed proportion for each such year` IS A NUMBER @desc What proportion of the benefit do the regulations prescribe for each such year? (for example 0.01 for one per cent)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 60A, what proportion of my benefit am I entitled to although the paragraph 5A contribution condition is not satisfied` IS
    `s 60A(2) the proportion of the benefit to which the person is entitled`
        (`s 60A(1) subsection (2) applies`
            (`s 60A(6) the contribution condition in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5A is satisfied for the purposes of subsections (1) to (3)`
                `paragraph 5A(4) modifies the condition for me`
                (JUST `the condition as modified is satisfied`)
                (JUST `the condition as unmodified is satisfied`))
            `the benefit is one to which paragraph 5A applies`)
        (JUST `I would have been entitled to the benefit had the condition been satisfied`)
        `the number of years of the contributor's working life that satisfy paragraph 5A(2)(a) and (b)`
        (JUST `the prescribed proportion for each such year`)

-- s 61ZA(1) and (2). A person with units of additional pension who would be entitled to a Category A retirement
-- pension if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied is taken to satisfy them.
@export Under section 61ZA, are the contribution conditions for my Category A retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my units of additional pension?
GIVEN `the number of units of additional pension I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension do you have?
      `I am entitled to a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category A retirement pension?
      `I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the contribution conditions were satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61ZA, are the contribution conditions for my Category A retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my units of additional pension` IS
    `s 61ZA(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied`
        (`s 61ZA(1) this section applies to the person`
            `the number of units of additional pension I have`
            `I am entitled to a Category A retirement pension`
            (JUST `I would be entitled to a Category A retirement pension if the contribution conditions were satisfied`))

-- s 61ZB(1) and (2). A person whose spouse or civil partner died with units of additional pension, and who would be entitled to a
-- Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied, is taken to satisfy them.
@export Under section 61ZB, are the contribution conditions for my Category B retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension?
GIVEN `the number of units of additional pension my late spouse or civil partner had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many units of additional pension did your late spouse or civil partner have?
      `I am entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death?
      `I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the contribution conditions were satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the relevant contribution conditions were satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61ZB, are the contribution conditions for my Category B retirement pension taken to be satisfied because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension` IS
    `s 61ZB(2) the relevant contribution conditions are taken to be satisfied`
        (`s 61ZB(1) this section applies to the person`
            `the number of units of additional pension my late spouse or civil partner had`
            `I am entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death`
            (JUST `I would be entitled to a Category B retirement pension as a result of the death if the contribution conditions were satisfied`))

-- s 61ZC(1) and (2). Section 43 does not prevent a person from being entitled for the same period to both a Category A pension because of
-- s 61ZA and one Category B pension (subsection (1)), or to a Category A pension and one Category B pension because of s 61ZB (subsection (2)).
-- The questions are asked the way the person puts them ("may I have both ... despite section 43?"), so JUST TRUE means yes, they may;
-- NOTHING means the subsection does not reach the facts and section 43 is not lifted by it.
@export Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43?
GIVEN `I have a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA (units of additional pension)?
      `the number of Category B retirement pensions I have` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Category B retirement pensions do you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61ZC(1), may I have both a Category A retirement pension because of units of additional pension and a Category B retirement pension, despite section 43` IS
    `s 61ZC(1) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` `I have a Category A retirement pension because of section 61ZA` `the number of Category B retirement pensions I have`

@export Under section 61ZC(2), may I have both a Category A retirement pension and a Category B retirement pension because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension, despite section 43?
GIVEN `I have a Category A retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a Category A retirement pension?
      `the number of Category B retirement pensions I have because of section 61ZB` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Category B retirement pensions do you have because of section 61ZB (your late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61ZC(2), may I have both a Category A retirement pension and a Category B retirement pension because of my late spouse's or civil partner's units of additional pension, despite section 43` IS
    `s 61ZC(2) section 43 does not prevent entitlement to both pensions` `I have a Category A retirement pension` `the number of Category B retirement pensions I have because of section 61ZB`

-- s 61A(1) and (2). Where an individual has paid primary Class 1 contributions in error because they were not an employed earner, and
-- prescribed conditions are satisfied, regulations may (if the Inland Revenue think it appropriate) provide for additional pension to be
-- determined as if the contributions had been properly paid.
@export Under section 61A, are the contributions I paid in error treated as properly paid for my additional pension?
GIVEN `I paid primary Class 1 contributions in error because I was not an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay primary Class 1 contributions that, because you were not an employed earner, were paid in error?
      `the prescribed conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions that regulations prescribe satisfied in your case?
      `the Inland Revenue think it appropriate for the regulations to apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the Inland Revenue of the opinion that it is appropriate for the regulations to apply to you?
      `regulations under section 61A(2) so provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 61A(2) provide for your entitlement to additional pension to be determined as if the contributions had been properly paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 61A, are the contributions I paid in error treated as properly paid for my additional pension` IS
    `s 61A(2) the contributions are treated as properly paid, as if the individual had been an employed earner, for the additional pension`
        (`s 61A(1) this section applies in the case of the individual`
            `I paid primary Class 1 contributions in error because I was not an employed earner`
            (JUST `the prescribed conditions are satisfied`))
        `the Inland Revenue think it appropriate for the regulations to apply to me`
        (JUST `regulations under section 61A(2) so provide`)

-- s 62(3) and (4). Where a woman's late wife was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and
-- their marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued, the two are treated in the same way as a woman and
-- her late husband for the purposes of ss 36 and 37 of the National Insurance Act 1965.
@export Under section 62, am I treated like a woman whose husband has died, because my late wife changed gender?
GIVEN `my late wife was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your late wife, at the time of her death, a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004?
      `our marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your marriage to her subsist before that certificate was issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 62, am I treated like a woman whose husband has died, because my late wife changed gender` IS
    `s 62(3) the woman and her late wife are treated in the same way as a woman and her late husband for sections 36 and 37 of the National Insurance Act 1965`
        (`s 62(4) the case is a relevant gender change case`
            `my late wife was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate`
            `our marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc4 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), ss 63-111 (Parts III, IV and V) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great Britain.
-- This layer asks the questions that person would ask about Part III (attendance allowance, carer's allowance, disability living allowance,
-- guardian's allowance, retirement pensions of Categories C and D, age additions), Part IV (increases for dependants) and Part V (industrial injuries
-- benefit: the accident, disablement pension, increases, prescribed diseases). Nothing here is new law: every question calls a rule of the layer-1 modules.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from the Act's own lists), one per fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. A figure the Act leaves to regulations or to Schedule 4 (the table is omitted from the
-- converter rendering this encoding reads) is asked as a number. A prescribed condition is asked as yes or no.
-- A judgment the Act hands to the Secretary of State ("the Secretary of State considers ...") is asked as a fact the person can report from the decision.
-- Records the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question from those answers; a record field that the rule called never reads is given a
-- placeholder, with a comment saying so.
--
-- READING A RESULT. A question answers JUST TRUE (the Act says yes), JUST FALSE (the Act says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the Act does not answer
-- on these facts: it is silent, the list is open, the term is undefined, the answer is in a rule outside this encoding, or the rule is limited by its own wording).
-- NOTHING is never FALSE: do not read it as "no". A question phrased "Am I barred ...?" answers JUST TRUE for barred and JUST FALSE for not barred.
-- Several questions are the Act's separate subsections; the Act's final answer to "may I be paid?" is the combination of the entitlement question and every bar
-- that applies, and this layer does not combine them for the person.
--
-- NOT ASKED ON THEIR OWN: the regulative rule s 65(6)(a) (the claim window; the question about the day answers it), the helper functions (the day count since a Sunday,
-- the month arithmetic, the last day of a run of days: each is reached through the questions that use it), the sums over a list of present disablements in s 109(5) and (6)
-- (the per-disablement tests are asked), s 104(4) (what "modifications" includes in a power to make regulations), the definition rows of s 67(4), (5), (7) and s 72(10),
-- (11), (13) (what counts as a service or an enactment; they bear on the care home rules, not on the person), and every power to make regulations.
-- Officials get no seat. The Secretary of State's judgments enter as facts above.

§ `Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, ss 63 to 111 -- the individual's questions`


§ `Part III -- Non-contributory benefits`


§§ `s 63 -- Descriptions of non-contributory benefits`

@export Under section 63, is this a non-contributory benefit under Part III?
GIVEN `the benefit I am asking about` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63, is this a non-contributory benefit under Part III` IS
    `s 63 the benefit is a non-contributory benefit under Part III` `the benefit I am asking about`

@export Under section 63(f)(i), is a Category C retirement pension payable in my case?
GIVEN `I am a widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a widow?
      `my marriage was ended otherwise than by my husband's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your marriage ended in some way other than by your husband's death?
      `my husband was over pensionable age on 5 July 1948` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your husband over pensionable age on 5 July 1948?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63(f)(i), is a Category C retirement pension payable in my case` IS
    `s 63(f)(i) a Category C retirement pension is payable in the case described` `I am a widow` `my marriage was ended otherwise than by my husband's death` `my husband was over pensionable age on 5 July 1948`

@export Under section 63(f)(ii), is a Category D retirement pension payable to me?
GIVEN `I am over 80` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 80?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63(f)(ii), is a Category D retirement pension payable to me` IS
    `s 63(f)(ii) a Category D retirement pension is payable to the person` (JUST `I am over 80`)

@export Under section 63(g), is an age addition payable in my case?
GIVEN `I am over 80` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 80?
      `it is an increase of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an increase of a retirement pension of a category under this Act?
      `it is an increase of another pension or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an increase of some other pension or allowance from the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 63(g), is an age addition payable in my case` IS
    `s 63(g) an age addition is payable in the case described` (JUST `I am over 80`) `it is an increase of a retirement pension` `it is an increase of another pension or allowance`


§§ `s 64 -- Attendance allowance`

-- s 64(1): the person built here carries placeholders for the fields the rule does not read.
@export Under section 64(1), am I entitled to an attendance allowance?
GIVEN `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you, or will you, reach pensionable age?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking whether you are entitled?
      `I get personal independence payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get personal independence payment?
      `I get adult disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get adult disability payment?
      `I get the care component of disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get the care component of disability living allowance?
      `I get pension age disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get pension age disability payment?
      `I get the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance?
      `I get another allowance of a kind section 64(1A) does not name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you get any other allowance for disability or care that is not one of those above?
      `by day I need attention or supervision from another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you so severely disabled, physically or mentally, that by day you need attention or supervision from another person?
      `by day I need frequent attention with my bodily functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By day, do you need frequent attention throughout the day in connection with your bodily functions?
      `by day I need continual supervision to avoid substantial danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By day, do you need continual supervision throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger to yourself or others?
      `at night I need attention or watching over from another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you so severely disabled, physically or mentally, that at night you need attention or watching over from another person?
      `at night I need prolonged or repeated attention with my bodily functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At night, do you need prolonged or repeated attention in connection with your bodily functions?
      `at night I need someone awake to watch over me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At night, do you need another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals to watch over you in order to avoid substantial danger to yourself or others?
      `I meet the prescribed residence and presence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions about residence and presence in Great Britain that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 64(1), am I entitled to an attendance allowance` IS
    `s 64(1) the person is entitled to an attendance allowance` `me` `the day I am asking about` `my allowances` `my day facts` `my night facts` (JUST `I meet the prescribed residence and presence conditions`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900    -- placeholder: section 64(1) does not read it
                `sex` IS Woman    -- placeholder: section 64(1) does not read it
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`    -- placeholder: section 64(1) does not read it
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`
        `my allowances` MEANS concat (LIST (IF `I get personal independence payment` THEN LIST `s 64(1A)(a) personal independence payment` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I get adult disability payment` THEN LIST `s 64(1A)(aa) adult disability payment` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I get the care component of disability living allowance` THEN LIST `s 64(1A)(b) the care component of a disability living allowance` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I get pension age disability payment` THEN LIST `s 64(1A)(c) pension age disability payment` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I get the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance` THEN LIST `s 64(1A)(d) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I get another allowance of a kind section 64(1A) does not name` THEN LIST `s 64(1A) another allowance` ELSE EMPTY))
        `my day facts` MEANS `s 64(2) Day attendance facts` OF `by day I need attention or supervision from another person`, `by day I need frequent attention with my bodily functions`, `by day I need continual supervision to avoid substantial danger`
        `my night facts` MEANS `s 64(3) Night attendance facts` OF `at night I need attention or watching over from another person`, `at night I need prolonged or repeated attention with my bodily functions`, `at night I need someone awake to watch over me`


§§ `s 65 -- Provisions supplementary to section 64`

@export Under section 65(1), is this period one for which I am entitled to an attendance allowance?
GIVEN `the first day of the period I ask about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period you are asking about?
      `the last day of the period I ask about` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period?
      `throughout that period I meet or am likely to meet the day or night condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Throughout that period do you, or are you likely to, meet the day or the night attendance condition, or both?
      `the first day of my preceding period` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your preceding period of entitlement?
      `the last day of my preceding period` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your preceding period of entitlement?
      `throughout the preceding period I met or was likely to meet one or both conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Throughout the preceding period did you, or were you likely to, meet one or both of those conditions?
      `the prescribed time in days` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days of the start of this period must the preceding period have ended, under the regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(1), is this period one for which I am entitled to an attendance allowance` IS
    `s 65(1) the period is one for which the person is entitled to an attendance allowance` `this period` `throughout that period I meet or am likely to meet the day or night condition` `my preceding period` `throughout the preceding period I met or was likely to meet one or both conditions` (JUST `the prescribed time in days`)
    WHERE
        `this period` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of the period I ask about`, `the last day` IS `the last day of the period I ask about`
        `my preceding period` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of my preceding period`, `the last day` IS `the last day of my preceding period`

@export Under section 65(2), am I deemed to meet the attendance conditions because of renal failure?
GIVEN `I suffer from renal failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from renal failure?
      `I am undergoing a prescribed form of treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing a form of treatment that the regulations prescribe?
      `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(2), am I deemed to meet the attendance conditions because of renal failure` IS
    `s 65(2) the person is deemed to satisfy or to be likely to satisfy the day or the night attendance condition or both` `I suffer from renal failure` (JUST `I am undergoing a prescribed form of treatment`) (JUST `the circumstances are those prescribed`)

@export Under section 65(3), what is my weekly rate of attendance allowance in pounds?
GIVEN `I meet both conditions for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the period, do you meet or are you likely to meet both the day and the night attendance conditions?
      `I meet both conditions for the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the 6 months mentioned in section 65(1)(b), do you meet or are you likely to meet both conditions?
      `the higher weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the higher weekly rate of attendance allowance in Schedule 4, in pounds?
      `the lower weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower weekly rate of attendance allowance in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 65(3), what is my weekly rate of attendance allowance in pounds` IS
    `s 65(3) the weekly rate of the attendance allowance in pounds` `I meet both conditions for the period` `I meet both conditions for the 6 months` (JUST `the higher weekly rate in pounds`) (JUST `the lower weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 65(4), am I barred from attendance allowance for a day before my claim?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the day I made, or am treated as making, my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim, or the date you are treated as making it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(4), am I barred from attendance allowance for a day before my claim` IS
    `s 65(4) the person is barred from an attendance allowance for the day by the date of claim` `the day I ask about` `the day I made, or am treated as making, my claim`

@export Under section 65(6)(a), may I make my claim on this day?
GIVEN `the first day of my entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period for which you would be entitled?
      `the day I make my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you making the claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(6)(a), may I make my claim on this day` IS
    `s 65(6)(a) the claim may be made on the day` `the first day of my entitlement` `the day I make my claim`

@export Under section 65(6)(b), is the condition on my advance award met?
GIVEN `throughout the 6 months I meet both conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Throughout the 6 months, do you meet both the day and the night attendance conditions?
      `my award is at the lower rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your award at the lower rate?
      `throughout the 6 months I meet one condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Throughout the 6 months, do you meet one of those conditions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(6)(b), is the condition on my advance award met` IS
    `s 65(6)(b) the condition on an award made on a claim made in advance is satisfied` `throughout the 6 months I meet both conditions` `my award is at the lower rate` `throughout the 6 months I meet one condition`

@export Under section 65(7), am I barred from attendance allowance by the EC Regulations?
GIVEN `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 apply to you?
      `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, is the United Kingdom the state competent to pay your sickness benefits in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 65(7), am I barred from attendance allowance by the EC Regulations` IS
    `s 65(7) the person is barred from an attendance allowance for the period by the Regulations` `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash`


§§ `s 66 -- Attendance allowance for persons who are terminally ill`

@export Under section 66(1)(a)(i), am I taken to meet the attendance conditions on a day because I am terminally ill?
GIVEN `I claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
      `I am terminally ill on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill on the day you ask about?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(1)(a)(i), am I taken to meet the attendance conditions on a day because I am terminally ill` IS
    `s 66(1)(a)(i) the person is taken to satisfy both the day attendance condition and the night attendance condition on the day` `I claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` `I am terminally ill on the day` `the day I ask about` `the date of my claim`

@export Under section 66(1)(a)(ii), from what day am I taken to have met the conditions?
GIVEN `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
      `the first date on which I was terminally ill` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date on which you were terminally ill?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 66(1)(a)(ii), from what day am I taken to have met the conditions` IS
    `s 66(1)(a)(ii) the first day of the period for which the person is taken to have satisfied the conditions` `the date of my claim` `the first date on which I was terminally ill`

@export Under section 66(1)(b), is this day in the period for which I get attendance allowance as a terminally ill person?
GIVEN `I claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
      `I am terminally ill on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill on the day you ask about?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(1)(b), is this day in the period for which I get attendance allowance as a terminally ill person` IS
    `s 66(1)(b) the day is in the period for which the person is entitled to attendance allowance` `I claim expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` `I am terminally ill on the day` `the day I ask about` `the date of my claim`

@export Under section 66(2)(a), am I terminally ill?
GIVEN `I suffer from a progressive disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer from a progressive disease?
      `my death in consequence can reasonably be expected within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your death in consequence of that disease reasonably be expected within 12 months?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(2)(a), am I terminally ill` IS
    `s 66(2)(a) the person is terminally ill at the time` `I suffer from a progressive disease` `my death in consequence can reasonably be expected within 12 months`

@export Under section 66(2)(b), am I regarded as making a claim made for me on the ground that I am terminally ill?
GIVEN `a person purports to claim for me under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person purport to make a claim for an attendance allowance by virtue of subsection (1) on your behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 66(2)(b), am I regarded as making a claim made for me on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS
    `s 66(2)(b) the other person is regarded as making the claim` `a person purports to claim for me under subsection (1)`


§§ `s 67 -- Attendance allowance: care homes`

@export Under section 67(3), is this place a care home?
GIVEN `it provides accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the establishment provide accommodation?
      `it provides nursing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide nursing?
      `it provides personal care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide personal care?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 67(3), is this place a care home` IS
    `s 67(3) the establishment is a care home` `it provides accommodation` `it provides nursing` `it provides personal care`


§§ `s 70 -- Carer's allowance`

@export Under section 70(1), am I entitled to a carer's allowance for a day?
GIVEN `I am engaged in caring for a severely disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day, are you engaged in caring for a severely disabled person?
      `I am regularly and substantially engaged in caring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you regularly and substantially engaged in caring for that person?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed?
      `the person I care for is a relative of a prescribed kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you care for a relative of yours, or a person of another description, that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(1), am I entitled to a carer's allowance for a day` IS
    `s 70(1) the person is entitled to a carer's allowance for the day` `I am engaged in caring for a severely disabled person` `I am regularly and substantially engaged in caring` `I am gainfully employed` (JUST `the person I care for is a relative of a prescribed kind`)

@export Under section 70(1A), do I stay entitled to a carer's allowance after the death of the person I care for?
GIVEN `I was entitled just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a carer's allowance immediately before the death of the person you cared for?
      `the date of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that person die?
      `I have stopped meeting another requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped meeting any other requirement for entitlement?
      `the day I stopped meeting it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first stop meeting it? (Ignored if you have not stopped.)
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(1A), do I stay entitled to a carer's allowance after the death of the person I care for` IS
    `s 70(1A) the person continues to be entitled to a carer's allowance for the day` `I was entitled just before the death` `the date of the death` `the day I stopped, if I have` `the day I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the day I stopped, if I have` MEANS IF `I have stopped meeting another requirement` THEN JUST `the day I stopped meeting it` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 70(2), is the person I care for a severely disabled person?
GIVEN `the payment the person I care for receives` IS A `s 70(2) Payment in respect of the person cared for` @desc Which payment does the person you care for receive?
      `it is a payment prescribed as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment one the regulations prescribe as such a payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(2), is the person I care for a severely disabled person` IS
    `s 70(2) the person cared for is a severely disabled person` `the payment the person I care for receives` (JUST `it is a payment prescribed as such`)

@export Under section 70(3), am I barred from a carer's allowance by age or education?
GIVEN `I am under 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 16?
      `I am in full-time education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving full-time education?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(3), am I barred from a carer's allowance by age or education` IS
    `s 70(3) the person is barred from a carer's allowance by age or education` (JUST `I am under 16`) `I am in full-time education`

@export Under section 70(4), am I barred from a carer's allowance by the residence and presence conditions?
GIVEN `I meet the prescribed residence or presence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions about residence or presence in Great Britain that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(4), am I barred from a carer's allowance by the residence and presence conditions` IS
    `s 70(4) the person is barred from a carer's allowance by the residence and presence conditions` (JUST `I meet the prescribed residence or presence conditions`)

@export Under section 70(4A), am I barred from a carer's allowance by the EC Regulations?
GIVEN `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 apply to you?
      `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, is the United Kingdom the state competent to pay your sickness benefits in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(4A), am I barred from a carer's allowance by the EC Regulations` IS
    `s 70(4A) the person is barred from a carer's allowance for the period by the Regulations` `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash`

@export Under section 70(7), am I barred from a further carer's allowance for a day?
GIVEN `the number of carer's allowances I would be entitled to for the day` IS A NUMBER @desc For that day, how many carer's allowances would you be entitled to?
      `I would be entitled to carer support payment for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that day, would you be entitled to carer support payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7), am I barred from a further carer's allowance for a day` IS
    `s 70(7) the person is barred from a further allowance for the day` `the number of carer's allowances I would be entitled to for the day` `I would be entitled to carer support payment for the day`

@export Under section 70(7ZA), am I the person who has the relevant entitlement for a day?
GIVEN `the number of people with a relevant entitlement in respect of the same person` IS A NUMBER @desc For that day, how many people would have a relevant entitlement in respect of the same severely disabled person?
      `we jointly elected me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did those people jointly elect you, in the prescribed manner?
      `the Secretary of State determined it should be me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State determine that you should have the entitlement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7ZA), am I the person who has the relevant entitlement for a day` IS
    `s 70(7ZA) the person is the one who has the relevant entitlement for the day` `the number of people with a relevant entitlement in respect of the same person` (JUST `we jointly elected me`) (JUST `the Secretary of State determined it should be me`)

@export Under section 70(7ZB), does subsection (7ZC) apply to me?
GIVEN `A has or would have an entitlement to carer support payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A have, or would A have, an entitlement to carer support payment (disregarding regulation 5(3))?
      `A has or would have a carer's allowance entitlement the Scottish Ministers decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A have, or would A have, an entitlement to carer's allowance in respect of which the Scottish Ministers have the power to make decisions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7ZB), does subsection (7ZC) apply to me` IS
    `s 70(7ZB) subsection (7ZC) applies` `A has or would have an entitlement to carer support payment` `A has or would have a carer's allowance entitlement the Scottish Ministers decide`

@export Under section 70(7ZC), am I, as the other person B, barred from a relevant entitlement for a day?
GIVEN `subsection (7ZC) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection (7ZC) apply?
      `A and B jointly elect that B shall have the entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do A and B jointly elect, in the prescribed manner, that B shall have the relevant entitlement?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the Scottish Ministers have decided that B shall` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In default of an election, is the Secretary of State satisfied, after consulting the Scottish Ministers, that they have decided or will decide that A shall not have the entitlement and that B shall?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7ZC), am I, as the other person B, barred from a relevant entitlement for a day` IS
    `s 70(7ZC) the other person B is barred from a relevant entitlement for the day` (JUST `subsection (7ZC) applies`) `A and B jointly elect that B shall have the entitlement` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the Scottish Ministers have decided that B shall`

@export Under section 70(7A), do I have a relevant entitlement?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a carer's allowance decided by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a carer's allowance in respect of which the Secretary of State has the power to make decisions?
      `I am entitled to the universal credit carer element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled under section 12 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 to the inclusion in an award of universal credit of an amount for regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7A), do I have a relevant entitlement` IS
    `s 70(7A) the person has a relevant entitlement` `I am entitled to a carer's allowance decided by the Secretary of State` `I am entitled to the universal credit carer element`

@export Under section 70(7B), is my payment a carer support payment?
GIVEN `it is the carer support payment component of carer's assistance given in accordance with the 2023 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment the carer support payment component of carer's assistance, given in accordance with the Carer's Assistance (Carer Support Payment) (Scotland) Regulations 2023?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 70(7B), is my payment a carer support payment` IS
    `s 70(7B) the payment is carer support payment` `it is the carer support payment component of carer's assistance given in accordance with the 2023 Regulations`

@export Under section 70(9), what is my weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of carer's allowance in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 70(9), what is my weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds` IS
    `s 70(9) the weekly rate of a carer's allowance in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of carer's allowance in pounds`)


§§ `ss 71 to 76 -- Disability living allowance`

@export Under section 71(1), is this a component of disability living allowance?
GIVEN `the component I am asking about` IS A `s 71(1) Component` @desc Which component are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(1), is this a component of disability living allowance` IS
    `s 71(1) the component is part of disability living allowance` `the component I am asking about`

@export Under section 71(2), is my disability living allowance an entitlement to the components?
GIVEN `I am entitled to the care component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the care component?
      `I am entitled to the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the mobility component?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(2), is my disability living allowance an entitlement to the components` IS
    `s 71(2) the person's entitlement to disability living allowance is an entitlement to the components` `I am entitled to the care component` `I am entitled to the mobility component`

@export Under section 71(3), are the terms of my disability living allowance award permitted?
GIVEN `my care component is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a care component awarded to you?
      `my care component award is for a fixed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your care component award for a fixed period?
      `the last day of my care component award` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your care component award end? (Ignored if it is not for a fixed period.)
      `my mobility component is awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a mobility component awarded to you?
      `my mobility component award is for a fixed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your mobility component award for a fixed period?
      `the last day of my mobility component award` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your mobility component award end? (Ignored if it is not for a fixed period.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(3), are the terms of my disability living allowance award permitted` IS
    `s 71(3) the terms of the award are permitted` `my care component is awarded` `my care term` `my mobility component is awarded` `my mobility term`
    WHERE
        `my care term` MEANS IF `my care component award is for a fixed period` THEN `s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` `the last day of my care component award` ELSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period`
        `my mobility term` MEANS IF `my mobility component award is for a fixed period` THEN `s 71(3) a fixed period ending on a date` `the last day of my mobility component award` ELSE `s 71(3) an indefinite period`

@export Under section 71(4), what is my weekly rate of disability living allowance for a week with one component, in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate for that component in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of that component in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 71(4), what is my weekly rate of disability living allowance for a week with one component, in pounds` IS
    `s 71(4) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with one component in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate for that component in pounds`)

@export Under section 71(5), what is my weekly rate of disability living allowance for a week with both components, in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your care component, in pounds?
      `the weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of your mobility component, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 71(5), what is my weekly rate of disability living allowance for a week with both components, in pounds` IS
    `s 71(5) the weekly rate of the disability living allowance for a week with both components in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of the care component in pounds`) (JUST `the weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds`)

@export Under section 71(6), am I barred from disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions?
GIVEN `I meet the prescribed residence and presence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions about residence and presence in Great Britain that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(6), am I barred from disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` IS
    `s 71(6) the person is barred from a disability living allowance by the residence and presence conditions` (JUST `I meet the prescribed residence and presence conditions`)

@export Under section 71(7), am I barred from disability living allowance while I am entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment?
GIVEN `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to pension age disability payment?
      `I am entitled to adult disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to adult disability payment?
      `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance?
      `I am entitled to child disability payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child disability payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 71(7), am I barred from disability living allowance while I am entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` IS
    `s 71(7) the person is barred from a disability living allowance while entitled to a Scottish or pension age payment` `I am entitled to pension age disability payment` `I am entitled to adult disability payment` `I am entitled to Scottish adult disability living allowance` `I am entitled to child disability payment`

@export Under section 72(1), am I entitled to the care component of disability living allowance for the period?
GIVEN `I need attention with my bodily functions for a significant portion of the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you need, in connection with your bodily functions, attention from another person for a significant portion of the day?
      `I cannot prepare a cooked main meal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you not prepare a cooked main meal for yourself if you have the ingredients?
      `by day I need frequent attention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By day, do you need frequent attention from another person throughout the day in connection with your bodily functions?
      `by day I need continual supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By day, do you need continual supervision from another person throughout the day in order to avoid substantial danger?
      `at night I need prolonged or repeated attention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At night, do you need prolonged or repeated attention from another person in connection with your bodily functions?
      `at night I need someone awake to watch over me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At night, do you need another person to be awake for a prolonged period or at frequent intervals to watch over you in order to avoid substantial danger?
      `I am under 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 16?
      `I have requirements substantially in excess of the normal requirements of my age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have requirements of that description substantially in excess of the normal requirements of persons of your age?
      `I have substantial requirements that younger people may also have` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have substantial requirements of that description which younger persons in normal health may also have but which persons of your age in normal health would not have?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(1), am I entitled to the care component of disability living allowance for the period` IS
    `s 72(1) the person is entitled to the care component for the period` `my facts` (JUST `I am under 16`) `I have requirements substantially in excess of the normal requirements of my age` `I have substantial requirements that younger people may also have`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 72(1) Care component facts` OF `I need attention with my bodily functions for a significant portion of the day`, `I cannot prepare a cooked main meal`, `by day I need frequent attention`, `by day I need continual supervision`, `at night I need prolonged or repeated attention`, `at night I need someone awake to watch over me`

-- s 72(2): the 3 month requirement is met when the run began on or before the day 3 months before the award; a prescribed other period (none here) can also meet it.
@export Under section 72(2), am I barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements?
GIVEN `the date my award would begin` IS A DATE @desc On what date would your award of the care component begin?
      `the first day of my unbroken run of meeting a condition` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the unbroken run in which you have met, or are likely to meet, one or other of the conditions?
      `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that run, that is, the last day on which you are likely to continue to meet one or other of the conditions?
      `my death is expected before the run ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your death expected before the run ends?
      `the day my death is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your death expected? (Ignored if it is not expected.)
      `I met a condition throughout another prescribed period of 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you meet one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as is prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(2), am I barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` IS
    `s 72(2) the person is barred from the care component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` `the date my award would begin` `the first day of my unbroken run of meeting a condition` `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` `my expected death` (JUST `I met a condition throughout another prescribed period of 3 months`)
    WHERE
        `my expected death` MEANS IF `my death is expected before the run ends` THEN JUST `the day my death is expected` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 72(2A), do the under-16 modifications apply to my care component on a day?
GIVEN `I am under 16 on the date my award would begin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 16 on the date on which the award of the care component would begin?
      `the day falls before I reach 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day you ask about fall before the day you reach 16?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(2A), do the under-16 modifications apply to my care component on a day` IS
    `s 72(2A) the modifications in subsection (1A) have effect for subsection (2) on the day` (JUST `I am under 16 on the date my award would begin`) (JUST `the day falls before I reach 16`)

@export Under section 72(4), what is my weekly rate of the care component in pounds?
GIVEN `I meet both conditions throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet or are you likely to meet both the conditions in section 72(1)(b) and (c) throughout both periods?
      `I meet one or other condition throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet or are you likely to meet one or other of those conditions throughout both periods?
      `the highest weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the highest weekly rate of the care component, in pounds?
      `the middle weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the middle weekly rate of the care component, in pounds?
      `the lowest weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lowest weekly rate of the care component, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 72(4), what is my weekly rate of the care component in pounds` IS
    `s 72(4) the weekly rate of the care component in pounds` `I meet both conditions throughout both periods` `I meet one or other condition throughout both periods` (JUST `the highest weekly rate in pounds`) (JUST `the middle weekly rate in pounds`) (JUST `the lowest weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 72(5)(a), from what day am I taken to have met the care component conditions?
GIVEN `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
      `the first date on which I was terminally ill` IS A DATE @desc What was the first date on which you were terminally ill?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 72(5)(a), from what day am I taken to have met the care component conditions` IS
    `s 72(5)(a) the first day of the period for which the person is taken to have satisfied the conditions` `the date of my claim` `the first date on which I was terminally ill`

@export Under section 72(5)(b), am I taken to meet the care component conditions on this day because I am terminally ill?
GIVEN `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill, as section 66(2) defines it, and claiming expressly on that ground?
      `I am terminally ill on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill on the day you ask about?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(5)(b), am I taken to meet the care component conditions on this day because I am terminally ill` IS
    `s 72(5)(b) the person is taken to satisfy or to be likely to satisfy the conditions on the day` `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` `I am terminally ill on the day` `the day I ask about` `the date of my claim`

@export Under section 72(7B), am I barred from the care component by the EC Regulations?
GIVEN `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or Regulation (EC) No 883/2004 apply to you?
      `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period, is the United Kingdom the state competent to pay your sickness benefits in cash?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(7B), am I barred from the care component by the EC Regulations` IS
    `s 72(7B) the person is barred from the care component for the period by the Regulations` `Regulation (EC) No 1408/71 or No 883/2004 applies to me` `the United Kingdom is competent to pay my sickness benefits in cash`

@export Under section 72(9), is this place a care home?
GIVEN `it provides accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the establishment provide accommodation?
      `it provides nursing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide nursing?
      `it provides personal care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide personal care?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 72(9), is this place a care home` IS
    `s 72(9) the establishment is a care home` `it provides accommodation` `it provides nursing` `it provides personal care`

@export Under section 73(1), am I entitled to the mobility component of disability living allowance for the period?
GIVEN `I am unable, or virtually unable, to walk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you suffering from physical disablement such that you are unable to walk or virtually unable to do so?
      `I fall within section 73(1AB)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within subsection (1AB), that is, have such severe visual impairment as the regulations prescribe and satisfy such other conditions as they prescribe?
      `I fall within section 73(2) but not (1AB)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you both blind and deaf (and satisfy such other conditions as the regulations prescribe), so that you fall within subsection (2) but not (1AB)?
      `I fall within section 73(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within subsection (3), that is, are you severely mentally impaired or displaying severe behavioural problems and satisfy the conditions in section 72(1)(b) and (c)?
      `I can walk but need guidance or supervision most of the time out of doors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you walk, but are so severely disabled physically or mentally that, disregarding routes familiar to you on your own, you cannot take advantage of the faculty out of doors without guidance or supervision from another person most of the time?
      `I am over 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 3?
      `I am over 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 5?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(1), am I entitled to the mobility component of disability living allowance for the period` IS
    `s 73(1) the person is entitled to the mobility component for the period` `my facts` (JUST `I am over 3`) (JUST `I am over 5`)
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 73(1) Mobility component facts` OF `I am unable, or virtually unable, to walk`, `I fall within section 73(1AB)`, `I fall within section 73(2) but not (1AB)`, `I fall within section 73(3)`, `I can walk but need guidance or supervision most of the time out of doors`

@export Under section 73(1A), from what age can I qualify for the mobility component under the condition that applies to me?
GIVEN `the condition that applies to me` IS A `s 73(1) Condition` @desc Which of the five conditions in section 73(1) applies to you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 73(1A), from what age can I qualify for the mobility component under the condition that applies to me` IS
    `s 73(1A) the relevant age in years for the condition` `the condition that applies to me`

@export Under section 73(1AB), do I fall within the severe visual impairment subsection?
GIVEN `I have such severe visual impairment as is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have such severe visual impairment as the regulations prescribe?
      `I satisfy such other conditions as are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy such other conditions as the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(1AB), do I fall within the severe visual impairment subsection` IS
    `s 73(1AB) the person falls within this subsection` (JUST `I have such severe visual impairment as is prescribed`) (JUST `I satisfy such other conditions as are prescribed`)

@export Under section 73(2), am I both blind and deaf within the mobility rules?
GIVEN `I am both blind and deaf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you both blind and deaf?
      `I satisfy such other conditions as are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy such other conditions as the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(2), am I both blind and deaf within the mobility rules` IS
    `s 73(2) the person falls within this subsection` `I am both blind and deaf` (JUST `I satisfy such other conditions as are prescribed`)

@export Under section 73(3), am I severely mentally impaired or behaviourally disturbed within the mobility rules?
GIVEN `I am severely mentally impaired, in a case regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you severely mentally impaired, in a case that the regulations specify under subsection (6)?
      `I display severe behavioural problems, in a case regulations specify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you display severe behavioural problems, in a case that the regulations specify under subsection (6)?
      `I satisfy the conditions in section 72(1)(b) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy both the condition in section 72(1)(b) and the condition in section 72(1)(c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(3), am I severely mentally impaired or behaviourally disturbed within the mobility rules` IS
    `s 73(3) the person falls within this subsection` (JUST `I am severely mentally impaired, in a case regulations specify`) (JUST `I display severe behavioural problems, in a case regulations specify`) `I satisfy the conditions in section 72(1)(b) and (c)`

@export Under section 73(4A), am I taken to meet the guidance condition before I reach 16?
GIVEN `I am under 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 16?
      `the condition in paragraph (d) is met apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition in paragraph (d) met apart from this subsection?
      `I need substantially more guidance or supervision than others of my age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you require substantially more guidance or supervision from another person than persons of your age in normal physical and mental health would require?
      `others of my age would not need such guidance or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would persons of your age in normal physical and mental health not require such guidance or supervision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(4A), am I taken to meet the guidance condition before I reach 16` IS
    `s 73(4A) the condition in subsection (1)(d) is taken to be satisfied for the part of a period before he reaches 16` (JUST `I am under 16`) `the condition in paragraph (d) is met apart from this subsection` `I need substantially more guidance or supervision than others of my age` `others of my age would not need such guidance or supervision`

@export Under section 73(7), am I taken to meet the condition for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)?
GIVEN `I am taken for section 72 to satisfy the condition in section 72(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taken, for the purposes of section 72, to satisfy the condition in section 72(1)(b) or (c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(7), am I taken to meet the condition for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)` IS
    `s 73(7) the person is taken to satisfy the condition for the purposes of subsection (3)(c)` (JUST `I am taken for section 72 to satisfy the condition in section 72(1)(b) or (c)`)

@export Under section 73(8), am I barred from the mobility component by my condition?
GIVEN `during most of the period my condition will let me benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During most of the period, will your condition be such that it permits you from time to time to benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(8), am I barred from the mobility component by my condition` IS
    `s 73(8) the person is barred from the mobility component for the period by his condition` `during most of the period my condition will let me benefit from enhanced facilities for locomotion`

@export Under section 73(9), am I barred from the mobility component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements?
GIVEN `the date my award would begin` IS A DATE @desc On what date would your award of the mobility component begin?
      `the first day of my unbroken run of meeting a condition` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the unbroken run in which you have met, or are likely to meet, one or other of the conditions?
      `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that run?
      `my death is expected before the run ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your death expected before the run ends?
      `the day my death is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your death expected? (Ignored if it is not expected.)
      `I met a condition throughout another prescribed period of 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you meet one or other of the conditions throughout such other period of 3 months as is prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(9), am I barred from the mobility component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` IS
    `s 73(9) the person is barred from the mobility component by the 3 month and 6 month requirements` `the date my award would begin` `the first day of my unbroken run of meeting a condition` `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` `my expected death` (JUST `I met a condition throughout another prescribed period of 3 months`)
    WHERE
        `my expected death` MEANS IF `my death is expected before the run ends` THEN JUST `the day my death is expected` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 73(9A), do the under-16 modifications apply to my mobility component on a day?
GIVEN `I am under 16 on the date my award would begin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you under 16 on the date on which the award of the mobility component would begin?
      `the day falls before I reach 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day you ask about fall before the day you reach 16?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(9A), do the under-16 modifications apply to my mobility component on a day` IS
    `s 73(9A) the modifications in subsection (4A) have effect for subsection (9) on the day` (JUST `I am under 16 on the date my award would begin`) (JUST `the day falls before I reach 16`)

@export Under section 73(11), what is my weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds?
GIVEN `I meet one or other of the conditions throughout both periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet or are you likely to meet one or other of the conditions in section 73(1)(a), (ab), (b) and (c) throughout both periods?
      `the higher weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the higher weekly rate of the mobility component, in pounds?
      `the lower weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower weekly rate of the mobility component, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 73(11), what is my weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` IS
    `s 73(11) the weekly rate of the mobility component in pounds` `I meet one or other of the conditions throughout both periods` (JUST `the higher weekly rate in pounds`) (JUST `the lower weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 73(12)(a), am I, as a terminally ill person, barred from the mobility component by the 6 month requirement alone?
GIVEN `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill, as section 66(2) defines it, and claiming expressly on that ground?
      `the date my award would begin` IS A DATE @desc On what date would your award of the mobility component begin?
      `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which you are likely to continue to meet one or other of the conditions?
      `my death is expected before then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your death expected within the 6 months?
      `the day my death is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your death expected? (Ignored if it is not expected.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(12)(a), am I, as a terminally ill person, barred from the mobility component by the 6 month requirement alone` IS
    `s 73(12)(a) the person is barred from the mobility component by the 6 month requirement alone` `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` `the date my award would begin` `the last day I am likely to go on meeting a condition` `my expected death`
    WHERE
        `my expected death` MEANS IF `my death is expected before then` THEN JUST `the day my death is expected` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under section 73(12)(b), what is my weekly rate of the mobility component as a terminally ill person in pounds?
GIVEN `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you terminally ill, as section 66(2) defines it, and claiming expressly on that ground?
      `I meet one or other condition throughout the period in subsection (9)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet, or are you likely to meet, one or other of the conditions throughout the period mentioned in subsection (9)(b)?
      `the higher weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the higher weekly rate of the mobility component, in pounds?
      `the lower weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower weekly rate of the mobility component, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 73(12)(b), what is my weekly rate of the mobility component as a terminally ill person in pounds` IS
    `s 73(12)(b) the weekly rate of the mobility component of a terminally ill person in pounds` `I am terminally ill and claim on that ground` `I meet one or other condition throughout the period in subsection (9)(b)` (JUST `the higher weekly rate in pounds`) (JUST `the lower weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 73(14), is my mobility payment disregarded when means are counted?
GIVEN `the payment is attributable to my entitlement to the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment, or your right to receive it, attributable to your entitlement to the mobility component?
      `the case is within a prescribed exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the case fall within the circumstances and purposes the regulations prescribe as exceptions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 73(14), is my mobility payment disregarded when means are counted` IS
    `s 73(14) the payment is disregarded in applying an enactment under which regard is to be had to a person's means` `the payment is attributable to my entitlement to the mobility component` (JUST `the case is within a prescribed exception`)

@export Under section 74(1), am I deemed to meet the mobility condition in section 73(1)(a)?
GIVEN `a certificate in respect of me is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate in respect of you in force?
      `section 74 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 74 apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(1), am I deemed to meet the mobility condition in section 73(1)(a)` IS
    `s 74(1) the person is deemed for the purposes of section 73 to satisfy the condition mentioned in subsection (1)(a) of that section` `a certificate in respect of me is in force` (JUST `section 74 applies to me`)

@export Under section 74(2), does section 74 apply to me?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State considers I held an invalid carriage or vehicle on 1 January 1976` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that on 1 January 1976 you had an invalid carriage or other vehicle provided under section 33 of the Health Services and Public Health Act 1968, or were receiving payments under subsection (3) of that section?
      `the Secretary of State considers I had made an approved application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that you had at that date, or a later date the Secretary of State specified, made an application which was approved for such a carriage, vehicle or payments?
      `the Secretary of State considers I held one both before and after that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that you were, both at some time in a prescribed period before that date and at some time in a prescribed period after it, in possession of such a carriage or vehicle or receiving such payments?
      `the Secretary of State considers an error or delay was not my fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider that you would have qualified under the preceding paragraphs but for an error or delay for which you were not responsible and which was brought to the Secretary of State's attention within one year beginning with 30 March 1977?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 74(2), does section 74 apply to me` IS
    `s 74(2) this section applies to the person` `the Secretary of State considers I held an invalid carriage or vehicle on 1 January 1976` `the Secretary of State considers I had made an approved application` `the Secretary of State considers I held one both before and after that date` `the Secretary of State considers an error or delay was not my fault`

@export Under section 75(1), am I barred from disability living allowance for a day after I reach pensionable age?
GIVEN `the day I reach pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you, or will you, reach pensionable age?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the date of my award` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your award made?
      `the regulations provide otherwise for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations provide otherwise for a person in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 75(1), am I barred from disability living allowance for a day after I reach pensionable age` IS
    `s 75(1) the person is barred from a component of disability living allowance for the day after pensionable age` `me` `the day I ask about` `the date of my award` (JUST `the regulations provide otherwise for me`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900    -- placeholder: section 75(1) does not read it
                `sex` IS Woman    -- placeholder: section 75(1) does not read it
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`    -- placeholder: section 75(1) does not read it
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I reach pensionable age`

@export Under section 76(1), am I barred from disability living allowance for a day before my claim?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the day I made, or am treated as making, my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim, or the date you are treated as making it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(1), am I barred from disability living allowance for a day before my claim` IS
    `s 76(1) the person is barred from a disability living allowance for the day by the date of claim` `the day I ask about` `the day I made, or am treated as making, my claim`

@export Under section 76(3), am I regarded as making a claim made for me on the ground that I am terminally ill?
GIVEN `a person purports to claim on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person purport to make a claim for disability living allowance on your behalf?
      `the claim is expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim made expressly on the ground that you are terminally ill?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 76(3), am I regarded as making a claim made for me on the ground that I am terminally ill` IS
    `s 76(3) the other person is regarded as making the claim` `a person purports to claim on my behalf` `the claim is expressly on the ground that I am terminally ill`


§ `ss 77 to 79 -- Guardian's allowance and age-related pensions`


§§ `s 77 -- Guardian's allowance`

@export Under section 77(1), am I entitled to a guardian's allowance for this child?
GIVEN `I am entitled to child benefit for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person?
      `the circumstances are those in section 77(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances those in section 77(1)(b) as section 77(2) describes them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(1), am I entitled to a guardian's allowance for this child` IS
    `s 77(1) the person is entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of the child or qualifying young person` `I am entitled to child benefit for the child` (JUST `the circumstances are those in section 77(2)`)

@export Under section 77(2), are the circumstances those in which I may get a guardian's allowance?
GIVEN `both parents are dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are both of the child's (or qualifying young person's) parents dead?
      `one parent is dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the parents dead?
      `I was unaware of the other parent's whereabouts at the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show that at the date of the death you were unaware of the whereabouts of the other parent?
      `I have failed after all reasonable efforts to find the other parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed, after all reasonable efforts, to discover the whereabouts of the other parent?
      `the other parent is in prison` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other parent in prison, treated as such under the regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(2), are the circumstances those in which I may get a guardian's allowance` IS
    `s 77(2) the circumstances are among those referred to in subsection (1)(b)` `both parents are dead` `one parent is dead` `I was unaware of the other parent's whereabouts at the death` `I have failed after all reasonable efforts to find the other parent` (JUST `the other parent is in prison`)

@export Under section 77(3), am I barred from a guardian's allowance by the parents' conditions?
GIVEN `a parent meets, or met before death, the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does at least one of the parents satisfy, or did one immediately before death satisfy, the conditions the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(3), am I barred from a guardian's allowance by the parents' conditions` IS
    `s 77(3) the person is barred from a guardian's allowance by the parents' conditions` (JUST `a parent meets, or met before death, the prescribed conditions`)

@export Under section 77(4), is the amount barred from payment by the conditions in section 77(5)?
GIVEN `I would be treated as having the child living with me for Part IX` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the purposes of Part IX, would you be treated as having the child or qualifying young person living with you?
      `the condition in section 77(5)(b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the condition in subsection (5)(b) met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(4), is the amount barred from payment by the conditions in section 77(5)` IS
    `s 77(4) the amount is barred from payment by the conditions in subsection (5)` (JUST `I would be treated as having the child living with me for Part IX`) (JUST `the condition in section 77(5)(b) is met`)

@export Under section 77(6), is the condition in section 77(5)(b) met?
GIVEN `the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable, in pounds?
      `the weekly rate at which I contribute in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate are you contributing to the child's maintenance, in pounds?
      `I am one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of two spouses or civil partners residing together?
      `the weekly rate at which we together contribute in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate do you and your spouse or civil partner together contribute, in pounds?
      `the contributions are over and above those required by section 143(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the contributions over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)?
      `the case is a prescribed case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case a prescribed case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(6), is the condition in section 77(5)(b) met` IS
    `s 77(6) the condition in subsection (5)(b) is satisfied` `the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable in pounds` `the weekly rate at which I contribute in pounds` `I am one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` `the weekly rate at which we together contribute in pounds` (JUST `the contributions are over and above those required by section 143(1)(b)`) (JUST `the case is a prescribed case`)

@export Under section 77(7), what is my weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of guardian's allowance in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 77(7), what is my weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds` IS
    `s 77(7) the weekly rate of a guardian's allowance in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds`)

@export Under section 77(9), am I the one of a couple who is entitled to the guardian's allowance?
GIVEN `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man?
      `a man and a woman are married or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are a man and a woman, married to or civil partners of each other, residing together?
      `we would each be entitled for the same child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from this subsection, would each of you be entitled in respect of the same child or qualifying young person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(9), am I the one of a couple who is entitled to the guardian's allowance` IS
    `s 77(9) the person is the one who is entitled to the guardian's allowance` `my sex` `a man and a woman are married or civil partners residing together` `we would each be entitled for the same child`

-- The seat names the same section as the question above; the two functions it calls have the same section label and differ in their words.
@export Under section 77(9), may payment be made to the man?
GIVEN `a man and a woman are married or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are a man and a woman, married to or civil partners of each other, residing together?
      `the woman elects that payment is not to be made to him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the woman elect, in the prescribed manner, that payment is not to be made to him?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(9), may payment be made to the man` IS
    `s 77(9) payment may be made to the man` `a man and a woman are married or civil partners residing together` `the woman elects that payment is not to be made to him`

@export Under section 77(10), am I barred from a guardian's allowance because I am the parent?
GIVEN `I am the parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the parent of the child or qualifying young person?
      `subsection (11) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection (11) apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(10), am I barred from a guardian's allowance because I am the parent` IS
    `s 77(10) the person is barred from a guardian's allowance because he or she is the parent` `I am the parent of the child or qualifying young person` (JUST `subsection (11) applies to me`)

@export Under section 77(11), does my adoption of the child leave my entitlement in place?
GIVEN `I have adopted the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you adopted the child or qualifying young person?
      `I was entitled just before the adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to guardian's allowance for the child just before the adoption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 77(11), does my adoption of the child leave my entitlement in place` IS
    `s 77(11) subsection (10) does not terminate the person's entitlement` `I have adopted the child or qualifying young person` `I was entitled just before the adoption`


§§ `s 78 -- Retirement pensions of Category C and Category D`

@export Under section 78(3), am I entitled to a Category D retirement pension?
GIVEN `the day I reached pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach pensionable age?
      `I am over 80` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 80?
      `I meet the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions the regulations prescribe?
      `I am entitled to a Category A, B or C retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category C retirement pension?
      `my weekly rate of that pension, disregarding the section 78(4) elements, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of that pension, disregarding additional pension, increases attributable to it, graduated retirement benefit and similar elements, in pounds?
      `the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(3), am I entitled to a Category D retirement pension` IS
    `s 78(3) the person is entitled to a Category D retirement pension` `me` (JUST `I am over 80`) (JUST `I meet the prescribed conditions`) `I am entitled to a Category A, B or C retirement pension` `my weekly rate of that pension, disregarding the section 78(4) elements, in pounds` (JUST `the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds`)
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
                `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1900    -- placeholder: section 78(3) does not read it
                `sex` IS Woman    -- placeholder: section 78(3) does not read it
                `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`    -- placeholder: section 78(3) does not read it
                `date of attaining pensionable age` IS `the day I reached pensionable age`

@export Under section 78(4), what is the weekly rate of my retirement pension disregarding the section 78(4) elements in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate at which my pension is payable in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate is the pension payable, in pounds?
      `any additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much additional pension is included, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `any increase attributable to additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much increase attributable to additional pension is included, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `any increase attributable to an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much increase attributable to an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension is included, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `any graduated retirement benefit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much graduated retirement benefit is included, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 78(4), what is the weekly rate of my retirement pension disregarding the section 78(4) elements in pounds` IS
    `s 78(4) the weekly rate of the pension disregarding the elements in pounds` `the weekly rate at which my pension is payable in pounds` `any additional pension in pounds` `any increase attributable to additional pension in pounds` `any increase attributable to an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension in pounds` `any graduated retirement benefit in pounds`

@export Under section 78(6), what is the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds?
GIVEN `the appropriate weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate in Schedule 4 for a Category D retirement pension, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 78(6), what is the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` IS
    `s 78(6) the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` (JUST `the appropriate weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 78(7), does my Category D retirement pension entitlement continue on a day?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a Category D retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category D retirement pension?
      `I am alive on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you alive on the day you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(7), does my Category D retirement pension entitlement continue on a day` IS
    `s 78(7) the entitlement continues on the day` `I am entitled to a Category D retirement pension` `I am alive on the day`

@export Under section 78(8), is my Category D retirement pension barred from payment for a day?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the day my entitlement is regarded as commencing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your entitlement to be regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 78(8), is my Category D retirement pension barred from payment for a day` IS
    `s 78(8) the Category D retirement pension is barred from payment for the day` `the day I ask about` `the day my entitlement is regarded as commencing`


§§ `s 79 -- Increase of retirement pension etc. for persons over 80`

@export Under section 79(1), am I entitled to an age addition to a retirement pension?
GIVEN `I am over 80` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 80?
      `I am entitled to a retirement pension of a category under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a retirement pension of a category under this Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(1), am I entitled to an age addition to a retirement pension` IS
    `s 79(1) the person is entitled to an age addition to a retirement pension` (JUST `I am over 80`) `I am entitled to a retirement pension of a category under this Act`

@export Under section 79(2), am I entitled to an age addition to another pension or allowance?
GIVEN `I get a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument?
      `I am over 80` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you over 80?
      `I meet such other conditions as are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fulfil such other conditions as the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(2), am I entitled to an age addition to another pension or allowance` IS
    `s 79(2) the person is entitled to an age addition to another pension or allowance` (JUST `I get a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument`) (JUST `I am over 80`) (JUST `I meet such other conditions as are prescribed`)

@export Under section 79(3), is my age addition payable on a day?
GIVEN `I am entitled to an age addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an age addition?
      `I am alive on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you alive on the day you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 79(3), is my age addition payable on a day` IS
    `s 79(3) the age addition is payable on the day` `I am entitled to an age addition` `I am alive on the day`

@export Under section 79(3), what is my weekly rate of age addition in pounds?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of age addition in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of age addition in Schedule 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 79(3), what is my weekly rate of age addition in pounds` IS
    `s 79(3) the weekly rate of age addition in pounds` (JUST `the weekly rate of age addition in pounds`)


§ `Part IV -- Increases for dependants`


§§ `s 86A -- Incapacity benefit: increase for adult dependants`

@export Under section 86A(1), what is the increase of my incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds?
GIVEN `the prescribed circumstances for an increase are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances the regulations prescribe for an increase for an adult dependant met in your case?
      `the Schedule 4 amount for an adult dependant in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount for an adult dependant in Schedule 4, Part IV, column (3), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 86A(1), what is the increase of my incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` IS
    `s 86A(1) the increase of incapacity benefit for an adult dependant in pounds` (JUST `the prescribed circumstances for an increase are met`) (JUST `the Schedule 4 amount for an adult dependant in pounds`)


§§ `s 87 -- Rate of increase where associated retirement pension is attributable to reduced contributions`

@export Under section 87(1), is the amount of my increase determined under the regulations?
GIVEN `I am entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b)?
      `the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the retirement pension by reference to which the rate is determined have been payable only by virtue of section 60?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 87(1), is the amount of my increase determined under the regulations` IS
    `s 87(1) the amount of any increase is determined in accordance with regulations under this section` `I am entitled to short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(2)(b)` (JUST `the retirement pension would be payable only by virtue of section 60`)

@export Under section 87(2), am I barred from an increase under the regulations?
GIVEN `the retirement pension would have been payable only by virtue of section 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the retirement pension have been payable only by virtue of section 60?
