§ `Part V -- Benefit for industrial injuries`


§§ `s 94 -- Right to industrial injuries benefit`

@export Under section 94(1), is industrial injuries benefit payable for my injury?
GIVEN `I am an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employed earner?
      `I suffered personal injury caused by an accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer personal injury caused by an accident?
      `the accident arose out of and in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accident arise out of and in the course of your employment? (Sections 94(3) and 98 to 101 below may help you answer.)
      `my employment is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment employed earner's employment, within section 95?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(1), is industrial injuries benefit payable for my injury` IS
    `s 94(1) industrial injuries benefit is payable` `the kind`
    WHERE
        `the kind` MEANS `s 94(1) the personal injury is of a kind mentioned in section 94(1)` (JUST `I am an employed earner`) `I suffered personal injury caused by an accident` (JUST `the accident arose out of and in the course of my employment`) (JUST `my employment is employed earner's employment`)

@export Under section 94(2), is this benefit part of industrial injuries benefit?
GIVEN `the benefit I am asking about` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(2), is this benefit part of industrial injuries benefit` IS
    `s 94(2) the benefit is part of industrial injuries benefit` `the benefit I am asking about`

@export Under section 94(3), is my accident taken to have arisen out of my employment?
GIVEN `the accident arose in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accident arise in the course of an employed earner's employment?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence that it did not arise out of that employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(3), is my accident taken to have arisen out of my employment` IS
    `s 94(3) the accident is taken to have arisen out of the employment` `the accident arose in the course of my employment` `there is evidence to the contrary`

@export Under section 94(5), am I barred from industrial injuries benefit because the accident was outside Great Britain?
GIVEN `the accident happened while I was outside Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accident happen while you were outside Great Britain?
      `the exception in section 117 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 117 apply to the accident?
      `the exception in section 119 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 119 apply to the accident?
      `the exception in section 120 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 120 apply to the accident?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(5), am I barred from industrial injuries benefit because the accident was outside Great Britain` IS
    `s 94(5) the person is barred from industrial injuries benefit for an accident outside Great Britain` `the accident happened while I was outside Great Britain` (JUST `the exception in section 117 applies`) (JUST `the exception in section 119 applies`) (JUST `the exception in section 120 applies`)

@export Under section 94(6), am I incapable of work, work meaning work I can reasonably be expected to do?
GIVEN `the word is used in a later provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question asked in one of the provisions of this Part that follow section 94(6)?
      `I am incapable of the work in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of the work in question?
      `it is work I can reasonably be expected to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it work which you can reasonably be expected to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 94(6), am I incapable of work, work meaning work I can reasonably be expected to do` IS
    `s 94(6) the person is incapable of work, "work" meaning work the person can reasonably be expected to do` `the word is used in a later provision of this Part` `I am incapable of the work in question` `it is work I can reasonably be expected to do`


