§ `Part V, continued -- from the cross-heading Disablement pension to Old cases`


§§ `s 103 -- Disablement pension`

@export Under section 103(1), am I entitled to disablement pension?
GIVEN `I am an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employed earner?
      `I suffer loss of physical or mental faculty as the result of the relevant accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer, as the result of the relevant accident, from loss of physical or mental faculty?
      `the assessed extent of my disablement as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the assessed extent of your disablement, as a percentage?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(1), am I entitled to disablement pension` IS
    `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST `I am an employed earner`) `I suffer loss of physical or mental faculty as the result of the relevant accident` (JUST `the assessed extent of my disablement as a percentage`) `the date of my claim`

@export Under section 103(2), what is my aggregate percentage of disablement?
GIVEN `the percentage from the relevant accident` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of disablement results from the relevant accident?
      `the percentage of my first earlier disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have an earlier present disablement, what is its assessed percentage? (0 if none)
      `it resulted from another accident in my employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it result from another accident arising out of and in the course of your employment, being employed earner's employment?
      `no disablement gratuity was paid for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it one for which a disablement gratuity was not paid after a final assessment?
      `the percentage of my second earlier disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a second earlier present disablement, what is its assessed percentage? (0 if none)
      `the second resulted from another accident in my employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it result from another accident arising out of and in the course of your employment, being employed earner's employment?
      `no disablement gratuity was paid for the second` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it one for which a disablement gratuity was not paid after a final assessment?
      `the percentage added under regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage is added in accordance with regulations under section 109(2) made by virtue of section 109(4)(b)? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 103(2), what is my aggregate percentage of disablement` IS
    `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` `the percentage from the relevant accident` `my earlier disablements` (JUST `the percentage added under regulations`)
    WHERE
        `my earlier disablements` MEANS LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` OF `the percentage of my first earlier disablement`, `it resulted from another accident in my employed earner's employment`, `no disablement gratuity was paid for it`), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` OF `the percentage of my second earlier disablement`, `the second resulted from another accident in my employed earner's employment`, `no disablement gratuity was paid for the second`)

@export Under section 103(3), what percentage is my assessment treated as?
GIVEN `my assessed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the assessed percentage of your disablement?
      `the date of my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your claim?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 103(3), what percentage is my assessment treated as` IS
    `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` `my assessed percentage` `the date of my claim`

@export Under section 103(4), which percentage does the rounding rule read?
GIVEN `subsection (2) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the extent of your disablement determined with an addition under subsection (2)?
      `the percentage from the relevant accident` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage results from the relevant accident alone?
      `the aggregate percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate percentage?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 103(4), which percentage does the rounding rule read` IS
    `s 103(4) the percentage to which subsection (3) applies` `subsection (2) applies to me` `the percentage from the relevant accident` `the aggregate percentage`

@export Under section 103(5), is the extent of my disablement assessed?
GIVEN `the extent was assessed in accordance with Schedule 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the extent of your disablement assessed in accordance with Schedule 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(5), is the extent of my disablement assessed` IS
    `s 103(5) the extent of the disablement is assessed` `the extent was assessed in accordance with Schedule 6`

@export Under section 103(5), am I taken to have no relevant loss of faculty?
GIVEN `the extent of the resulting disablement, if so assessed, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc If your disablement were assessed under Schedule 6, what percentage would the extent be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(5), am I taken to have no relevant loss of faculty` IS
    `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST `the extent of the resulting disablement, if so assessed, as a percentage`)

@export Under section 103(6), am I barred from disablement pension for a day by the 90 days?
GIVEN `the day of the relevant accident` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the relevant accident happen?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(6), am I barred from disablement pension for a day by the 90 days` IS
    `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` `the day of the relevant accident` `the day I ask about`

@export Under section 103(7), what weekly rate is my disablement pension paid at in pounds?
GIVEN `the pension is payable for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is disablement pension payable to you for the period?
      `the Schedule 4 weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate weekly rate in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 1, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 103(7), what weekly rate is my disablement pension paid at in pounds` IS
    `s 103(7) the weekly rate at which the disablement pension is paid in pounds` `the pension is payable for the period` (JUST `the Schedule 4 weekly rate in pounds`)

@export Under section 103(8), does my pension cease on my death before the end of its period?
GIVEN `my pension is limited by reference to a definite date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period of your pension limited by reference to a definite date?
      `that date` IS A DATE @desc What is that date? (Ignored if the period is not so limited.)
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beneficiary died?
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the beneficiary die? (Ignored if not died.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(8), does my pension cease on my death before the end of its period` IS
    `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` `the limit` `the death`
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS IF `my pension is limited by reference to a definite date` THEN JUST `that date` ELSE NOTHING
        `the death` MEANS IF `I have died` THEN JUST `the date of death` ELSE NOTHING


§§ `ss 104 and 105 -- Increases of disablement pension`

@export Under section 104(1), is my disablement pension increased for constant attendance?
GIVEN `a disablement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a disablement pension payable to you?
      `the assessment is a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage assessment is the pension payable in respect of?
      `I require constant attendance as the result of the loss of faculty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as the result of the relevant loss of faculty, require constant attendance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 104(1), is my disablement pension increased for constant attendance` IS
    `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` `a disablement pension is payable to me` `the assessment is a percentage` `I require constant attendance as the result of the loss of faculty`

@export Under section 104(1), how much is the constant attendance increase in pounds?
GIVEN `the increase applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pension increased for constant attendance under section 104(1)?
      `the amount determined by regulations in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do the regulations determine, by reference to the extent and nature of the attendance you require, in pounds?
      `the Schedule 4 limit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate amount in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 104(1), how much is the constant attendance increase in pounds` IS
    `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST `the increase applies to me`) (JUST `the amount determined by regulations in pounds`) (JUST `the Schedule 4 limit in pounds`)

@export Under section 104(2), is my constant attendance increase payable on a day?
GIVEN `the first day of the period fixed when it was granted` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period fixed when the increase was granted?
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 104(2), is my constant attendance increase payable on a day` IS
    `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` `the period` `the day I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of the period fixed when it was granted`, `the last day` IS `the last day of that period`

@export Under section 105(1), is my disablement pension further increased for exceptionally severe disablement?
GIVEN `a disablement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a disablement pension payable to you?
      `I am, or but for in-patient treatment would be, entitled to a section 104 increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or but for medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution would you be, entitled to an increase under section 104?
      `the weekly rate of my section 104 increase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of that increase, in pounds?
      `the Schedule 4 paragraph 2(a) amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a), in pounds?
      `my need for constant attendance is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your need for constant attendance, of an extent and nature qualifying you for such an increase at a rate above that amount, likely to be permanent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(1), is my disablement pension further increased for exceptionally severe disablement` IS
    `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` `a disablement pension is payable to me` (JUST `I am, or but for in-patient treatment would be, entitled to a section 104 increase`) (JUST `the weekly rate of my section 104 increase in pounds`) (JUST `the Schedule 4 paragraph 2(a) amount in pounds`) `my need for constant attendance is likely to be permanent`

@export Under section 105(1), how much is the further increase in pounds?
GIVEN `the further increase applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your pension further increased under section 105(1)?
      `the Schedule 4 paragraph 3 amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 105(1), how much is the further increase in pounds` IS
    `s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` (JUST `the further increase applies to me`) (JUST `the Schedule 4 paragraph 3 amount in pounds`)

@export Under section 105(2), is my further increase for exceptionally severe disablement payable on a day?
GIVEN `the first day of the period fixed when it was granted` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period fixed when the increase was granted?
      `the last day of that period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 105(2), is my further increase for exceptionally severe disablement payable on a day` IS
    `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` `the period` `the day I ask about`
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of the period fixed when it was granted`, `the last day` IS `the last day of that period`


§§ `s 106 -- Benefits and increases subject to qualifications as to time`

@export Under section 106, does Schedule 7 have effect for this benefit or increase?
GIVEN `the benefit or increase I am asking about` IS A `s 106 Benefit or increase` @desc Which benefit or increase are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 106, does Schedule 7 have effect for this benefit or increase` IS
    `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `the benefit or increase I am asking about`


§§ `s 107 -- Adjustments for successive accidents`

@export Under section 107(1)(a), am I barred from an aggregate weekly rate of disablement pensions above the appropriate amount?
GIVEN `I have suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of your employed earner's employment?
      `my aggregate weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate weekly rate of your disablement pensions for the same period, apart from the increases in subsection (2), in pounds?
      `the Schedule 4 paragraph 4 amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate amount in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(1)(a), am I barred from an aggregate weekly rate of disablement pensions above the appropriate amount` IS
    `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` `I have suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of my employment` `my aggregate weekly rate in pounds` (JUST `the Schedule 4 paragraph 4 amount in pounds`)

@export Under section 107(1)(a), what is the most I may receive in aggregate for the same period in pounds?
GIVEN `I have suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of your employed earner's employment?
      `my aggregate weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the aggregate weekly rate of your disablement pensions for the same period, apart from the increases in subsection (2), in pounds?
      `the Schedule 4 paragraph 4 amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the appropriate amount in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 4, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 107(1)(a), what is the most I may receive in aggregate for the same period in pounds` IS
    `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` `I have suffered two or more successive accidents arising out of and in the course of my employment` `my aggregate weekly rate in pounds` (JUST `the Schedule 4 paragraph 4 amount in pounds`)

@export Under section 107(2), is this increase one referred to in section 107(1)?
GIVEN `the provision the increase is under` IS A `s 107(2) Provision` @desc Under which provision is the increase?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 107(2), is this increase one referred to in section 107(1)` IS
    `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `the provision the increase is under`


§§ `ss 108 to 110 -- Prescribed industrial diseases, etc.`

@export Under section 108(1), are industrial injuries benefits payable for my prescribed disease or injury?
GIVEN `I have been in employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in employed earner's employment?
      `the disease is a prescribed disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disease a prescribed disease?
      `the injury is a prescribed personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury a prescribed personal injury?
      `the injury was caused by accident arising out of and in the course of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the injury caused by accident arising out of and in the course of your employment?
      `it is due to the nature of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disease or injury due to the nature of that employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(1), are industrial injuries benefits payable for my prescribed disease or injury` IS
    `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` `I have been in employed earner's employment` (JUST `the disease is a prescribed disease`) (JUST `the injury is a prescribed personal injury`) `the injury was caused by accident arising out of and in the course of my employment` (JUST `it is due to the nature of that employment`)

@export Under section 108(6), am I barred from benefit for a disease as an injury by accident?
GIVEN `I claim for a disease as an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of an employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of an employment?
      `at the time of the accident the disease was a prescribed disease by virtue of my occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the accident, was the disease in relation to you a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation in which you were engaged in that employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 108(6), am I barred from benefit for a disease as an injury by accident` IS
    `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` `I claim for a disease as an injury by accident arising out of and in the course of an employment` (JUST `at the time of the accident the disease was a prescribed disease by virtue of my occupation`)

@export Under section 109(1), are the benefit and conditions for a prescribed disease the same as for an accident?
GIVEN `different provision is made by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations make different provision for your case?
      `a later provision of section 109 or 110 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a later provision of section 109 or section 110 provide otherwise for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(1), are the benefit and conditions for a prescribed disease the same as for an accident` IS
    `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST `different provision is made by regulations`) (JUST `a later provision of section 109 or 110 provides otherwise`)

@export Under section 109(2), is this provision taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance?
GIVEN `it is section 1 of the Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it section 1 of the Administration Act?
      `it relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(2), is this provision taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` IS
    `s 109(2) the provision is taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` `it is section 1 of the Administration Act` `it relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits`

@export Under section 109(5), does my present disablement count in the appropriate percentage for section 109(4)(a)?
GIVEN `the assessed percentage of my present disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the assessed percentage of your present disablement?
      `it resulted from an accident arising out of and in the course of my employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it result from an accident arising out of and in the course of your employment, being employed earner's employment?
      `it resulted from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it result from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment?
      `no disablement gratuity was paid to me after a final assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disablement in respect of which no disablement gratuity was paid to you after a final assessment of your disablement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(5), does my present disablement count in the appropriate percentage for section 109(4)(a)` IS
    `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` `my present disablement`
    WHERE
        `my present disablement` MEANS `s 109(5) Present disablement` WITH `the assessed percentage` IS `the assessed percentage of my present disablement`, `it resulted from an accident arising out of and in the course of his employment, being employed earner's employment` IS `it resulted from an accident arising out of and in the course of my employed earner's employment`, `it resulted from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment` IS `it resulted from another prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of that employment`, `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement` IS `no disablement gratuity was paid to me after a final assessment`

@export Under section 109(6), does my present disablement count in the appropriate percentage for section 109(4)(b)?
GIVEN `the assessed percentage of my present disablement` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the assessed percentage of your present disablement?
      `it resulted from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it result from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of your employment?
      `no disablement gratuity was paid to me after a final assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disablement in respect of which no disablement gratuity was paid to you after a final assessment of your disablement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(6), does my present disablement count in the appropriate percentage for section 109(4)(b)` IS
    `s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` `my present disablement`
    WHERE
        `my present disablement` MEANS `s 109(6) Present disablement` WITH `the assessed percentage` IS `the assessed percentage of my present disablement`, `it resulted from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment` IS `it resulted from a prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of my employment`, `a disablement gratuity was not paid to him after a final assessment of his disablement` IS `no disablement gratuity was paid to me after a final assessment`

@export Under section 110(3), what least extent of disablement am I treated as having from pneumoconiosis, as a percentage?
GIVEN `I am found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 110(3), what least extent of disablement am I treated as having from pneumoconiosis, as a percentage` IS
    `s 110(3) the least assessed extent of the disablement treated as resulting, as a percentage` `I am found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis`

@export Under section 110(4), am I barred from disablement benefit for byssinosis?
GIVEN `my claim is in respect of byssinosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim in respect of byssinosis?
      `regulations otherwise provide for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations otherwise provide for your case?
      `I am found to be suffering a loss of faculty likely to be permanent as the result of byssinosis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found to be suffering, as the result of byssinosis, from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 110(4), am I barred from disablement benefit for byssinosis` IS
    `s 110(4) the person is barred from disablement benefit in respect of byssinosis` `my claim is in respect of byssinosis` (JUST `regulations otherwise provide for me`) `I am found to be suffering a loss of faculty likely to be permanent as the result of byssinosis`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc5 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, 1992 c. 4 -- part ssc5 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who works, is self-employed, or claims a benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great
-- Britain: the person asking whether and how much they must pay in contributions, whether they are entitled to a
-- benefit or to statutory pay, how much, for how long, and what ends or reduces it.  This part's questions cover
-- Parts VI to X of the Act (ss 112 to 150), lines 2444 to 3094 of the source.
--
-- This layer phrases rules already encoded in the ssc5 modules imported above as the questions that person would
-- ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the records a rule needs from
-- plain answers and calls the rule.  Every question is named "Under section N, ..." with the Act's own numbering.
--
-- A result of MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER is read as in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ssc5)":
-- JUST FALSE is the Act saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "the text does not answer", never "no".
--
-- Plain inputs.  A fact that is a Boolean, a number or a date is asked as such.  A choice among the module's own
-- cases (a kind of payment, a place, a sex) is asked as a choice from the list.  Where a rule reads only part of
-- a record, the unread fields are fixed placeholders with a comment.  Figures that regulations prescribe are
-- never in the Act: they are asked.
--
-- Seams.  Questions in this layer that need an answer from another part's section (Schedule 9 and Schedule 10 for
-- child benefit, s 55(3) and s 55C(3) for deferment) take it as a plain fact from the person; the merged layer
-- may wire them.  See NOTES.md, "Seams (ssc5)".


§ `Part VI -- Earnings, disqualification, Crown and forces, tax years (ss 112-122)`

-- Most of these questions arise only for a person who is in the situation they name (a lump sum on reinstatement, a spell abroad or in custody, Crown or forces service, an accident outside Great Britain, work offshore, a spouse, infirmity): the form can ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing each.

@export Under section 112(2), is a sum I was paid an employment protection entitlement?
GIVEN `which kind of sum it is` IS A `s 112(3) Sum` @desc Which kind of sum is it? Choose: arrears of pay under a reinstatement or re-engagement order; pay under an order continuing a contract of employment; remuneration under a protective award; or some other sum
      `only part of that sum is in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking about only a part of that sum?
      `that part is one the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that part one that regulations prescribe?
      `the amount is prescribed and regulations treat it as related to one of those sums` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an amount that regulations prescribe and treat as related to one of those sums?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 112(2), is a sum I was paid an employment protection entitlement` IS
    `s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` `which kind of sum it is` `only part of that sum is in question` `that part is one the regulations prescribe` `the amount is prescribed and regulations treat it as related to one of those sums`

@export Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period?
GIVEN `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one of the benefits under Parts II to V of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (contributory, non-contributory or industrial injuries benefits)?
      `I am absent from Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from Great Britain for the period you are asking about?
      `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period you are asking about?
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide otherwise for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(1), am I disqualified from receiving a benefit for a period` IS
    `s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of the Act` `I am absent from Great Britain for the period` `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` `regulations otherwise provide`

@export Under section 113(1), is an increase of benefit payable for my wife, husband or civil partner for a period?
GIVEN `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one of the benefits under Parts II to V of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (contributory, non-contributory or industrial injuries benefits)?
      `I am absent from Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you absent from Great Britain for the period you are asking about?
      `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period you are asking about?
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide otherwise for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 113(1), is an increase of benefit payable for my wife, husband or civil partner for a period` IS
    `s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of the Act` `I am absent from Great Britain for the period` `I am undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` `regulations otherwise provide`

@export Under section 115(1), do Parts I to V of the Act apply to me as if I were employed by a private person?
GIVEN `I am employed by or under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by or under the Crown?
      `I am serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces, in that capacity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(1), do Parts I to V of the Act apply to me as if I were employed by a private person` IS
    `s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` `I am employed by or under the Crown` `I am serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces in that capacity`

@export Under section 115(3), is my employment employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V?
GIVEN `my employment is as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `my employment is other prescribed employment under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment some other employment under the Crown that regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 115(3), is my employment employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` IS
    `s 115(3) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` `my employment is as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `my employment is other prescribed employment under the Crown`

@export Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces?
GIVEN `I am serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces?
      `the purpose is` IS A `s 116(1) Purpose` @desc For which purpose are you asking? Choose: a purpose of Parts I to IV of the Act; a purpose of Part V; a purpose of Part VI; a purpose of a provision of the Administration Act as it applies to you as an employed earner; or some other purpose
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(1), am I treated as an employed earner because I serve in Her Majesty's forces` IS
    `s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` `I am serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces` `the purpose is`

@export Under section 117, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for ships, hovercraft and aircraft?
GIVEN `I was employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed (now, before, or in future) on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft?
      `regulations under section 117(1) apply the provision to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 117(1) apply the provision to your accident?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 117, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for ships, hovercraft and aircraft` IS
    `s 117 the accident falls within the exception` `I was employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` `regulations under section 117(1) apply the provision to my accident`

@export Under section 119, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for persons outside Great Britain?
GIVEN `I was outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you outside Great Britain at a time, or in circumstances, that regulations prescribe?
      `regulations under section 119 apply the provision to my accident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 119 apply the provision to your accident?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 119, does my accident outside Great Britain fall within the exception for persons outside Great Britain` IS
