GIVEN `the amount is a prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount one that regulations prescribe?
      `I am of a prescribed description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you of a description that regulations prescribe?
      `the circumstances are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances ones that regulations prescribe?
      `the expenses are for heating and appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the expenses for heating that appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 138(2), may a heating payment for cold weather be made to me` IS
    `s 138(2) the heating payment may be made out of the social fund` `the amount is a prescribed amount` `I am of a prescribed description` `the circumstances are prescribed` `the expenses are for heating and appear to the Secretary of State to have been or to be likely to be incurred in cold weather`

@export Under section 139(4), is my crisis loan or budgeting loan repayable on the terms notified to me?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment` @desc Which kind of payment is it? Choose: maternity expenses; funeral expenses; community care grant; crisis loan; budgeting loan; or some other kind
      `before the award was paid the Secretary of State notified terms and conditions to the person who made the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the award was paid, did the Secretary of State notify you of terms and conditions of repayment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 139(4), is my crisis loan or budgeting loan repayable on the terms notified to me` IS
    `s 139(4) the award is repayable on the notified terms` `the kind of payment` `before the award was paid the Secretary of State notified terms and conditions to the person who made the application`

@export Under section 139(5), is payment of my award to be made to me?
GIVEN `the appropriate officer has determined that the payment is to be made otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appropriate officer determined that the payment is to be made otherwise than to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 139(5), is payment of my award to be made to me` IS
    `s 139(5) payment of the award is to be made to the applicant` `the appropriate officer has determined that the payment is to be made otherwise`

@export Under section 140(1), must the officer have regard to a matter in deciding my award?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `s 138(1) Kind of payment` @desc Which kind of payment is it? Choose: maternity expenses; funeral expenses; community care grant; crisis loan; budgeting loan; or some other kind
      `the matter` IS A `s 140 Matter` @desc Which matter are you asking about? Choose: the nature, extent and urgency of the need; the existence of resources; the possibility that another person or body may meet the need; likelihood and time of repayment; any relevant allocation under section 168; any other circumstance of the case; or your personal circumstances specified in directions
      `the payment is repayable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment repayable?
      `a direction or guidance under section 140(2) displaces the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a direction or guidance of the Secretary of State under section 140(2) displace the duty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 140(1), must the officer have regard to a matter in deciding my award` IS
    `s 140(1) the officer must have regard to the matter` `the kind of payment` `the matter` `the payment is repayable` `a direction or guidance under section 140(2) displaces the duty`

@export Under section 140A, am I entitled to health in pregnancy grant?
GIVEN `my sex` IS A Sex @desc Are you a woman or a man? (choose Woman or Man)
      `I satisfy prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions that regulations prescribe in relation to a pregnancy of yours?
      `I have reached the 25th week of my pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the 25th week of your pregnancy?
      `the date I reached the 25th week of my pregnancy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you reach the 25th week of your pregnancy? (any date if you have not)
      `I have received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional?
      `I am in Great Britain at the time I make a claim for the grant (or am treated by regulations as being there)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain when you make your claim for the grant (or treated by regulations as being there)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 140A, am I entitled to health in pregnancy grant` IS
    `s 140A the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant` (`s 140A(1) the woman is entitled to payment of health in pregnancy grant` (`s 140A(5) the person is a woman` `my sex`) `I satisfy prescribed conditions in relation to a pregnancy of mine`) (`s 140A(2) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as subsection (2) goes` `I have reached the 25th week of my pregnancy` `the date I reached the 25th week of my pregnancy`) (`s 140A(3)(a) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (a) goes` `I have received advice on matters relating to maternal health from a health professional`) (`s 140A(3)(b) the woman is entitled to health in pregnancy grant as far as paragraph (b) goes` `I am in Great Britain at the time I make a claim for the grant (or am treated by regulations as being there)`)

@export Under section 140B(1), what amount of health in pregnancy grant do I get in pounds?
GIVEN `regulations prescribe an amount for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Treasury's regulations prescribe an amount for your case?
      `that amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do they prescribe, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 140B(1), what amount of health in pregnancy grant do I get in pounds` IS
    `s 140B(1) the amount of health in pregnancy grant in pounds` (IF `regulations prescribe an amount for my case` THEN JUST `that amount in pounds` ELSE NOTHING)

§ `Part IX -- Child benefit (ss 141-147)`

-- These questions arise only for a person who is responsible for, or has been responsible for, a child or a qualifying young person: the form can ask "Do you have a child for whom you claim, or may claim, child benefit?" before showing the group.

@export Under section 141, am I entitled to child benefit for a week?
GIVEN `the child is living with me in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child living with you in the week?
      `I have had the child living with me at some time before the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had the child living with you at some time before the week?
      `the days in the 16 weeks before the week on which we were absent from one another` IS A NUMBER @desc In the 16 weeks before the week, for how many days were you and the child absent from one another?
      `the days of those that are to be disregarded under section 143(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those days, how many are to be disregarded under section 143(3)?
      `the weekly rate at which I contribute to the cost of providing for the child in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate do you contribute to the cost of providing for the child, in pounds?
      `the weekly rate of child benefit payable for the child for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of child benefit payable for the child for the week, in pounds?
      `the child is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child in Great Britain in the week (or treated by regulations as being there)?
      `I am in Great Britain in the week (or am treated as being)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Great Britain in the week (or treated by regulations as being there)?
      `Schedule 9 excludes my entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Schedule 9 exclude your entitlement to child benefit?
      `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week apart from section 144(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people (you included) would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week, apart from section 144(3)?
      `Schedule 10 makes me the one entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Schedule 10 make you the one of them who is entitled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 141, am I entitled to child benefit for a week` IS
    `s 141 the person is entitled to child benefit for the week` `my responsibility` (`s 146(1) the child or qualifying young person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` `the child is in Great Britain in the week (or is treated as being)`) (`s 146(2) the person is in Great Britain as the subsection requires` `I am in Great Britain in the week (or am treated as being)`) (`s 144(2) entitlement to child benefit is excluded by Schedule 9` (JUST `Schedule 9 excludes my entitlement`)) `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week apart from section 144(3)` (JUST `Schedule 10 makes me the one entitled`)
    WHERE
        `my responsibility` MEANS
            `s 143(1) the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person in the week`
                (`s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` `the child is living with me in the week`
                    (`s 143(2) the child or qualifying young person is treated as living with the person in the week` `I have had the child living with me at some time before the week` `the days in the 16 weeks before the week on which we were absent from one another` `the days of those that are to be disregarded under section 143(3)`))
                (`s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` `the weekly rate at which I contribute to the cost of providing for the child in pounds` `the weekly rate of child benefit payable for the child for the week in pounds`)

@export Under section 142(1), is my child a child for the purposes of child benefit?
GIVEN `my child is under 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child under 16?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 142(1), is my child a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS
    `s 142(1) the person is a child` (JUST `my child is under 16`)

@export Under section 142(2), is my child a qualifying young person?
GIVEN `my child is under 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child under 16?
      `my child is under the age prescribed under section 142(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child under the age (greater than 16) that regulations prescribe?
      `my child satisfies the conditions prescribed under section 142(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the child satisfy the conditions that regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 142(2), is my child a qualifying young person` IS
    `s 142(2) the person is a qualifying young person` (`s 142(1) the person is a child` (JUST `my child is under 16`)) (JUST `my child is under the age prescribed under section 142(2)(a)`) `my child satisfies the conditions prescribed under section 142(2)(b)`

@export Under section 143(3), is a day when my child was away from me disregarded?
GIVEN `the reason for the absence` IS A `s 143(3) Reason for the absence` @desc What was the reason for the absence? Choose: education or training; in-patient treatment in a hospital or similar institution; residential accommodation under listed arrangements; or some other reason
      `the absence is due solely to that fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence due solely to that reason?
      `the circumstances are prescribed ones for the residential accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For residential accommodation: are the circumstances ones that regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 143(3), is a day when my child was away from me disregarded` IS
    `s 143(3) the day of absence is disregarded` `the reason for the absence` `the absence is due solely to that fact` `the circumstances are prescribed ones for the residential accommodation`

@export Under section 143(4), how many days of my child's absence may be disregarded?
GIVEN `the days of absence for education or training` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of absence were for education or training?
      `the days of absence for in-patient treatment or residential accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of absence were for in-patient treatment or residential accommodation?
      `the number of days regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days do the regulations prescribe as the limit?
      `I regularly incur expenditure in respect of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you regularly incur expenditure in respect of the child?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 143(4), how many days of my child's absence may be disregarded` IS
    `s 143(4) the number of days that may be disregarded` `the days of absence for education or training` `the days of absence for in-patient treatment or residential accommodation` `the number of days regulations prescribe` `I regularly incur expenditure in respect of the child`

@export Under section 144(3), am I the one entitled to child benefit when two or more people would be?
GIVEN `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week apart from section 144(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people (you included) would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week, apart from section 144(3)?
      `Schedule 10 makes me the one entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Schedule 10 make you the one of them who is entitled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 144(3), am I the one entitled to child benefit when two or more people would be` IS
    `s 144(3) the person is the one entitled among those who would be entitled` `the number of persons who would be entitled to child benefit for the child for the week apart from section 144(3)` (JUST `Schedule 10 makes me the one entitled`)

@export Under section 145A(1), am I entitled to child benefit for a week after my child's death?
GIVEN `the child died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the child die?
      `I was entitled to child benefit for the child for the week in which the death occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to child benefit for the child for the week in which the death occurred?
      `the week asked about, counting the first week after the week of death as 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week after the death are you asking about? (the first week after the week of the death is 1)
      `the length of the prescribed period in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is the period that regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 145A(1), am I entitled to child benefit for a week after my child's death` IS
    `s 145A(1) the person is entitled to child benefit for the week after the death` `the child died` `I was entitled to child benefit for the child for the week in which the death occurred` `the week asked about, counting the first week after the week of death as 1` `the length of the prescribed period in weeks`

@export Under section 145A(2), am I entitled to the child benefit a dead partner would have received?
GIVEN `the person entitled under section 145A(1) died before the end of the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person entitled under section 145A(1) die before the end of the prescribed period?
      `the two people are a man and a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the two people a man and a woman?
      `they are married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they married to each other?
      `they are civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they civil partners of each other?
      `they are separated under a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they separated under a court order?
      `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent?
      `they are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners?
      `the dead person was living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the dead person living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 145A(2), am I entitled to the child benefit a dead partner would have received` IS
    `s 145A(2) the other member of the couple is entitled to child benefit for the rest of the period` `the person entitled under section 145A(1) died before the end of the prescribed period` (`s 145A(5) the two people are a married couple` `the two people are a man and a woman` `they are married to each other` `they are separated under a court order` `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent`) (`s 145A(5) the two people are a civil partnership` `they are civil partners of each other` `they are separated under a court order` `they are separated in circumstances in which the separation is likely to be permanent`) (`s 145A(5) the two people are a cohabiting couple` (`they are married to each other` OR `they are civil partners of each other`) `they are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners`) `the dead person was living with the person to whom he was married or who was his civil partner`

@export Under section 147(1), in which Monday-to-Sunday week does a date fall?
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE @desc What is the date?
GIVETH A Period
DECIDE `Under section 147(1), in which Monday-to-Sunday week does a date fall` IS
    `s 147(1) the week containing the date` `the date`

§ `Part X -- Christmas bonus for pensioners (ss 148-150)`

-- The Christmas bonus arises only for a person who is entitled to a qualifying benefit, such as a retirement pension, in the week the Act names: the form can ask "Do you receive a pension or a similar benefit?" before showing the group.

@export Under section 148(1), am I entitled to a Christmas bonus?
GIVEN `the place I was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week` IS A `s 148(1)(a) Place` @desc Where were you present or ordinarily resident during the relevant week? Choose: the United Kingdom; an EEA state; Switzerland; the Channel Islands; the Isle of Man; Gibraltar; or somewhere else
      `I am entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a day in the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a day in the relevant week?
      `I am treated as so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated (under section 149) as so entitled?
      `the provision to which my entitlement is subject allows the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision to which your entitlement is subject allow the payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 148(1), am I entitled to a Christmas bonus` IS
    `s 148(1) the person is entitled to payment under subsection (1)` `the place I was present or ordinarily resident in during the relevant week` `I am entitled to a payment of a qualifying benefit for a period that includes a day in the relevant week` `I am treated as so entitled` `the provision to which my entitlement is subject allows the payment`

@export Under section 148(3)(b), how much is my Christmas bonus in pounds?
GIVEN `an order specifies a larger sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State specified, by order, a larger sum than 10 pounds?
      `the sum the order specifies in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum does the order specify, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 148(3)(b), how much is my Christmas bonus in pounds` IS
    `s 148(3)(b) the amount of the payment in pounds` (IF `an order specifies a larger sum` THEN JUST `the sum the order specifies in pounds` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 148(5), is a further Christmas bonus payable in respect of me?
GIVEN `a sum has already been paid under section 148 in respect of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a sum already been paid under section 148 in respect of you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 148(5), is a further Christmas bonus payable in respect of me` IS
    `s 148(5) a further sum is payable in respect of the person` `a sum has already been paid under section 148 in respect of me`

@export Under section 150(1), is a payment I receive a qualifying benefit for the Christmas bonus?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `s 150(1) Kind of payment` @desc What kind of payment is it? (choose from the list)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 150(1), is a payment I receive a qualifying benefit for the Christmas bonus` IS
    `s 150(1) the payment is a qualifying benefit` `the kind of payment`

@export Under section 150(4), which is the relevant week for the Christmas bonus in a year?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc Which year? (for example 2025)
      `an order specifies another week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order specified another week instead of the first week in December?
      `the first day of that other week` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the other week begin?
      `the last day of that other week` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the other week end?
GIVETH A Period
DECIDE `Under section 150(4), which is the relevant week for the Christmas bonus in a year` IS
    `s 150(4) the relevant week` `the year` (IF `an order specifies another week` THEN JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of that other week`, `the last day` IS `the last day of that other week`) ELSE NOTHING)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc6 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4,
-- ss 151-171ZT (Parts XI, XII, 12ZA and 12ZB) -- LAYER 2, THE SEAT.
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in
-- Great Britain, here asking about statutory sick pay, statutory maternity pay, statutory paternity
-- pay and statutory adoption pay: whether they are entitled, how much, for how long, and what ends
-- or reduces it. The employer's seat is a separate layer that this file does not provide.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of ssc6-ssp, ssc6-smp, ssc6-spp and ssc6-sap as the questions that
-- person asks. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every question builds the modules'
-- records from plain answers (in its WHERE) and calls the module's rule. Every question's name begins
-- "Under section N," with the Act's own number.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes yes/no, a number or a date, one per fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked. A fact that another part of the Act or
-- another Act decides (section 6, section 172(a), section 173(a), Schedules 11 to 13, the Children
-- Act 1989) is asked as a yes/no answer, and the answer is passed on as `JUST` that answer.
-- A record field that the rule called never reads gets a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying so.
-- Figures the Act states in its own words are the modules' constants (26 weeks, 28 days, 52 weeks,
-- 8 weeks, 6 weeks, 90 per cent, 80 per cent, 123.25 pounds): an order or regulations that
-- substituted another figure would change these answers. Figures regulations or an order set (the
-- lower earnings limit, a prescribed weekly rate, the length of a pay period) are asked.
-- "Do regulations prescribe another period in your case?" and its like are asked wherever the Act
-- says "except as may be prescribed"; the default of the Act alone is the answer "no".
--
-- READING THE ANSWER. The answers are `MAYBE` values. `JUST FALSE` is the text's own "no". `NOTHING`
-- is "not covered" (the text leaves it to regulations, or is silent on this case) and is never a
-- "no": see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ssc6)".

§ `Statutory pay -- the questions of a person who works or claims (ss 151-171ZT)`

-- The employment the person describes. Placeholder fields: no rule called here reads the employee's
-- personal details or the kind of employer.
GIVEN contract IS A BOOLEAN
      office IS A BOOLEAN
      inGB IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Employment
`Under section 163, the employment I describe` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
        `sex` IS Woman
        `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057
    `the kind of employer` IS `an individual`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS contract
    `held in an office` IS office
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS inGB

§§ `Part XI -- Statutory Sick Pay (ss 151-163)`

-- Ask this group when you are, or have been, off work because of illness or disability.

@export Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day (ss 151, 153, 154)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to ask about?
      `I was unable that day to do the work I could reasonably be expected to do under my contract of service because of a specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On that day were you unable to do the work you could reasonably be expected to do under your contract of service, because of a specific disease or bodily or mental disablement?
      `regulations treat me as unable to work that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations treat you as unable to work on that day? (No, unless you know of such a rule that covers you.)
      `the first day of my period of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your period of entitlement to statutory sick pay (normally the first day of your period of incapacity for work)?
      `my period of entitlement has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your period of entitlement ended?
      `the last day of my period of entitlement` IS A DATE @desc If it has ended, what was its last day? (Any date if it has not ended.)
      `a circumstance in Schedule 11 stops a period of entitlement arising` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any circumstance specified in Schedule 11 to the Act stop a period of entitlement arising in your case?
      `my employer and I have agreed which days are qualifying days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer agreed which days of the week are qualifying days (the days you must be available for work)?
      `that day is one of the agreed days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that day one of the days you agreed?
      `regulations make that day a qualifying day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not agree, do regulations make that day a qualifying day for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 151, is my employer liable to pay me statutory sick pay for a day` IS
    `s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day`
        (`s 151(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to the contract of service` `I was unable that day to do the work I could reasonably be expected to do under my contract of service because of a specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` `regulations treat me as unable to work that day`)
        (`s 153(1) the first condition is satisfied` `the day I am asking about` `my period of entitlement` (JUST `a circumstance in Schedule 11 stops a period of entitlement arising`))
        (`s 154(1) the second condition is satisfied` (`s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` `my employer and I have agreed which days are qualifying days` `that day is one of the agreed days` (JUST `regulations make that day a qualifying day`)))
    WHERE
        `my period of entitlement` MEANS `s 153 Period of entitlement` WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my period of entitlement`
            `the last day` IS (IF `my period of entitlement has ended` THEN JUST `the last day of my period of entitlement` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Under section 151, is a term in my agreement with my employer void (s 151(2))?
GIVEN `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory sick pay rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to exclude, limit or otherwise change any provision of the statutory sick pay rules in Part XI?
      `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory sick pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to make you (or a former employee) pay, directly or indirectly, towards your employer's costs of paying statutory sick pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 151, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` IS
    `s 151(2) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory sick pay rules` `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory sick pay`

@export Under section 152, are my two periods of sickness treated as a single period of incapacity for work (s 152(3))?
GIVEN `the last day of my earlier period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your earlier period of incapacity for work?
      `the first day of my later period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc What was the first day of your later period of incapacity for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 152, are my two periods of sickness treated as a single period of incapacity for work` IS
    `s 152(3) the two periods of incapacity for work are treated as a single period` `the last day of my earlier period of incapacity for work` `the first day of my later period of incapacity for work` `s 152(3) the number of weeks specified in the Act`

@export Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end (s 153(2))?
GIVEN `my period of incapacity for work has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your period of incapacity for work ended?
      `the last day of my period of incapacity for work` IS A DATE @desc If it has, what was its last day? (Any date if not.)
      `I have reached my maximum entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached your maximum entitlement to statutory sick pay from this employer?
      `the day I reached my maximum entitlement` IS A DATE @desc If you have, on what day? (Any date if not.)
      `my contract of service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your contract of service expired or been brought to an end?
      `the day my contract of service ended` IS A DATE @desc If it has, on what day? (Any date if not.)
      `I am, or have been, pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, pregnant?
      `my disqualifying period has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are pregnant, has your maternity pay period or maternity allowance period begun, or is the day it will begin known?
      `the first day of my disqualifying period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first day of that period? (Any date if not.)
      `my pregnancy ended before that period began, other than by a confinement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your pregnancy end, before that period began, other than by a confinement (for example, a miscarriage before 24 weeks)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 153, on what day does my period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end` IS
    `s 153(2) the period of entitlement ends on`
        (IF `my period of incapacity for work has ended` THEN JUST `the last day of my period of incapacity for work` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `I have reached my maximum entitlement` THEN JUST `the day I reached my maximum entitlement` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my contract of service has ended` THEN JUST `the day my contract of service ended` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my disqualifying period has begun` THEN JUST (`the first day of my disqualifying period` MINUS 1) ELSE NOTHING)
        (`s 153(2)(d) the period of entitlement ends on the day before the disqualifying period` `I am, or have been, pregnant` (JUST `my pregnancy ended before that period began, other than by a confinement`))

@export Under section 154, is a day a qualifying day for me (s 154(2))?
GIVEN `my employer and I have agreed which days are qualifying days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer agreed which days of the week are qualifying days (the days you must be available for work)?
      `that day is one of the agreed days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day you ask about one of the days you agreed?
      `regulations make that day a qualifying day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did not agree, do regulations make that day a qualifying day for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 154, is a day a qualifying day for me` IS
    `s 154(2) the day is a qualifying day` `my employer and I have agreed which days are qualifying days` `that day is one of the agreed days` (JUST `regulations make that day a qualifying day`)

@export Under section 155, what is the most statutory sick pay my employer must pay me in one period of entitlement, in pounds (ss 155(4), 157(1))?
