    `s 161 Part XI applies to the person employed by or under the Crown` `I am employed by or under the Crown` `I serve as a member of Her Majesty's forces, in that capacity`

@export Under section 163, am I an employee for the purposes of statutory sick pay (s 163(1))?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my work is in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work carried on in Great Britain?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed?
      `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain?
      `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does section 172(a) of the Act treat that place as part of Great Britain?
      `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work paid with earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act?
      `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are not to be treated as an employee for this Part?
      `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are to be treated as an employee for this Part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 163, am I an employee for the purposes of statutory sick pay` IS
    `s 163(1) the person is an employee` (`Under section 163, the employment I describe` `I work under a contract of service` `I hold an office` `my work is in Great Britain`) `I am gainfully employed` `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` (JUST `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain`) `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee`

@export Under section 163, what are my normal weekly earnings for statutory sick pay, in pounds (s 163(2))?
GIVEN `the earnings paid to me or for my benefit under my contract of service in the relevant period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid to you, or for your benefit, under your contract of service with this employer in the relevant period, in pounds?
      `the number of weeks in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks are in the relevant period?
      `regulations require my normal weekly earnings to be calculated another way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations require your normal weekly earnings to be worked out another way in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 163, what are my normal weekly earnings for statutory sick pay` IS
    `s 163(2) the employee's normal weekly earnings in pounds` `the earnings paid to me or for my benefit under my contract of service in the relevant period, in pounds` `the number of weeks in the relevant period` `regulations require my normal weekly earnings to be calculated another way`

§§ `Part XII -- Statutory Maternity Pay (ss 164-171)`

-- Ask this group when you are pregnant, or have had a baby.

@export Under section 164, am I entitled to statutory maternity pay (s 164)?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my work is in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work carried on in Great Britain?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed?
      `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain?
      `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does section 172(a) of the Act treat that place as part of Great Britain?
      `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work paid with earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act?
      `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are not to be treated as an employee for this Part?
      `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are to be treated as an employee for this Part?
      `my employment with the employer is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job employed earner's employment?
      `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the 15th week before my baby is due` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks, without a break, had you worked for the employer by the end of the 15th week before your baby is due?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with the 15th week before your baby is due?
      `the lower earnings limit in force then, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the lower earnings limit, in pounds a week, in force immediately before the 14th week before your baby is due?
      `I have ceased to work for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped working for that employer?
      `I have become pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `I have reached the 11th week before the week my baby is due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached the start of the 11th week before the week your baby is due?
      `I was confined before reaching it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, did you have your baby (a confinement) before reaching it?
      `I gave notice of the date I expect to start getting maternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell the person who will pay you the date from which you expect them to start paying statutory maternity pay?
      `the number of days before that date on which I gave notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before that date did you give the notice?
      `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was fewer than 28 days, was it not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice?
      `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the notice as soon as was reasonably practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164, am I entitled to statutory maternity pay` IS
    `s 164(1) the woman is entitled to payments of statutory maternity pay`
        (`s 171(1) she is an employee` (`Under section 163, the employment I describe` `I work under a contract of service` `I hold an office` `my work is in Great Britain`) `I am gainfully employed` `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` (JUST `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain`) `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee`)
        (`s 164(2) the conditions mentioned in subsection (1) are satisfied`
            (`s 164(2)(a) she has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks and has ceased to work for him` `my service` `my employment with the employer is employed earner's employment` `I have ceased to work for the employer`)
            (`s 164(2)(b) her normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` `my service` `the lower earnings limit in force then, in pounds`)
            (`s 164(2)(c) she has become pregnant and has reached, or been confined before reaching, the commencement of the 11th week` `I have become pregnant` `I have reached the 11th week before the week my baby is due` `I was confined before reaching it`))
        (`s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` `I gave notice of the date I expect to start getting maternity pay` `the number of days before that date on which I gave notice` `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable`)
    WHERE
        `my service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
            `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the 15th week before my baby is due`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds`
            -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the last day of the relevant week.
            `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 164, have I given notice in time to be paid statutory maternity pay (s 164(4))?
GIVEN `I gave notice of the date I expect to start getting maternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell the person who will pay you the date from which you expect them to start paying statutory maternity pay?
      `the number of days before that date on which I gave notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before that date did you give the notice?
      `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was fewer than 28 days, was it not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice?
      `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the notice as soon as was reasonably practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164, have I given notice in time to be paid statutory maternity pay` IS
    `s 164(4) the notice condition for payments of statutory maternity pay is met` `I gave notice of the date I expect to start getting maternity pay` `the number of days before that date on which I gave notice` `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable`

@export Under section 164, is a term in my agreement with my employer void (s 164(6))?
GIVEN `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory maternity pay rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to exclude, limit or otherwise change any provision of the statutory maternity pay rules in Part XII?
      `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory maternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to make you (or a former employee) pay, directly or indirectly, towards your employer's costs of paying statutory maternity pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 164, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` IS
    `s 164(6) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory maternity pay rules` `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory maternity pay`

@export Under section 164, which week is the week my service and earnings are counted up to (s 164(2)(a), (b))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my baby is due` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the week (beginning with Sunday) in which your baby is expected to be born.
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe another period, in place of a week beginning with Sunday, for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 164, which week is the week my service and earnings are counted up to` IS
    `s 164 the relevant week` `a day in the week my baby is due` `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case`

@export Under section 165, on what day does my maternity pay period begin (s 165(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my baby is due` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the week (beginning with Sunday) in which your baby is expected to be born.
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe another period, in place of a week beginning with Sunday, for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 165, on what day does my maternity pay period begin` IS
    `s 165(2) the day on which the maternity pay period begins` (`s 171(1A) the first day of the week containing the day` `a day in the week my baby is due` `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case`)

@export Under section 165, what is my maternity pay period (s 165(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my maternity pay period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your maternity pay period begin?
      `the length of my maternity pay period in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is your maternity pay period (the Act allows at most 52)?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 165, what is my maternity pay period` IS
    `s 165(1) the maternity pay period` `the first day of my maternity pay period` `the length of my maternity pay period in weeks`

@export Under section 165, what is my maternity pay period if regulations have shortened it (s 165(3A))?
GIVEN `the first day of my maternity pay period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your maternity pay period begin?
      `the length of my maternity pay period before the reduction in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long was your maternity pay period before it was reduced?
      `the number of weeks to which regulations reduce it` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many weeks do regulations reduce it for you?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 165, what is my maternity pay period if regulations have shortened it` IS
    `s 165(3A) the maternity pay period as reduced` `the first day of my maternity pay period` `the length of my maternity pay period before the reduction in weeks` `the number of weeks to which regulations reduce it`

@export Under section 165, is statutory maternity pay payable to me for a week in which I work (s 165(4))?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of service with the person paying me in some part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, in any part of that week, under a contract of service with the person who pays you statutory maternity pay?
      `regulations prescribe my case as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 165, is statutory maternity pay payable to me for a week in which I work` IS
    `s 165(4) statutory maternity pay is payable by the person for the week` `I work under a contract of service with the person paying me in some part of the week` `regulations prescribe my case as an exception`

@export Under section 166, what is my weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for a week, in pounds (s 166(1))?
GIVEN `the number of the week, counting the first week I am paid as week 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of your maternity pay do you ask about (the first week you are paid is week 1)?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to the 15th week before my baby is due, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with the 15th week before your baby is due?
      `the weekly rate regulations prescribe, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate, in pounds, do regulations prescribe for the weeks after the first six?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 166, what is my weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for a week` IS
    `s 166(1) the weekly rate of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` `the number of the week, counting the first week I am paid as week 1` `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to the 15th week before my baby is due, in pounds` `the weekly rate regulations prescribe, in pounds`

@export Under section 169, do the statutory maternity pay rules apply to me as someone employed by the Crown (s 169)?
GIVEN `I am employed by or under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by or under the Crown?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 169, do the statutory maternity pay rules apply to me as someone employed by the Crown` IS
    `s 169 Part XII applies to the woman as it applies to women employed otherwise than by or under the Crown` `I am employed by or under the Crown`

@export Under section 171, am I treated as confined (s 171(1))?
GIVEN `the weeks of pregnancy when my labour began` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many weeks of pregnancy did your labour begin?
      `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your labour result in the issue of a living child?
      `my labour resulted in the issue of a child, alive or dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your labour result in the issue of a child, alive or dead?
