            `labour resulted in the issue of a living child` IS `my labour resulted in the issue of a living child`
            -- Placeholder: s 171(1) she is confined does not read the day of the issue.
            `the day of the issue of the child, or of the last of the children` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 171, what are my normal weekly earnings for statutory maternity pay, in pounds (s 171(4))?
GIVEN `the earnings paid to me or for my benefit under my contract of service in the relevant period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid to you, or for your benefit, under your contract of service with this employer in the relevant period, in pounds?
      `the number of weeks in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks are in the relevant period?
      `regulations require my normal weekly earnings to be calculated another way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations require your normal weekly earnings to be worked out another way in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171, what are my normal weekly earnings for statutory maternity pay` IS
    `s 171(4) her normal weekly earnings in pounds` `the earnings paid to me or for my benefit under my contract of service in the relevant period, in pounds` `the number of weeks in the relevant period` `regulations require my normal weekly earnings to be calculated another way`

§§ `Part 12ZA -- Statutory Paternity Pay (ss 171ZA-171ZK)`

-- Ask this group when you are the father of a newborn child, or the partner of the child's mother,
-- or when a child is being placed for adoption with you or your partner.

@export Under section 171ZA, am I entitled to statutory paternity pay on the birth of a child (s 171ZA)?
GIVEN `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the newborn child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions regulations prescribe about your relationship with the newborn child?
      `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the child's mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions regulations prescribe about your relationship with the child's mother?
      `my job is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job employed earner's employment?
      `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks, without a break, had you worked for the employer by the end of the 15th week before the week your baby is due?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with that week?
      `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the lower earnings limit, in pounds a week, at the end of that week?
      `I stayed in employment with that employer from the end of that week to the day my child was born` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay in employment with that employer from the end of that week until the day the child was born?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZA, am I entitled to statutory paternity pay on the birth of a child` IS
    `s 171ZA(1) he is entitled to statutory paternity pay on a birth`
        (`s 171ZA(2) the conditions are satisfied`
            (`s 171ZA(2)(a) he satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with a newborn child and with the child's mother` `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the newborn child` `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the child's mother`)
            (`s 171ZA(2)(b) he has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week` `my service` `my job is employed earner's employment`)
            (`s 171ZA(2)(c) his normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit at the end of the relevant week` `my service` `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds`)
            (`s 171ZA(2)(d) he has been in employed earner's employment with that employer from the end of the relevant week to the day the child is born` `I stayed in employment with that employer from the end of that week to the day my child was born`))
    WHERE
        `my service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
            `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds`
            -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the last day of the relevant week.
            `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 171ZA, which week is the relevant week for statutory paternity pay on a birth (s 171ZA(3))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my child is due` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the week (beginning with Sunday) in which the child is expected to be born.
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe another period, in place of a week beginning with Sunday, for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 171ZA, which week is the relevant week for statutory paternity pay on a birth` IS
    `s 171ZA(2) the relevant week` `a day in the week my child is due` `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case`

@export Under section 171ZB, am I entitled to statutory paternity pay on the adoption of a child (s 171ZB)?
GIVEN `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the child placed for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions regulations prescribe about your relationship with the child placed for adoption?
      `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the person with whom the child is placed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions regulations prescribe about your relationship with the person with whom the child is placed?
      `the child is placed with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with you (answer no if it is placed with your partner)?
      `my job is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job employed earner's employment?
      `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks, without a break, had you worked for the employer by the end of the week in which the adopter was told of the match?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with that week?
      `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the lower earnings limit, in pounds a week, at the end of that week?
      `I stayed in employment with that employer from the end of that week to the day the child was placed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay in employment with that employer from the end of that week until the day the child was placed for adoption?
      `I have elected to receive statutory paternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected to receive statutory paternity pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZB, am I entitled to statutory paternity pay on the adoption of a child` IS
    `s 171ZB(1) he is entitled to statutory paternity pay on an adoption`
        (`s 171ZB(2) the conditions are satisfied`
            (`s 171ZB(2)(a) he satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child and with the person with whom the child is placed` `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the child placed for adoption` `I satisfy the prescribed conditions about my relationship with the person with whom the child is placed`)
            (`s 171ZB(2)(b) he has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week` `my service` `my job is employed earner's employment`)
            (`s 171ZB(2)(c) his normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit at the end of the relevant week` `my service` `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds`)
            (`s 171ZB(2)(d) he has been in employed earner's employment with that employer from the end of the relevant week to the day the child is placed` `I stayed in employment with that employer from the end of that week to the day the child was placed`)
            (`s 171ZB(2)(e) where he is a person with whom the child is placed, he has elected to receive statutory paternity pay` `my relationship to the placement` `I have elected to receive statutory paternity pay`))
    WHERE
        `my relationship to the placement` MEANS
            IF `the child is placed with me`
            THEN `s 171ZB the person with whom the child is placed`
            ELSE `s 171ZB the partner of the person with whom the child is placed`
        `my service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
            `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds`
            -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the last day of the relevant week.
            `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 171ZB, may I elect to receive statutory paternity pay (s 171ZB(4))?
GIVEN `I have elected to receive statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected to receive statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZB, may I elect to receive statutory paternity pay` IS
    `s 171ZB(4) he may elect to receive statutory paternity pay` `I have elected to receive statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL`

@export Under section 171ZC, have I given notice that I expect to be paid statutory paternity pay (s 171ZC(1))?
GIVEN `I gave the person who will pay me notice of the week or weeks for which I expect statutory paternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the person who will pay you notice of the week or weeks for which you expect to be paid statutory paternity pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZC, have I given notice that I expect to be paid statutory paternity pay` IS
    `s 171ZC(1) the notice condition for payments of statutory paternity pay is met` `I gave the person who will pay me notice of the week or weeks for which I expect statutory paternity pay`

@export Under section 171ZE, what is my daily rate of statutory paternity pay, in pounds (s 171ZE(10A))?
GIVEN `my weekly rate of statutory paternity pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of statutory paternity pay, in pounds (the rate regulations prescribe)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZE, what is my daily rate of statutory paternity pay` IS
    `s 171ZE(10A) the daily rate of statutory paternity pay in pounds` `my weekly rate of statutory paternity pay in pounds`

@export Under section 171ZE, may I be paid statutory paternity pay for a week (s 171ZE(3A), (4), (7))?
GIVEN `I am paid, or take leave, under the shared parental rules in part of that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is statutory shared parental pay payable to you for part of that week, or do you take shared parental leave in part of it?
      `I was paid, or took leave, under the shared parental rules for this child before that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was statutory shared parental pay payable to you, or did you take shared parental leave, in respect of this child before that week?
      `at the beginning of the week it is my purpose to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the beginning of the week, is it your purpose to care for the child?
      `at the beginning of the week it is my purpose to support the other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the beginning of the week, is it your purpose to support the child's mother (or the adopter)?
      `I work in part of that week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, in part of that week, for an employer who is not liable to pay you statutory paternity pay?
      `regulations prescribe my case as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to the rule about working for another employer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZE, may I be paid statutory paternity pay for a week` IS
    `s 171ZA(1) all of these answers hold`
        (LIST (`s 171ZE(3A) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` `I am paid, or take leave, under the shared parental rules in part of that week` `I was paid, or took leave, under the shared parental rules for this child before that week`),
              (`s 171ZE(4) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` `at the beginning of the week it is my purpose to care for the child` `at the beginning of the week it is my purpose to support the other person`),
              (`s 171ZE(7) statutory paternity pay is payable to him in respect of the statutory pay week` `I work in part of that week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` `regulations prescribe my case as an exception`))

@export Under section 171ZF, is a term in my agreement with my employer void (s 171ZF(1))?
GIVEN `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory paternity pay rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to exclude, limit or otherwise change any provision of the statutory paternity pay rules in Part 12ZA?
      `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory paternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to make you (or a former employee) pay, directly or indirectly, towards your employer's costs of paying statutory paternity pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZF, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` IS
    `s 171ZF(1) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory paternity pay rules` `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory paternity pay`

@export Under section 171ZG, how much statutory paternity pay is still owed to me for a period after my contractual pay, in pounds (s 171ZG(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my employer's liability to pay statutory paternity pay for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much statutory paternity pay does your employer owe you for the period, in pounds?
      `the contractual pay my employer has paid me for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much contractual pay (pay under your contract of service) has your employer paid you for the same period, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZG, how much statutory paternity pay is still owed to me for a period after my contractual pay` IS
    `s 171ZG(2)(a) the statutory paternity pay still owed for the period in pounds` `my employer's liability to pay statutory paternity pay for the period, in pounds` `the contractual pay my employer has paid me for the same period, in pounds`

§§ `Part 12ZB -- Statutory Adoption Pay (ss 171ZL-171ZT)`

-- Ask this group when a child is being placed with you for adoption.

@export Under section 171ZL, am I entitled to statutory adoption pay (s 171ZL)?
GIVEN `a child is, or is expected to be, placed with me for adoption in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed, or expected to be placed, with you for adoption under the law of any part of the United Kingdom?
      `I work under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work under a contract of service?
      `I hold an office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you hold an office (including an elective office)?
      `my work is in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work carried on in Great Britain?
      `I am gainfully employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you gainfully employed?
      `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work done in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain?
      `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does section 172(a) of the Act treat that place as part of Great Britain?
      `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your work paid with earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act?
      `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are not to be treated as an employee for this Part?
      `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations say you are to be treated as an employee for this Part?
      `my job is employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your job employed earner's employment?
      `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks, without a break, had you worked for the employer by the end of the week in which you were told you had been matched with the child?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with that week?
      `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the lower earnings limit, in pounds a week, at the end of that week?
      `I have ceased to work for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped working for that employer?
      `I have elected to receive statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected to receive statutory adoption pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZL, am I entitled to statutory adoption pay` IS
    `s 171ZL(1) he is entitled to statutory adoption pay`
        (`s 171ZS(2) the person is an employee` (`Under section 163, the employment I describe` `I work under a contract of service` `I hold an office` `my work is in Great Britain`) `I am gainfully employed` `my work is in the territorial waters adjacent to Great Britain` (JUST `section 172(a) treats that place as part of Great Britain`) `I am paid earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5 of the Act` `regulations say I am not to be treated as an employee` `regulations say I am to be treated as an employee`)
        (`s 171ZL(2) the conditions are satisfied`
            (`s 171ZL(2)(a) he is a person with whom a child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption` `a child is, or is expected to be, placed with me for adoption in the United Kingdom`)
            (`s 171ZL(2)(b) he has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week` `my service` `my job is employed earner's employment`)
            (`s 171ZL(2)(c) he has ceased to work for the employer` `I have ceased to work for the employer`)
            (`s 171ZL(2)(d) his normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit at the end of the relevant week` `my service` `the lower earnings limit in force at the end of that week, in pounds`)
            (`s 171ZL(2)(e) he has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` `I have elected to receive statutory adoption pay`))
    WHERE
        `my service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
            `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS `the weeks I have worked for the employer without a break up to the relevant week`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to that week, in pounds`
            -- Placeholder: no rule called here reads the last day of the relevant week.
            `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 171ZL, which week is the relevant week for statutory adoption pay (s 171ZL(3))?
GIVEN `the day I was told I had been matched with the child` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you told you had been matched with the child (or, for a placement under section 22C or section 81, that the child is to be placed with you)?
      `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe another period, in place of a week beginning with Sunday, for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 171ZL, which week is the relevant week for statutory adoption pay` IS
    `s 171ZL(2) the relevant week` `my placement` `regulations prescribe another period in place of a week beginning with Sunday for my case`
    WHERE
        `my placement` MEANS Placement WITH
            -- Placeholder: s 171ZL(2) the relevant week reads only the day he was told of the match.
            `the kind of placement` IS `placed for adoption under the law of a part of the United Kingdom`
            `the day the person was notified of the match` IS `the day I was told I had been matched with the child`
            -- Placeholder: s 171ZL(2) the relevant week does not read the day of the placement.
            `the day the child was or is expected to be placed` IS `the day I was told I had been matched with the child`

@export Under section 171ZL, may I elect to receive statutory adoption pay (s 171ZL(4))?
GIVEN `I have elected to receive statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected to receive statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB?
      `the child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child, or is the child expected to be, placed for adoption with you?
      `the adoption is under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the adoption (or expected adoption) under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland?
      `the adoption is under the law of Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the adoption (or expected adoption) under the law of Scotland?
      `I am a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland: are you a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002?
      `I am a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is under the law of Scotland: are you a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007?
      `the other member of the couple is a person to whom the conditions in section 171ZL(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other member of the couple a person to whom the conditions in section 171ZL(2) apply?
      `the other member of the couple has elected to receive statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other member of the couple elected to receive statutory adoption pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZL, may I elect to receive statutory adoption pay` IS
    `s 171ZL(4) he may elect to receive statutory adoption pay` `I have elected to receive statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB`
        (`s 171ZL(4A) he falls within the subsection` `the child is, or is expected to be, placed for adoption with me`
            (`s 171ZL(4B) he is a member of a couple` `the law of my adoption` (JUST `I am a member of a couple within the meaning of section 144(4) of the Adoption and Children Act 2002`) (JUST `I am a member of a relevant couple within the meaning of section 29(3) of the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007`))
            `the other member of the couple is a person to whom the conditions in section 171ZL(2) apply` `the other member of the couple has elected to receive statutory adoption pay`)
    WHERE
        `the law of my adoption` MEANS
            IF `the adoption is under the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland`
            THEN `s 171ZL(4B) the law of England and Wales or Northern Ireland`
            ELSE IF `the adoption is under the law of Scotland`
                 THEN `s 171ZL(4B) the law of Scotland`
                 ELSE `s 171ZL(4B) the law of another place`

@export Under section 171ZL, have I given notice in time to be paid statutory adoption pay (s 171ZL(6))?
GIVEN `I gave the person who will pay me notice of the date I expect to start getting adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the person who will pay you notice of the date from which you expect them to start paying statutory adoption pay?
      `the day I gave the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the notice?
      `the date from which I expect payment to begin` IS A DATE @desc What is the date from which you expect the payments to begin?
      `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you gave it fewer than 28 days before that date, was it not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice?
      `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the notice as soon as was reasonably practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZL, have I given notice in time to be paid statutory adoption pay` IS
    `s 171ZL(6) the notice condition for payments of statutory adoption pay is met`
        (`s 171ZL(6)(a) he gives the notice of the date the liability is to begin` `I gave the person who will pay me notice of the date I expect to start getting adoption pay`)
        (`s 171ZL(6)(b) the notice is given at least 28 days before that date or, if that is not reasonably practicable, as soon as is reasonably practicable` `the day I gave the notice` `the date from which I expect payment to begin` `it was not reasonably practicable to give 28 days' notice` `I gave notice as soon as was reasonably practicable`)

@export Under section 171ZN, what is my adoption pay period (s 171ZN(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my adoption pay period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your adoption pay period begin?
      `the length of my adoption pay period in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is your adoption pay period (the Act allows at most 52)?
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
DECIDE `Under section 171ZN, what is my adoption pay period` IS
    `s 171ZN(2) the adoption pay period` `the first day of my adoption pay period` `the length of my adoption pay period in weeks`

@export Under section 171ZN, what is my weekly rate of statutory adoption pay for a week, in pounds (s 171ZN(2E))?
GIVEN `the number of the week, counting the first week I am paid as week 1` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of your adoption pay do you ask about (the first week you are paid is week 1)?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to the week I was told of the match, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your average weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with the week in which you were told you had been matched with the child?
      `the weekly rate regulations prescribe, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate, in pounds, do regulations prescribe for the weeks after the first six?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZN, what is my weekly rate of statutory adoption pay for a week` IS
    `s 171ZN(2E) the weekly rate of statutory adoption pay for the week in pounds` `the number of the week, counting the first week I am paid as week 1` `my service` `the weekly rate regulations prescribe, in pounds`
    WHERE
        `my service` MEANS `Service for statutory pay` WITH
            -- Placeholder: s 171ZN(2E) does not read the weeks of continuous employment.
            `weeks of continuous employment with the employer ending with the relevant week` IS 0
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds over the period the section names` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks up to the week I was told of the match, in pounds`
            -- Placeholder: s 171ZN(2E) does not read the last day of the relevant week.
            `the last day of the relevant week` IS Date 1 1 2026

@export Under section 171ZN, is statutory adoption pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer (s 171ZN(5))?
GIVEN `I work in part of that week for an employer who is not liable to pay me statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, in part of that week, for an employer who is not liable to pay you statutory adoption pay?
      `regulations prescribe my case as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZN, is statutory adoption pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer` IS
    `s 171ZN(5) statutory adoption pay is payable to him in respect of the week` `I work in part of that week for an employer who is not liable to pay me statutory adoption pay` `regulations prescribe my case as an exception`

@export Under section 171ZO, is a term in my agreement with my employer void (s 171ZO(1))?
GIVEN `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory adoption pay rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to exclude, limit or otherwise change any provision of the statutory adoption pay rules in Part 12ZB?
      `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory adoption pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term try to make you (or a former employee) pay, directly or indirectly, towards your employer's costs of paying statutory adoption pay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZO, is a term in my agreement with my employer void` IS
    `s 171ZO(1) the agreement is void to the extent that it purports` `the term tries to exclude, limit or change any provision of the statutory adoption pay rules` `the term tries to make me pay towards my employer's costs of statutory adoption pay`

@export Under section 171ZP, how much statutory adoption pay is still owed to me for a week after my contractual pay, in pounds (s 171ZP(5)(a))?
GIVEN `my employer's liability to pay statutory adoption pay for the week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much statutory adoption pay does your employer owe you for the week, in pounds?
      `the contractual pay my employer has paid me for the same week, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much contractual pay (pay under your contract of service) has your employer paid you for the same week, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZP, how much statutory adoption pay is still owed to me for a week after my contractual pay` IS
    `s 171ZP(5)(a) the statutory adoption pay still owed for the week in pounds` `my employer's liability to pay statutory adoption pay for the week, in pounds` `the contractual pay my employer has paid me for the same week, in pounds`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc7 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for lines 3718-4330:
-- Part 12ZC (statutory shared parental pay), Part 12ZD (statutory parental bereavement pay), Part 12ZE (statutory neonatal
-- care pay) and Part XIIA (incapacity for work).
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a benefit or statutory pay in Great Britain.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the four modules imported above as the questions that person asks about
-- their own pay, leave and incapacity. Nothing here is new law.  The source text is a converter rendering, not the official text.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own short lists of choices), one for
-- each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked.  The records the modules expect are
-- built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated.
-- A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment.
-- The figures that regulations or an order supply (the lower earnings limit, the prescribed weeks and lengths) are asked as
-- numbers; the question for each says so.  Whether regulations exist that give an entitlement (the "gate" of ss 171ZU, 171ZV)
-- is asked as a yes/no, because the Act's text alone does not give the entitlement.
-- Every question answers MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE NUMBER where the module does: NOTHING means "the text alone does not answer",
-- never "no".  A caller must not turn it into "no".
-- The questions of the Parts about people who are not the seat (the employer, the Commissioners) appear only as what they mean for the person.
-- Questions are named "Under section N, ..." with the Act's own numbering.

§ `Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 -- the questions of a person who works or claims, lines 3718-4330`

§§ `Statutory shared parental pay (Part 12ZC)`

-- The groups below arise only when the person is a parent of a new baby or an adopted child.

-- s 171ZU(1) and (2). Regulations may provide that the mother is entitled where all of the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied.
-- The conditions are the facts below; "prescribed" ones are what the regulations say, stated by you.
@export Under section 171ZU(1), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the mother of the child?
GIVEN `my case: (a) the claimant mother and P satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I and my partner satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child?
      `my case: (b)(i) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment?
      `my case: (b)(ii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period?
      `my case: (b)(iii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with me?
      `my case: (c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you been in continuous employed earner's employment with the same employer, up to the end of the week that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of continuous employment do the regulations prescribe for this entitlement?
      `my case: (d) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the end of that prescribed week I was entitled to be in that employment?
      `my case: (e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the period that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (f) the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I continue in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (g) the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child?
      `my case: (h) the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I satisfy prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period?
      `my case: (i)(i) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised?
      `my case: (i)(ii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I intend to claim?
      `my case: (i)(iii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which my partner intends to claim?
      `my case: (j) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which I intend to claim?
      `my case: (k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed?
      `my case: (k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content?
      `my case: (l) P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner consents to the extent of my intended claim?
      `my case: (m) it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is my intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (n) the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I am absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996?
      `my case: (o) the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the time? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations made under section 171ZU(1) provide that the mother is entitled to statutory shared parental pay where all the conditions are satisfied?
      `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations disapply a condition above in your case, or apply it with modifications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(1), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the mother of the child` IS
    `s 171ZU(1) the claimant mother is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` `my case` `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZU(2) the claimant mother's case` OF `my case: (a) the claimant mother and P satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`, `my case: (b)(i) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`, `my case: (b)(ii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`, `my case: (b)(iii) P satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with the claimant mother`, `my case: (c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`, `my case: (d) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant mother was entitled to be in that employment`, `my case: (e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (f) the claimant mother continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (g) the claimant mother became entitled to statutory maternity pay by reference to the birth of the child`, `my case: (h) the claimant mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period`, `my case: (i)(i) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`, `my case: (i)(ii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks she intends to claim`, `my case: (i)(iii) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which P intends to claim`, `my case: (j) the claimant mother has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which she intends to claim`, `my case: (k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed`, `my case: (k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`, `my case: (l) P consents to the extent of the claimant mother's intended claim`, `my case: (m) it is the claimant mother's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her`, `my case: (n) the claimant mother is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to her`, `my case: (o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`, `my case: (o) the claimant mother's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`

-- s 171ZU(3) and (4). The same, for a person who is not the mother (called the claimant), by reference to the mother (called M).
@export Under section 171ZU(3), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the mother's partner or the child's other parent?
GIVEN `my case: (a) the claimant and M satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I and the mother satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child?
      `my case: (b)(i) the claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I satisfy prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child?
      `my case: (b)(ii) the claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with M` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I satisfy prescribed conditions as to relationship with the mother?
      `my case: (c)(i) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment?
      `my case: (c)(ii) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period?
      `my case: (d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you been in continuous employed earner's employment with the same employer, up to the end of the week that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of continuous employment do the regulations prescribe for this entitlement?
      `my case: (e) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the end of that prescribed week I was entitled to be in that employment?
      `my case: (f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the period that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (g) the claimant continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I continue in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (h)(i) M became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to a maternity allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to a maternity allowance?
      `my case: (h)(ii) M became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to statutory maternity pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to statutory maternity pay?
      `my case: (i)(i) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity allowance period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity allowance period?
      `my case: (i)(ii) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period?
      `my case: (j)(i) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks the claimant would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised?
      `my case: (j)(ii) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks the claimant intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I intend to claim?
      `my case: (j)(iii) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which M intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which the mother intends to claim?
      `my case: (k) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which the claimant intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which I intend to claim?
      `my case: (l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed?
      `my case: (l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content?
      `my case: (m) M consents to the extent of the claimant's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the mother consents to the extent of my intended claim?
      `my case: (n) it is the claimant's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is my intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (o) the claimant is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I am absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996?
      `my case: (p) the claimant's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the time? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations made under section 171ZU(3) provide that you are entitled to statutory shared parental pay where all the conditions are satisfied?
      `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations disapply a condition above in your case, or apply it with modifications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(3), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the mother's partner or the child's other parent` IS
    `s 171ZU(3) the claimant is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` `my case` `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZU(4) the claimant's case` OF `my case: (a) the claimant and M satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`, `my case: (b)(i) the claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child`, `my case: (b)(ii) the claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with M`, `my case: (c)(i) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`, `my case: (c)(ii) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`, `my case: (d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`, `my case: (e) at the end of that prescribed week the claimant was entitled to be in that employment`, `my case: (f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (g) the claimant continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (h)(i) M became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to a maternity allowance`, `my case: (h)(ii) M became entitled, by reference to the birth of the child, to statutory maternity pay`, `my case: (i)(i) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity allowance period`, `my case: (i)(ii) M satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the maternity pay period`, `my case: (j)(i) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks the claimant would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`, `my case: (j)(ii) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks the claimant intends to claim`, `my case: (j)(iii) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which M intends to claim`, `my case: (k) the claimant has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which the claimant intends to claim`, `my case: (l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed`, `my case: (l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`, `my case: (m) M consents to the extent of the claimant's intended claim`, `my case: (n) it is the claimant's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to the claimant`, `my case: (o) the claimant is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to the claimant`, `my case: (p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`, `my case: (p) the claimant's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`

-- s 171ZU(6), (7), (8). The most weeks of statutory shared parental pay: the weeks of the maternity pay period or maternity allowance period,
-- less the weeks used by an early return to work (the greater of the relevant weeks and the prescribed number), or less the weeks to which
-- the period was reduced.  A part of a week counts as a week.  The rule reads only the period that matches the kind of payment, so the one period is passed for both.
@export Under section 171ZU(6), what is the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay I can claim after maternity pay or allowance?
GIVEN `the mother was paid` IS A `s 171ZU(6) kind of maternity payment` @desc Was the mother paid maternity allowance or statutory maternity pay?
      `my maternity pay or allowance period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the maternity pay period (or maternity allowance period) begin?
      `my maternity pay or allowance period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does that period end?
      `I took action treated as my return to work without meeting the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take action that regulations treat as your return to work, without meeting the conditions the regulations prescribe for it?
      `relevant weeks of pay before my return to work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many relevant weeks of maternity pay or allowance were payable to you before that action? (0 if you took no such action)
      `the number of weeks the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of weeks do the regulations prescribe as the least that counts when you return to work early? (0 if none)
      `the weeks to which the period was reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many weeks was the period reduced under section 35(3A) or 165(3A)? (0 if it was not reduced)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(6), what is the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay I can claim after maternity pay or allowance` IS
    `s 171ZU(6) the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay` `the mother was paid` `my period` `my period` `I took action treated as my return to work without meeting the prescribed conditions` `relevant weeks of pay before my return to work` `the number of weeks the regulations prescribe` `the weeks to which the period was reduced` `the weeks to which the period was reduced`
    WHERE
        `my period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `my maternity pay or allowance period begins`
            `the last day` IS `my maternity pay or allowance period ends`

-- s 171ZV(6), (7), (8). The same for adoption pay: the weeks of the adoption pay period, less the weeks used by an early return to work, or less the weeks to which the period was reduced under section 171ZN(2A).
@export Under section 171ZV(6), what is the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay I can claim after adoption pay?
GIVEN `my adoption pay period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the adoption pay period begin?
      `my adoption pay period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the adoption pay period end?
      `I took action treated as my return to work without meeting the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you take action that regulations treat as your return to work, without meeting the conditions the regulations prescribe for it?
      `relevant weeks of adoption pay before my return to work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many relevant weeks of adoption pay were payable to you before that action? (0 if you took no such action)
      `the number of weeks the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What number of weeks do the regulations prescribe as the least that counts when you return to work early? (0 if none)
      `the weeks to which the period was reduced` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many weeks was the adoption pay period reduced under section 171ZN(2A)? (0 if it was not reduced)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZV(6), what is the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay I can claim after adoption pay` IS
    `s 171ZV(6) the greatest number of weeks of statutory shared parental pay` `my adoption pay period` `I took action treated as my return to work without meeting the prescribed conditions` `relevant weeks of adoption pay before my return to work` `the number of weeks the regulations prescribe` `the weeks to which the period was reduced`
    WHERE
        `my adoption pay period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `my adoption pay period begins`
            `the last day` IS `my adoption pay period ends`

-- s 171ZV(1) and (2). Regulations may provide that claimant A, a person who has been matched or placed with a child for adoption, is entitled where all of the conditions in subsection (2) are satisfied.
@export Under section 171ZV(1), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the first adopter of the child?
GIVEN `my case: (a) claimant A and X satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I and my partner satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child?
      `my case: (b)(i) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment?
      `my case: (b)(ii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period?
      `my case: (b)(iii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with me?
      `my case: (c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you been in continuous employed earner's employment with the same employer, up to the end of the week that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of continuous employment do the regulations prescribe for this entitlement?
      `my case: (d) at the end of that prescribed week claimant A was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the end of that prescribed week I was entitled to be in that employment?
      `my case: (e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the period that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (f) claimant A continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I continue in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (g) claimant A became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child?
      `my case: (h) claimant A satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I satisfy prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period?
      `my case: (i)(i) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised?
      `my case: (i)(ii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I intend to claim?
      `my case: (i)(iii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which X intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which my partner intends to claim?
      `my case: (j) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant A intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which I intend to claim?
      `my case: (k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed?
      `my case: (k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content?
      `my case: (l) X consents to the extent of claimant A's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my partner consents to the extent of my intended claim?
      `my case: (m) it is claimant A's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is my intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (n) claimant A is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I am absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996?
      `my case: (o) claimant A's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the time? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations made under section 171ZV(1) provide that you are entitled to statutory shared parental pay where all the conditions are satisfied?
      `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations disapply a condition above in your case, or apply it with modifications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZV(1), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the first adopter of the child` IS
    `s 171ZV(1) claimant A is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` `my case` `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZV(2) the claimant A's case` OF `my case: (a) claimant A and X satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`, `my case: (b)(i) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`, `my case: (b)(ii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`, `my case: (b)(iii) X satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship either with the child or with claimant A`, `my case: (c) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (c) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`, `my case: (d) at the end of that prescribed week claimant A was entitled to be in that employment`, `my case: (e) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (f) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (f) claimant A continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (g) claimant A became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child`, `my case: (h) claimant A satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period`, `my case: (i)(i) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`, `my case: (i)(ii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant A intends to claim`, `my case: (i)(iii) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which X intends to claim`, `my case: (j) claimant A has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant A intends to claim`, `my case: (k)(i) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) is given by such time as may be prescribed`, `my case: (k)(ii) a notice under paragraph (i) or (j) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`, `my case: (l) X consents to the extent of claimant A's intended claim`, `my case: (m) it is claimant A's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A`, `my case: (n) claimant A is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant A`, `my case: (o) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`, `my case: (o) claimant A's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`

-- s 171ZV(3) and (4). The same, for claimant B, by reference to the other adopter Y.
@export Under section 171ZV(3), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the second adopter of the child?
GIVEN `my case: (a) claimant B and Y satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I and the other claimant satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child?
