      `my case: (b)(ii) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with Y` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I satisfy prescribed conditions as to relationship with the other claimant?
      `my case: (c)(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment?
      `my case: (c)(ii) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period?
      `my case: (d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you been in continuous employed earner's employment with the same employer, up to the end of the week that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of continuous employment do the regulations prescribe for this entitlement?
      `my case: (e) at the end of that prescribed week claimant B was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that at the end of that prescribed week I was entitled to be in that employment?
      `my case: (f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the period that the regulations prescribe?
      `my case: (g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (g) claimant B continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I continue in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time?
      `my case: (h) Y became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other claimant became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child?
      `my case: (i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other claimant satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period?
      `my case: (j)(i) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised?
      `my case: (j)(ii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks I intend to claim?
      `my case: (j)(iii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which Y intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which the other claimant intends to claim?
      `my case: (k) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant B intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I have given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which I intend to claim?
      `my case: (l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed?
      `my case: (l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content?
      `my case: (m) Y consents to the extent of claimant B's intended claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the other claimant consents to the extent of my intended claim?
      `my case: (n) it is claimant B's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is my intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (o) claimant B is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that I am absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to me?
      `my case: (p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996?
      `my case: (p) claimant B's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that my absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the time? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations made under section 171ZV(3) provide that you are entitled to statutory shared parental pay where all the conditions are satisfied?
      `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations disapply a condition above in your case, or apply it with modifications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZV(3), am I entitled to statutory shared parental pay as the second adopter of the child` IS
    `s 171ZV(3) claimant B is entitled to statutory shared parental pay` `my case` `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `regulations provide that I am entitled where the conditions are satisfied` `regulations disapply or modify a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZV(4) the claimant B's case` OF `my case: (a) claimant B and Y satisfy prescribed conditions as to caring or intending to care for the child`, `my case: (b)(i) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child`, `my case: (b)(ii) claimant B satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with Y`, `my case: (c)(i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to employment or self-employment`, `my case: (c)(ii) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to having earnings of a prescribed amount for a prescribed period`, `my case: (d) weeks of continuous employment ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (d) the prescribed length of continuous employment in weeks`, `my case: (e) at the end of that prescribed week claimant B was entitled to be in that employment`, `my case: (f) normal weekly earnings in pounds for the prescribed period ending with the prescribed week`, `my case: (g) regulations so provide that the person continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (g) claimant B continues in employed earner's employment until a prescribed time`, `my case: (h) Y became entitled to statutory adoption pay by reference to the placement for adoption of the child`, `my case: (i) Y satisfies prescribed conditions as to the reduction of the duration of the adoption pay period`, `my case: (j)(i) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B would be entitled to claim if the entitlement were fully exercised`, `my case: (j)(ii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks claimant B intends to claim`, `my case: (j)(iii) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the number of weeks in respect of which Y intends to claim`, `my case: (k) claimant B has given the person who will be liable to pay notice of the period or periods during which claimant B intends to claim`, `my case: (l)(i) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) is given by such time as may be prescribed`, `my case: (l)(ii) a notice under paragraph (j) or (k) satisfies prescribed conditions as to form and content`, `my case: (m) Y consents to the extent of claimant B's intended claim`, `my case: (n) it is claimant B's intention to care for the child during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B`, `my case: (o) claimant B is absent from work during each week in respect of which the pay is paid to claimant B`, `my case: (p) the person is an employee within the meaning of the Employment Rights Act 1996`, `my case: (p) claimant B's absence from work during each such week is absence on shared parental leave`

-- s 171ZU(11). No payment of statutory shared parental pay may be made to the mother of the child before the end of her maternity pay period.
@export Under section 171ZU(11), may a payment of shared parental pay be made to me before my maternity pay period has ended?
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the payment of shared parental pay be made?
      `my maternity pay period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your maternity pay period begin?
      `my maternity pay period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your maternity pay period end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(11), may a payment of shared parental pay be made to me before my maternity pay period has ended` IS
    `s 171ZU(11) a payment may be made to the mother` `the day of the payment` `my maternity pay period`
    WHERE
        `my maternity pay period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `my maternity pay period begins`
            `the last day` IS `my maternity pay period ends`

-- s 171ZV(11). The same for a person who became entitled to statutory adoption pay: no payment before the end of the adoption pay period.
@export Under section 171ZV(11), may a payment of shared parental pay be made to me before my adoption pay period has ended?
GIVEN `the day of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the payment of shared parental pay be made?
      `my adoption pay period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your adoption pay period begin?
      `my adoption pay period ends` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your adoption pay period end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZV(11), may a payment of shared parental pay be made to me before my adoption pay period has ended` IS
    `s 171ZV(11) a payment may be made to the person who became entitled to statutory adoption pay` `the day of the payment` `my adoption pay period`
    WHERE
        `my adoption pay period` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `my adoption pay period begins`
            `the last day` IS `my adoption pay period ends`

-- s 171ZU(12), (13). Regulations may provide that a person entitled may vary the period or periods in which they intend to claim, where they have given notice of the intention, in time and in the prescribed form.
@export Under section 171ZU(12), may I vary the period or periods in which I intend to claim shared parental pay?
GIVEN `regulations provide for such a variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171ZU(12) allow a person who is entitled to vary the period or periods in which they intend to claim?
      `I have given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the person who will pay you notice of an intention to vary the period or periods?
      `my notice was given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your notice given by the time the regulations prescribe?
      `my notice meets the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice meet the conditions the regulations prescribe as to its form and content?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(12), may I vary the period or periods in which I intend to claim shared parental pay` IS
    `s 171ZU(12) V may vary the period or periods` `regulations provide for such a variation` (`s 171ZU(13) the conditions for varying the period or periods are satisfied` `I have given notice of an intention to vary the period or periods` `my notice was given by the prescribed time` `my notice meets the prescribed conditions as to form and content`)

-- s 171ZU(14), (15). Regulations may provide that a person entitled may vary the number of weeks, where they have given the four notices, in time and in form, and the other person (the mother, or the other adopter) consents.
@export Under section 171ZU(14), may I vary the number of weeks for which I intend to claim shared parental pay?
GIVEN `regulations provide for such a variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171ZU(14) allow a person who is entitled to vary the number of weeks for which they intend to claim?
      `I have given notice of the extent to which I have exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of how much of your entitlement you have already used?
      `I have given notice of the extent to which I intend to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of how much you intend to claim?
      `I have given notice of the extent to which the other person has exercised an entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of how much of their entitlement the other person has already used?
      `I have given notice of the extent to which the other person intends to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given notice of how much the other person intends to claim?
      `my notice was given by the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your notice given by the time the regulations prescribe?
      `my notice meets the prescribed conditions as to form and content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice meet the conditions the regulations prescribe as to its form and content?
      `the mother consents to the variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person whom the regulations name (the mother, for a mother's partner) consent to the variation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZU(14), may I vary the number of weeks for which I intend to claim shared parental pay` IS
    `s 171ZU(14) V may vary the number of weeks` `regulations provide for such a variation` (`s 171ZU(15) the conditions for varying the number of weeks are satisfied` `I have given notice of the extent to which I have exercised an entitlement` `I have given notice of the extent to which I intend to claim` `I have given notice of the extent to which the other person has exercised an entitlement` `I have given notice of the extent to which the other person intends to claim` `my notice was given by the prescribed time` `my notice meets the prescribed conditions as to form and content` `the mother consents to the variation`)

-- s 171ZX(1). The liability to pay statutory shared parental pay is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled has been an employee as mentioned in the entitlement conditions.
@export Under section 171ZX(1), is my employer liable to pay me shared parental pay?
GIVEN `I have been an employee of this employer as the entitlement conditions describe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been an employee of this employer, for the continuous period and as of the week that the entitlement conditions describe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZX(1), is my employer liable to pay me shared parental pay` IS
    `s 171ZX(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory shared parental pay` `I have been an employee of this employer as the entitlement conditions describe`

-- s 171ZY(2), (7), (8). Statutory shared parental pay is payable for each week in a relevant period (a week in a period specified in your notice and not afterwards excluded),
-- up to the number of weeks determined in your case.  Subsections (3) and (4) cut this back, and are asked separately below.
@export Under section 171ZY(2), is shared parental pay payable to me for a given week?
GIVEN `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall within a period that you specified in your notice (of the period or periods in which you intend to claim)?
      `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the week afterwards excluded from your periods by a variation you made?
      `the number of this week among my weeks paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting this week, how many weeks of shared parental pay is this (the first week is 1)?
      `the number of weeks determined in my case` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in all have been determined in your case under the regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZY(2), is shared parental pay payable to me for a given week` IS
    `s 171ZY(2) statutory shared parental pay is payable for the week` (`s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation`) `the number of this week among my weeks paid` `the number of weeks determined in my case`

-- s 171ZY(3). Except in prescribed cases, shared parental pay is not payable for a week in a relevant period if it is not your intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child.
@export Under section 171ZY(3), is shared parental pay payable to me for a week if I do not intend to care for the child?
GIVEN `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall within a period that you specified in your notice (of the period or periods in which you intend to claim)?
      `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the week afterwards excluded from your periods by a variation you made?
      `it is my intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the beginning of the week, was it your intention to care for the child?
      `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZY(3), is shared parental pay payable to me for a week if I do not intend to care for the child` IS
    `s 171ZY(3) the pay is payable for the week despite the intention to care` (`s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation`) `it is my intention at the beginning of the week to care for the child` `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception`

-- s 171ZY(4). Except in prescribed cases, shared parental pay is not payable for a week in a relevant period during any part of which you work for any employer.
@export Under section 171ZY(4), is shared parental pay payable to me for a week in which I work for an employer?
GIVEN `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall within a period that you specified in your notice (of the period or periods in which you intend to claim)?
      `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the week afterwards excluded from your periods by a variation you made?
      `I work for an employer during any part of the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work for any employer during any part of the week?
      `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZY(4), is shared parental pay payable to me for a week in which I work for an employer` IS
    `s 171ZY(4) the pay is payable for the week despite work for an employer` (`s 171ZY(7) the week falls within a relevant period` `the week falls within a period specified in my notice` `the week was afterwards excluded by a variation`) `I work for an employer during any part of the week` `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception`

-- s 171ZZ(1). An agreement is void to the extent that it purports to exclude, limit or modify any provision of Part 12ZC, or to make you contribute to your employer's costs under the Part.
@export Under section 171ZZ(1), is my agreement void to the extent that it limits my shared parental pay or makes me pay my employer's costs?
GIVEN `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of Part 12ZC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement purport to exclude, limit or otherwise change any provision of the Part on shared parental pay?
      `the agreement purports to make me contribute towards my employer's costs under Part 12ZC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement purport to make you contribute, directly or indirectly, towards costs your employer or former employer incurs under that Part?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ(1), is my agreement void to the extent that it limits my shared parental pay or makes me pay my employer's costs` IS
    `s 171ZZ(1) the agreement is void to that extent` `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of Part 12ZC` `the agreement purports to make me contribute towards my employer's costs under Part 12ZC`

§§ `Statutory parental bereavement pay (Part 12ZD)`

-- These questions arise only when a child has died or been stillborn.

-- s 171ZZ6(1), (2), (3), (5), (6), (7). A person who satisfies the conditions is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay: a bereaved parent (as prescribed), in employed earner's employment
-- for a continuous 26 weeks ending with the relevant week (the week before the week of the death), still entitled to be in it, with normal weekly earnings over 8 weeks at or above the lower
-- earnings limit, and in that employment to the day the child dies.  A stillborn child (after 24 weeks) counts, and the day of birth is the day of death (s 171ZZ15).
-- Placeholders: the rule does not read the person's date of birth, sex, marital status or pensionable age, nor the employer's kind, nor whether the job was in an office, so fixed values stand in.
@export Under section 171ZZ6(1), am I entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay?
GIVEN `the child was born dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child stillborn (born dead)?
      `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS A NUMBER @desc If the child was stillborn, after how many weeks of pregnancy did labour begin? (0 if the child was born alive)
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the child born?
      `the child has died on a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child died after being born alive?
      `the day the child died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the child die? (Give the day of birth if the child was stillborn.)
      `the child was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child under 18 when they died?
      `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks had you been in continuous employed earner's employment with your employer, up to the end of the week before the week in which the child died?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with that week?
      `I was entitled to be in that employment at the end of the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of that week, were you entitled to be in that employment?
      `my employment began on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employment with that employer begin?
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that employment ended?
      `my employment ended on` IS A DATE @desc On what day did it end? (Any date if it has not ended.)
      `I satisfy the prescribed conditions as to my relationship with the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions that the regulations prescribe as to your relationship with the child (for example, your care of the child before they died)?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the end of that week? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `the day section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day does section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 come fully into force?
      `regulations modify or disapply a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171ZZ7(4) modify or disapply any of these conditions in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ6(1), am I entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` IS
    `s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` `my case` (JUST `the child was under 18`) `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `the day section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force` `regulations modify or disapply a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case` WITH
            `the child who died` IS `the child who died`
            `the employment` IS `my employment`
            `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks`
            `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS `I was entitled to be in that employment at the end of the relevant week`
            `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child who died` IS `I satisfy the prescribed conditions as to my relationship with the child`
        `the child who died` MEANS `s 171ZZ6 the child who died` WITH
            `born dead` IS `the child was born dead`
            `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS `weeks of pregnancy when labour began`
            `the day the child was born` IS `the day the child was born`
            `the day the child died` IS IF `the child has died on a day` THEN JUST `the day the child died` ELSE NOTHING
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            `the employee` IS `me`
            -- Placeholder: the rules called do not read the kind of employer.
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS `my employment began on`
            `the employment ended on` IS IF `my employment has ended` THEN JUST `my employment ended on` ELSE NOTHING
            -- Placeholders: s 171ZZ6 does not read whether the job is held under a contract of service, in an office, or in Great Britain.
            `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
            `held in an office` IS FALSE
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `married`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

-- s 171ZZ9(2). Statutory parental bereavement pay is payable for one week, or for a number of weeks not above the prescribed number, within the qualifying period, as you choose.
@export Under section 171ZZ9(2), how much parental bereavement pay is payable to me for the weeks I choose?
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of statutory parental bereavement pay, in pounds? (The regulations prescribe it.)
      `the number of weeks I choose` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks do you choose to be paid?
      `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the largest number of weeks the regulations prescribe?
      `all my chosen weeks are within the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the weeks you choose within the qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ9(2), how much parental bereavement pay is payable to me for the weeks I choose` IS
    `s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` `the weekly rate in pounds` `the number of weeks I choose` `the prescribed number of weeks` `all my chosen weeks are within the qualifying period`

-- s 171ZZ9(8). Except in prescribed cases, statutory parental bereavement pay is not payable for a statutory pay week during any part of which you work for an employer who is not liable to pay you.
@export Under section 171ZZ9(8), is parental bereavement pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer?
GIVEN `I work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay you this pay?
      `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ9(8), is parental bereavement pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer` IS
    `s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` `I work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception`

-- s 171ZZ15(a). A reference to a child includes a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy.
@export Under section 171ZZ15(a), does my stillborn child count as a child for parental bereavement pay?
GIVEN `the child was born dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child stillborn (born dead)?
      `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS A NUMBER @desc After how many weeks of pregnancy did labour begin?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ15(a), does my stillborn child count as a child for parental bereavement pay` IS
    `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` `the child was born dead` `weeks of pregnancy when labour began`

§§ `Statutory neonatal care pay (Part 12ZE)`

-- These questions arise only when a newborn child is receiving or has received neonatal care.

-- s 171ZZ16(1), (2), (3), (4), (7). A person who satisfies the conditions, and any prescribed condition, is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay: a prescribed relationship with a child receiving neonatal care
-- (care of a prescribed kind that starts within 28 days of birth and continues without interruption for seven days), 26 weeks of employed earner's employment, and normal weekly earnings at or above the lower earnings limit.
-- Placeholders: the rule does not read the person's date of birth, sex, marital status or pensionable age, nor the employment's kind or place.
@export Under section 171ZZ16(1), am I entitled to statutory neonatal care pay?
GIVEN `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the child born?
      `the day the neonatal care started` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the child's neonatal care start?
      `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care of a medical or palliative kind that the regulations prescribe?
      `the last day of uninterrupted care` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day on which the care had continued without interruption?
      `I satisfy the prescribed conditions as to my relationship with the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you satisfy the conditions the regulations prescribe as to a parental or other personal relationship with the child?
      `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks had you been in continuous employed earner's employment with your employer, up to the end of the relevant week?
      `I was entitled to be in that employment at the end of the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the end of the relevant week, were you entitled to be in that employment?
      `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your normal weekly earnings, in pounds, over the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week?
      `regulations prescribe a further condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe a further condition under section 171ZZ16(3) for your case?
      `at the beginning of the week or period I am in the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a further condition applies: at the beginning of the week or period, are you in the employment?
      `my employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a further condition applies: has your employment been continuous from the end of the relevant week?
      `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the lower earnings limit a week, in pounds, in force at the end of the relevant week? (The Department publishes it each year.)
      `the day section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day does section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 come fully into force?
      `regulations modify or disapply a condition in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171ZZ17(4) modify or disapply any of these conditions in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ16(1), am I entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` IS
    `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `my case` `the lower earnings limit a week in force, in pounds` `the day section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force` `regulations modify or disapply a condition in my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case` WITH
            `the employment` IS `my employment`
            `the child's date of birth` IS `the child's date of birth`
            `the day the neonatal care started` IS `the day the neonatal care started`
            `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind`
            `the last day of uninterrupted care` IS `the last day of uninterrupted care`
            `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to a parental or other personal relationship with the child` IS `I satisfy the prescribed conditions as to my relationship with the child`
            `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`
            `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS `I was entitled to be in that employment at the end of the relevant week`
            `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week` IS `my normal weekly earnings over the 8 weeks`
            `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)` IS `regulations prescribe a further condition`
            `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment` IS `at the beginning of the week or period I am in the employment`
            `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week` IS `my employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week`
        `my employment` MEANS Employment WITH
            `the employee` IS `me`
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read the employment's kind, dates, or whether it is held under a contract, in an office, or in Great Britain.
            `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
            `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2020
            `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
            `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
            `held in an office` IS FALSE
            `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rules called do not read these fields.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
            `sex` IS Woman
            `marital status` IS `married`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

-- s 171ZZ19(2). Statutory neonatal care pay is payable for one week, or for a number of weeks not above the prescribed number, within the qualifying period, as you choose.
@export Under section 171ZZ19(2), how much neonatal care pay is payable to me for the weeks I choose?
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay, in pounds? (The regulations prescribe it.)
      `the number of weeks I choose` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks do you choose to be paid?
      `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the largest number of weeks the regulations prescribe?
      `all my chosen weeks are within the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the weeks you choose within the qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ19(2), how much neonatal care pay is payable to me for the weeks I choose` IS
    `s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` `the weekly rate in pounds` `the number of weeks I choose` `the prescribed number of weeks` `all my chosen weeks are within the qualifying period`

-- s 171ZZ19(8). Except in prescribed cases, statutory neonatal care pay is not payable for a statutory pay week during any part of which you work for an employer who is not liable to pay you.
@export Under section 171ZZ19(8), is neonatal care pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer?
GIVEN `I work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay you this pay?
      `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe your case as an exception to this rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ19(8), is neonatal care pay payable to me for a week in which I work for another employer` IS
    `s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` `I work during any part of the week for an employer who is not liable to pay me` `my case is one that regulations prescribe as an exception`

-- s 171ZZ16(4). Neonatal care is care of a prescribed medical or palliative kind that starts before the end of the period of 28 days beginning with the day after the child's birth.
@export Under section 171ZZ16(4), is my child's care neonatal care?
GIVEN `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the care of a medical or palliative kind that the regulations prescribe?
      `the day the care starts` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the care start?
      `the child's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the child born?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171ZZ16(4), is my child's care neonatal care` IS
    `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` `the day the care starts` `the child's date of birth`

§§ `Incapacity for work (Part XIIA)`

-- These questions arise only when the person is, or may be, incapable of work.

-- Input shaping only: the days of one unbroken series of days of incapacity, from the first to the last, as a list of dates.
GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`Under section 171B(3), the days of one unbroken series of incapacity` MEANS
    IF (Day firstDay) GREATER THAN (Day lastDay)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE firstDay FOLLOWED BY (`Under section 171B(3), the days of one unbroken series of incapacity` (Date ((Day firstDay) PLUS 1)) lastDay)

-- s 171A(1) with ss 171B to 171G. Whether you are capable or incapable of work is determined under Part XIIA unless another provision says otherwise: by regulations that treat you as capable or incapable,
-- or else by the own occupation test (if you have worked more than 8 of the last 21 weeks, and while it is carried forward through a spell of incapacity) or a personal capability assessment.
-- The day of the question is within one unbroken series of days of incapacity that began on the day the own occupation test was determined to apply and you were found incapable on it; breaks of up to 8 weeks between spells need the module's list rule.
@export Under section 171A(1), am I incapable of work on a given day?
GIVEN `the purpose is that of Part V of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question being asked for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit (Part V of the Act)?
      `the purpose is that of Part XI of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question being asked for the purposes of statutory sick pay (Part XI of the Act)?
      `the purpose is another purpose prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question being asked for another purpose that regulations exclude from this test?
      `another provision expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another provision of the Act expressly provide a different test for this purpose?
      `regulations treat me as capable of work for failing to give information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations treat a person who, without good cause, fails to give the required information or evidence as capable of work?
      `I failed to give the information or evidence required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to provide the information or evidence required, or to do so in the manner required?
      `I had good cause for that failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have good cause for that failure?
      `regulations treat me as capable of work for missing a medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations treat a person who, without good cause, fails to attend a medical examination as capable of work?
      `I was called for a medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you called to attend a medical examination in accordance with the regulations?
      `I failed to attend or submit to the medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to attend for or submit yourself to the examination?
      `I had good cause for missing the medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have good cause for that failure?
      `regulations treat me as capable of work for misconduct or refusing treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations treat a person in your case as capable of work because of misconduct or refusing treatment or rules of behaviour?
      `I became incapable through my own misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become incapable of work through your own misconduct?
      `I failed without good cause to attend for required treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail, without good cause, to attend for or submit to medical or other treatment required under the regulations?
      `I failed without good cause to observe the prescribed rules of behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail, without good cause, to observe the rules of behaviour the regulations prescribe?
      `regulations treat me as capable of work in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171D(1) treat you as capable of work in your case?
      `regulations treat me as incapable of work in my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171D(1) treat you as incapable of work in your case?
      `weeks of the last 21 in which I was engaged in remunerative work` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 21 weeks immediately before the day in question were you engaged in remunerative work?
      `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your current unbroken series of days of incapacity begin (the day the own occupation test was found to apply and you were found incapable on it)?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you want to know whether you are incapable of work?
      `regulations change the figures in section 171B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171B(8) change the 4 days or the 8 weeks in section 171B(3) in your case?
      `I am incapable by reason of a specific disease or disablement of the work of my occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement, are you incapable of doing work you could reasonably be expected to do in the occupation in which you were engaged?
      `I am incapable of work according to a personal capability assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a personal capability assessment has been carried out: does it find you incapable of work?
      `a personal capability assessment has been carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a personal capability assessment been carried out in your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171A(1), am I incapable of work on a given day` IS
    `s 171A(1) the person is incapable of work`
        (`s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` `the purpose is that of Part V of the Act` `the purpose is that of Part XI of the Act` `the purpose is another purpose prescribed by regulations`)
        (`s 171A(1) this Part determines whether the person is capable or incapable of work` `another provision expressly provides otherwise`)
        (`s 171A(2) the person is treated as capable of work` `regulations treat me as capable of work for failing to give information` `I failed to give the information or evidence required` `I had good cause for that failure`)
        (`s 171A(3) the person is treated as capable of work` `regulations treat me as capable of work for missing a medical examination` `I was called for a medical examination` `I failed to attend or submit to the medical examination` `I had good cause for missing the medical examination`)
        (`s 171E(1) the person is treated as capable of work` `regulations treat me as capable of work for misconduct or refusing treatment` `I became incapable through my own misconduct` `I failed without good cause to attend for required treatment` `I failed without good cause to observe the prescribed rules of behaviour`)
        (`s 171D(1) the treatment of the person` `regulations treat me as capable of work in my case` `regulations treat me as incapable of work in my case`)
        (`s 171C(1) the test that decides` (`s 171B(1) the own occupation test is applicable` `weeks of the last 21 in which I was engaged in remunerative work`) `the state of the own occupation test`)
        (`s 171B(2) the person is incapable of work on the own occupation test` `I am incapable by reason of a specific disease or disablement of the work of my occupation`)
        (IF `a personal capability assessment has been carried out` THEN JUST `I am incapable of work according to a personal capability assessment` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `the state of the own occupation test` MEANS
            `s 171B(3) the status of the own occupation test on the day`
                (`Under section 171B(3), the days of one unbroken series of incapacity` `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity` `the day in question`)
                `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity`
                `the day in question`
                `regulations change the figures in section 171B(3)`

-- s 171B(1). The own occupation test applies if you have been engaged in remunerative work for more than 8 weeks in the 21 weeks immediately before the day in question.
@export Under section 171B(1), does the own occupation test apply to me?
GIVEN `weeks of the last 21 in which I was engaged in remunerative work` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 21 weeks immediately before the day in question were you engaged in remunerative work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171B(1), does the own occupation test apply to me` IS
    `s 171B(1) the own occupation test is applicable` `weeks of the last 21 in which I was engaged in remunerative work`

-- s 171B(3). Once the own occupation test has been found to apply and you incapable on it, it remains applicable until the end of the spell of incapacity (4 or more consecutive days of incapacity; spells up to 8 weeks apart are one),
-- or until the 197th day of incapacity in the spell, whichever is earlier.  This question takes one unbroken series of days of incapacity.
@export Under section 171B(3), does the own occupation test still apply to me on a given day?
GIVEN `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your current unbroken series of days of incapacity begin (the day the own occupation test was found to apply and you were found incapable on it)?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you want to know?
      `regulations change the figures in section 171B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under section 171B(8) change the 4 days or the 8 weeks in section 171B(3) in your case?
GIVETH A `s 171B(3) status of the own occupation test`
DECIDE `Under section 171B(3), does the own occupation test still apply to me on a given day` IS
    `s 171B(3) the status of the own occupation test on the day`
        (`Under section 171B(3), the days of one unbroken series of incapacity` `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity` `the day in question`)
        `the first day of my unbroken series of incapacity`
        `the day in question`
        `regulations change the figures in section 171B(3)`

-- s 171B(4). A day of incapacity for work is a day on which it has been determined that you were incapable of work, or you were entitled to statutory sick pay, or (for a woman) it falls within her maternity allowance period, or regulations treat it as one.
@export Under section 171B(4), is a given day a day of incapacity for work for me?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `it has been determined that I was incapable of work on the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been determined, for any purpose of the Act, that you were incapable of work on that day?
      `I was entitled to statutory sick pay for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to statutory sick pay for that day?
      `the day falls within my maternity allowance period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall within your maternity allowance period?
      `regulations treat the day as a day of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations treat that day as a day of incapacity for work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171B(4), is a given day a day of incapacity for work for me` IS
    `s 171B(4) the day is a day of incapacity for work` `me` `it has been determined that I was incapable of work on the day` `I was entitled to statutory sick pay for the day` `the day falls within my maternity allowance period` `regulations treat the day as a day of incapacity for work`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS Person WITH
            -- Placeholders: the rule reads only the sex.
            `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
            `sex` IS IF `I am a woman` THEN Woman ELSE Man
            `marital status` IS `married`
            `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

-- s 171E(2). Any disqualification, or treatment as capable of work, under section 171E(1) is for a period not exceeding 6 weeks (42 days).
@export Under section 171E(2), may my disqualification or treatment as capable of work last a given number of days?
GIVEN `the period in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days long is the period of disqualification or of treatment as capable of work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171E(2), may my disqualification or treatment as capable of work last a given number of days` IS
    `s 171E(2) the period of the disqualification or treatment as capable of work is allowed` `the period in days`

-- s 171F(2). A councillor is, for England and Wales, a member of a London borough council, a county or county borough council, a district council, a parish or community council, the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly;
-- for Scotland, a member of a regional, islands or district council.  Work as a councillor is disregarded in deciding whether you are capable of work (s 171F(1)).
@export Under section 171F(2), am I a councillor whose work as a councillor is disregarded?
GIVEN `the part of Great Britain` IS A `s 171F(2) part of Great Britain` @desc Is the council in England and Wales, or in Scotland?
      `the kind of council` IS A `s 171F(2) kind of council` @desc What kind of council are you a member of?
      `I am a member of that council` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of that council?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171F(2), am I a councillor whose work as a councillor is disregarded` IS
    `s 171F(2) the person is a councillor` `the part of Great Britain` `the kind of council` `I am a member of that council`

-- s 171G(1). The provisions of Part XIIA do not apply for the purposes of Part V (industrial injuries), Part XI (statutory sick pay) or other purposes prescribed.
@export Under section 171G(1), does the Part on incapacity for work apply for my purpose?
GIVEN `the purpose is that of Part V of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose industrial injuries benefit (Part V of the Act)?
      `the purpose is that of Part XI of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose statutory sick pay (Part XI of the Act)?
      `the purpose is another purpose prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your purpose another purpose that regulations exclude?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 171G(1), does the Part on incapacity for work apply for my purpose` IS
    `s 171G(1) this Part applies for the purpose` `the purpose is that of Part V of the Act` `the purpose is that of Part XI of the Act` `the purpose is another purpose prescribed by regulations`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc8 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4 -- Schedules 1, 2, 3, 4A and 4B -- THE SEAT LAYER (ssc8).
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great Britain,
-- asking, on facts they can state, whether and how much they must pay in contributions, whether they are entitled to a benefit, how much, for how long,
-- and what ends or reduces it. Nothing here is new law: each question builds the records the long modules expect from plain answers and calls the
-- same rule, and no rule is restated. Every question name begins "Under schedule N paragraph M," so that no two parts' questions can share a name.
--
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text. The tables (Schedule 4 and the tables of Schedule 4A) are omitted
-- from it, so a rate, a band or a percentage that a table would give is asked of the person as a number. Rates and bands that regulations or orders set are likewise asked.
-- Schedule 4 itself has no question: it answers only the seams S2 and S34 as pass-throughs of rates the person would have to state.
--
-- A result of "no one can say from this text" is NOTHING (shown as not covered); a result of JUST FALSE is the text's own "no".
-- Where a question is for a person who may not be in the situation (an election to transfer liability, a pension from which the Secretary of State may deduct),
-- the heading says so, so that the form can ask "Has this happened to you?" first.
-- The employer's, the partner's and the Inland Revenue's positions have no seat of their own here: what the Schedules mean for them is asked from the person's side.

§ `Schedule 1 -- supplementary provisions about contributions of Classes 1, 1A, 1B, 2, 3 and 3A`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- if I work for more than one employer`

-- Only for a person who was paid by more than one employer, or twice by one, in the same week.
@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 1(1)(a), how much of what one employer paid me in a week counts as a single payment of earnings?
GIVEN `the first payment my employer made me in the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did your employer pay you in the first payment of the week, in pounds?
      `the second payment my employer made me in the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the same employer pay you in a second payment in the same week, in pounds? (0 if there was none)
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide that these payments are not to be added together?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 1(1)(a), how much of what one employer paid me in a week counts as a single payment of earnings` IS
    `sch 1 para 1(1)(a) the single payment of earnings in respect of employments under the same employer` `regulations provide otherwise` "my employer" `my payments`
    WHERE
        `my payments` MEANS LIST (`sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` OF "my employer", `the first payment my employer made me in the week in pounds`),
                                 (`sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` OF "my employer", `the second payment my employer made me in the week in pounds`)

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 1(1)(b), how much of what different people paid me in a week counts as a single payment of earnings?
GIVEN `what my first employer paid me in the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did your first employer pay you in the week, in pounds?
      `what my second employer paid me in the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did your second employer pay you in the week, in pounds?
      `my circumstances are ones that regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your circumstances ones in which regulations say earnings from different people are added together?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 1(1)(b), how much of what different people paid me in a week counts as a single payment of earnings` IS
    `sch 1 para 1(1)(b) the single payment of earnings paid by different persons in respect of different employments` `my circumstances are ones that regulations prescribe` `my payments`
    WHERE
        `my payments` MEANS LIST (`sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` OF "my first employer", `what my first employer paid me in the week in pounds`),
                                 (`sch 1 para 1 a payment of earnings` OF "my second employer", `what my second employer paid me in the week in pounds`)

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- who pays my Class 1 contributions first, and what can be taken back from me`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(1), how much of my own Class 1 contribution does my employer have to pay first, on my behalf?
GIVEN `I was paid earnings as an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were earnings paid to you as an employed earner?
      `both my and my employer's Class 1 contributions arise on that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do both primary Class 1 (yours) and secondary Class 1 (your employer's) contributions arise on that payment?
      `my case is one of the circumstances prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your case one of the circumstances in which regulations say your employer does not pay your contribution first?
      `my primary Class 1 contribution in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your own (primary) Class 1 contribution on that payment, in pounds?
      `regulations prescribe a part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations prescribe a part of your contribution that your employer pays first, instead of all of it?
      `the prescribed part in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If regulations prescribe a part, how much is it, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(1), how much of my own Class 1 contribution does my employer have to pay first, on my behalf` IS
    `sch 1 para 3(1) the primary contribution that the secondary contributor is liable in the first instance to pay`
        `I was paid earnings as an employed earner` `both my and my employer's Class 1 contributions arise on that payment`
        `my case is one of the circumstances prescribed by regulations` `my primary Class 1 contribution in pounds` `the part`
    WHERE
        `the part` MEANS IF `regulations prescribe a part` THEN JUST `the prescribed part in pounds` ELSE NOTHING

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3), how much of my Class 1 contribution that my employer has paid may my employer recover from me?
GIVEN `regulations so provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations allow your employer to recover from you the contribution it paid on your behalf?
      `the primary Class 1 contribution my employer paid or will pay for me in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your primary Class 1 contribution has your employer paid, or will it pay, on your behalf, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3), how much of my Class 1 contribution that my employer has paid may my employer recover from me` IS
    `sch 1 para 3(3) the amount the secondary contributor is entitled to recover from the earner` `regulations so provide` `the primary Class 1 contribution my employer paid or will pay for me in pounds`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3), can my employer recover what it paid in any way other than by deduction from my earnings?
GIVEN `recovery is by deduction from my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recovery by deduction from your earnings?
      `my case is a non-monetary earnings case under sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid in a form other than money (for instance a benefit in kind), including after leaving the job?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3), can my employer recover what it paid in any way other than by deduction from my earnings` IS
    `sch 1 para 3(3) the recovery is by deduction from the earner's earnings` `recovery is by deduction from my earnings` `my case is a non-monetary earnings case under sub-paragraphs (3A) to (5)`

-- Only for a person paid in a form other than money (a benefit in kind, say).
@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3B), how much of the Class 1 contribution my employer paid on my non-cash earnings may it recover from me?
GIVEN `my employer paid me earnings in a form other than money in the tax year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer pay you earnings in a form other than money in the tax year?
      `regulations allow recovery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations allow your employer to recover from you the contributions it paid on those earnings?
      `the amount regulations allow in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If regulations allow recovery, up to how much, in pounds? (0 if they do not)
      `the primary Class 1 contributions my employer paid on those earnings in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much primary Class 1 contribution did your employer pay on your behalf on those earnings, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3(3B), how much of the Class 1 contribution my employer paid on my non-cash earnings may it recover from me` IS
    `sch 1 para 3(3B) the amount the employer may recover from the employee`
        `my employer paid me earnings in a form other than money in the tax year` `the allowed amount` `the primary Class 1 contributions my employer paid on those earnings in pounds`
    WHERE
        `the allowed amount` MEANS IF `regulations allow recovery` THEN JUST `the amount regulations allow in pounds` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3A -- my employer cannot pass its own contributions on to me`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3A(1), is my employer forbidden to do this about its own contributions?
GIVEN `the contributions are` IS A `sch 1 para 3A kind of contribution` @desc Which contributions are they? One of: secondary Class 1 contributions, Class 1A contributions, Class 1B contributions, some other contributions.
      `what my employer proposes to do` IS A `sch 1 para 3A kind of act` @desc What does your employer propose to do? One of: make a deduction from earnings it pays you; otherwise recover the contributions from you, directly or indirectly; enter into an agreement with you for such a deduction or recovery; some other act.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3A(1), is my employer forbidden to do this about its own contributions` IS
    `sch 1 para 3A(1) the person liable is prohibited from the act` `the contributions are` `what my employer proposes to do`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3A(2), how much of my employer's secondary Class 1 contribution may be recovered from me under our agreement?
GIVEN `the amount our agreement allows my employer to recover in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does your agreement allow your employer to recover from you, in pounds?
      `the secondary Class 1 contribution payable on my relevant employment income in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much secondary Class 1 contribution is payable on your relevant employment income (restricted or convertible securities, or a gain treated as pay), in pounds?
      `the part of that amount that comes from securities with an artificially depressed market value or from retrospective regulations in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that amount relates to securities with an artificially depressed market value, or to contributions arising from retrospective regulations, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the day we made the agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the agreement made?
      `the day the liability arose` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the liability arise?
      `the day the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 passed? (The Act's text does not give it.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3A(2), how much of my employer's secondary Class 1 contribution may be recovered from me under our agreement` IS
    `sch 1 para 3A(2) the amount of the secondary Class 1 contribution that may be recovered under the agreement`
        `the amount our agreement allows my employer to recover in pounds`
        `the secondary Class 1 contribution payable on my relevant employment income in pounds`
        `the part of that amount that comes from securities with an artificially depressed market value or from retrospective regulations in pounds`
        `the day we made the agreement` `the day the liability arose`
        `the day the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 was passed`

§§ `Paragraph 3B -- an election to move my employer's liability on to me (only if I have made such an election)`

-- Only for a person who has made, or been asked to make, a joint election with an employer to take over the employer's liability on share-related employment income.
@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3B(3), is the election I made with my employer still in force on a given day?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to know whether the election is in force?
      `the day the election was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the election made?
      `the election ceased to have effect in accordance with its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the election cease to have effect in accordance with its own terms?
      `the day it ceased` IS A DATE @desc If it did, on what date? (any date if it did not)
      `the election was revoked jointly by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did both of you revoke the election together?
      `the day it was revoked` IS A DATE @desc If it was, on what date? (any date if it was not)
      `my employer gave me notice ending the election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer give you notice terminating the election?
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc If it did, on what date? (any date if it did not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3B(3), is the election I made with my employer still in force on a given day` IS
    `sch 1 para 3B(3) the election is in force on the day` `my election` `the day I ask about`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the in-force rule does not read the four facts that make paragraph 3B apply (joint election, transfer, approvals), so they are fixed at TRUE.
        `my election` MEANS `sch 1 para 3B an election` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `the day the election was made`,
                             `the date if it happened` `the election ceased to have effect in accordance with its terms` `the day it ceased`,
                             `the date if it happened` `the election was revoked jointly by both of us` `the day it was revoked`,
                             `the date if it happened` `my employer gave me notice ending the election` `the day the notice was given`
        `the date if it happened` MEANS GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN, day IS A DATE YIELD IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3B(8), may I appeal against the Inland Revenue's refusal or withdrawal of its approval?
GIVEN `the Inland Revenue refused the approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Inland Revenue refused the approval?
      `the Inland Revenue withdrew the approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Inland Revenue withdrawn the approval?
      `I applied for the approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply for the approval?
      `the approval was given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the approval given to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3B(8), may I appeal against the Inland Revenue's refusal or withdrawal of its approval` IS
    `sch 1 para 3B(8) the person may appeal against the Inland Revenue's decision`
        `the Inland Revenue refused the approval` `the Inland Revenue withdrew the approval` `I applied for the approval` `the approval was given to me`

§§ `Paragraphs 6 to 7B -- interest and penalties on contributions collected with tax`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 6(4), can I be required to pay interest on contributions while a decision that affects them is still to be made?
GIVEN `a decision on my contributions is due under section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a decision about your contributions due under section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999?
      `the decision will affect the interest I owe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the decision affect your liability for the interest, or its amount?
      `the decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the decision been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 6(4), can I be required to pay interest on contributions while a decision that affects them is still to be made` IS
    `sch 1 para 6(4) regulations under sub-paragraph (1) may require the interest to be paid`
        `a decision on my contributions is due under section 8, 10 or 11 of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999`
        `the decision will affect the interest I owe` `the decision has been made`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 7A(3)(b), can the Inland Revenue still impose a penalty on me for my contributions return on a given day?
GIVEN `the day the penalty was incurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the penalty incurred?
      `the day the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the penalty be imposed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 7A(3)(b), can the Inland Revenue still impose a penalty on me for my contributions return on a given day` IS
    `sch 1 para 7A(3)(b) the penalty may be imposed by the Inland Revenue on the day` `the day the penalty was incurred` `the day the penalty would be imposed`

§§ `Paragraph 10 -- paying my contributions out of my pension (only if I receive a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State)`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 10(1), may the Secretary of State pay my contributions and deduct them from my pension or allowance?
GIVEN `the class of contribution` IS A `Class of contribution` @desc Which class of contribution is it? One of: Class 1 primary, Class 1 secondary, Class 1A, Class 1B, Class 2, Class 3, Class 3A, Class 4.
      `I receive a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State under an enactment or instrument that regulations prescribe?
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 10(1), may the Secretary of State pay my contributions and deduct them from my pension or allowance` IS
    `sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State may pay the contributions and deduct the amount from the pension or allowance`
        `the class of contribution` `I receive a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument` `I consent`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 10(1), how much of my pension or allowance is left after the Secretary of State pays my contributions out of it?
GIVEN `the class of contribution` IS A `Class of contribution` @desc Which class of contribution is it? One of: Class 1 primary, Class 1 secondary, Class 1A, Class 1B, Class 2, Class 3, Class 3A, Class 4.
      `I receive a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State under an enactment or instrument that regulations prescribe?
      `I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent?
      `the pension or allowance payable in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the pension or allowance is payable to you, in pounds?
      `the contributions the Secretary of State would pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your contributions would the Secretary of State pay, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 10(1), how much of my pension or allowance is left after the Secretary of State pays my contributions out of it` IS
    `sch 1 para 10(1) the pension or allowance left after the deduction`
        (`sch 1 para 10(1) the Secretary of State may pay the contributions and deduct the amount from the pension or allowance`
            `the class of contribution` `I receive a pension or allowance from the Secretary of State under a prescribed enactment or instrument` `I consent`)
        `the pension or allowance payable in pounds` `the contributions the Secretary of State would pay in pounds`

§ `Schedule 2 -- levy of Class 4 contributions with income tax`

§§ `Paragraphs 2 and 3 -- which profits, and which reliefs (for a self-employed person)`

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 2, is this profit one on which I pay Class 4 contributions?
GIVEN `it is a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation?
      `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trade, profession or vocation carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `it is chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the profit chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 2, is this profit one on which I pay Class 4 contributions` IS
    `sch 2 para 2 the profit is one in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` `my profit`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the rule does not read the amount of the profit.
        `my profit` MEANS `sch 2 a profit` OF 0, `it is a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`, `my trade, profession or vocation is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`, `it is chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 2, what is the full amount of my profits on which Class 4 contributions are payable?
GIVEN `my first profit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your first profit, in pounds?
      `the first is of a relevant trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first profit a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation?
      `the first is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `the first is chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the first chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005?
      `my second profit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your second profit, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the second is of a relevant trade, profession or vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the second profit a profit of a relevant trade, profession or vocation?
      `the second is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the second carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom?
      `the second is chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the second chargeable to income tax under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 2, what is the full amount of my profits on which Class 4 contributions are payable` IS
    `sch 2 para 2 the full amount of the profits in respect of which Class 4 contributions are payable` `my profits`
    WHERE
        `my profits` MEANS LIST (`sch 2 a profit` OF `my first profit in pounds`, `the first is of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`, `the first is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`, `the first is chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`),
                               (`sch 2 a profit` OF `my second profit in pounds`, `the second is of a relevant trade, profession or vocation`, `the second is carried on wholly outside the United Kingdom`, `the second is chargeable under Chapter 2 of Part 2 of ITTOIA 2005`)

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 3(2), does this personal relief fail to apply in working out my Class 4 profits?
GIVEN `the relief` IS A `sch 2 para 3 relief provision` @desc Which relief is it? One of: ITA 2007 sections 64 and 72; ITA 2007 section 83; ITA 2007 section 89; Act of 1988 Chapter I of Part VII; ITA 2007 Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 3; ITA 2007 sections 457, 458 and 459; ITA 2007 section 383; ITA 2007 sections 88 and 94; sections 619 and 620; section 639; some other provision.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 3(2), does this personal relief fail to apply in working out my Class 4 profits` IS
    `sch 2 para 3(2) the relief provision does not apply` `the relief`

-- Only for a person who has a trade loss to deduct, in 1990-91 or a later year, for which relief is claimed and allowed.
@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 3(4), what are my profits for each year after a trade loss is deducted and carried forward?
GIVEN `I claim and am allowed relief for the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim relief for the loss under paragraph 3(1), and is it allowed?
      `the calendar year in which the year of the loss begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year did the tax year of the loss begin? (for 1995-96, 1995)
      `the deduction for the loss in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the deduction for the loss, in pounds?
      `my profits for that year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are your profits for that year, in pounds?
      `my profits for the next year in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are your profits for the next year, in pounds?
      `my profits for the year after that in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are your profits for the year after that, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF NUMBER)
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 3(4), what are my profits for each year after a trade loss is deducted and carried forward` IS
    `sch 2 para 3(4) the profits for each year after the loss is deducted`
        `I claim and am allowed relief for the loss` (`Tax year` OF `the calendar year in which the year of the loss begins`) `the deduction for the loss in pounds`
        (LIST `my profits for that year in pounds`, `my profits for the next year in pounds`, `my profits for the year after that in pounds`)

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- if I am in a partnership`

-- Only for a person who carries on a trade or profession jointly with others.
@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 4(1), what profits is my Class 4 liability based on?
GIVEN `the trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trade or profession carried on by two or more persons jointly?
      `my share of the partnership profits in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your share of the partnership profits, in pounds?
      `my share is immediately derived by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your share immediately derived by you from carrying on the trade or profession?
      `my share of another trade, profession or vocation in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your share of the profits of any other trade, profession or vocation, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `that share is immediately derived by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that share immediately derived by you from carrying it on or exercising it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 4(1), what profits is my Class 4 liability based on` IS
    `sch 2 para 4(1) the profits in respect of which the partner's liability arises` `the trade or profession is carried on by two or more persons jointly` `my shares`
    WHERE
        `my shares` MEANS LIST (`sch 2 para 4 a share` OF `my share of the partnership profits in pounds`, `my share is immediately derived by me`),
                              (`sch 2 para 4 a share` OF `my share of another trade, profession or vocation in pounds`, `that share is immediately derived by me`)

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- if I receive profits as a trustee`

@export Under schedule 2 paragraph 5, do I pay Class 4 contributions on profits I receive as a trustee?
GIVEN `I would otherwise be assessed to Class 4 contributions by virtue of section 8 of ITTOIA 2005 on profits I receive or can receive as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you, apart from this paragraph, be assessed and charged to Class 4 contributions under section 8 of the Income Tax (Trading and Other Income) Act 2005 on profits you receive or can receive as trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 2 paragraph 5, do I pay Class 4 contributions on profits I receive as a trustee` IS
    `sch 2 para 5 Class 4 contributions are payable on the profits received as trustee`
        `I would otherwise be assessed to Class 4 contributions by virtue of section 8 of ITTOIA 2005 on profits I receive or can receive as trustee`

§ `Schedule 3 -- contribution conditions for entitlement to benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- short-term incapacity benefit`

-- Only for a person claiming short-term incapacity benefit. The three years are the last three complete tax years before the beginning of the relevant benefit year, most recent first.
@export Under schedule 3 paragraph 2, do I satisfy the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which my relevant benefit year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the benefit year begin in which your period of incapacity for work began? (the benefit year begins on the first Sunday in January)
      `regulations take the first condition to be satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under paragraph 2(8) take the first contribution condition to be satisfied for you?
      `year 1 began in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The most recent complete tax year before the benefit year: in which calendar year did it begin?
      `year 1 lower earnings limit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that year's lower earnings limit, in pounds a week?
      `year 1 I paid contributions of a relevant class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year did you actually pay contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 1 they were paid before the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they paid before the day for which you claim benefit?
      `year 1 paid or credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were you paid or credited with contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 1 earnings credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were earnings credited to you (1987-88 or later)?
      `year 1 earnings factor from contributions paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year from contributions paid or treated as paid?
      `year 1 earnings factor with credits` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year with credited earnings added?
      `year 2 began in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The second most recent complete tax year: in which calendar year did it begin?
      `year 2 lower earnings limit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that year's lower earnings limit, in pounds a week?
      `year 2 I paid contributions of a relevant class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year did you actually pay contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 2 they were paid before the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they paid before the day for which you claim benefit?
      `year 2 paid or credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were you paid or credited with contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 2 earnings credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were earnings credited to you (1987-88 or later)?
      `year 2 earnings factor from contributions paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year from contributions paid or treated as paid?
      `year 2 earnings factor with credits` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year with credited earnings added?
      `year 3 began in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The third most recent complete tax year: in which calendar year did it begin?
      `year 3 lower earnings limit in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was that year's lower earnings limit, in pounds a week?
      `year 3 I paid contributions of a relevant class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year did you actually pay contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 3 they were paid before the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they paid before the day for which you claim benefit?
      `year 3 paid or credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were you paid or credited with contributions of a relevant class?
      `year 3 earnings credited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that year were earnings credited to you (1987-88 or later)?
      `year 3 earnings factor from contributions paid` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year from contributions paid or treated as paid?
      `year 3 earnings factor with credits` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your earnings factor for that year with credited earnings added?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 paragraph 2, do I satisfy the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit` IS
    `sch 3 pt I para 2 the contribution conditions for short-term incapacity benefit are satisfied`
        `the calendar year in which my relevant benefit year begins` `my three years` `regulations take the first condition to be satisfied`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: paragraph 2 does not read the primary threshold, the upper earnings limit, the secondary threshold or the qualifying earnings factor, so they are fixed at nil.
        `my three years` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 2 the last three complete years` OF `my year 1`, `my year 2`, `my year 3`
        `my year 1` MEANS `sch 3 pt I a year of the record` OF (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF `year 1 began in the calendar year`), `year 1 lower earnings limit in pounds`, 0, 0, 0),
                              `year 1 I paid contributions of a relevant class`, `year 1 they were paid before the relevant time`, `year 1 paid or credited`, `year 1 earnings credited`,
                              `year 1 earnings factor from contributions paid`, `year 1 earnings factor with credits`, 0
        `my year 2` MEANS `sch 3 pt I a year of the record` OF (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF `year 2 began in the calendar year`), `year 2 lower earnings limit in pounds`, 0, 0, 0),
                              `year 2 I paid contributions of a relevant class`, `year 2 they were paid before the relevant time`, `year 2 paid or credited`, `year 2 earnings credited`,
                              `year 2 earnings factor from contributions paid`, `year 2 earnings factor with credits`, 0
        `my year 3` MEANS `sch 3 pt I a year of the record` OF (`Earnings limits` OF (`Tax year` OF `year 3 began in the calendar year`), `year 3 lower earnings limit in pounds`, 0, 0, 0),
                              `year 3 I paid contributions of a relevant class`, `year 3 they were paid before the relevant time`, `year 3 paid or credited`, `year 3 earnings credited`,
                              `year 3 earnings factor from contributions paid`, `year 3 earnings factor with credits`, 0

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- widowed mother's and parent's allowance, widow's pension, Category A and B retirement pensions`

-- Only for a person claiming one of those benefits, on the contributions of the contributor concerned (yourself, or your late spouse or civil partner).
@export Under schedule 3 paragraph 5, are the contribution conditions satisfied for this benefit?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit is it? (for example: widowed mother's allowance, widowed parent's allowance, widow's pension, Category A retirement pension, Category B retirement pension)
      `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the contributor attain pensionable age?
      `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA (Category B pension)?
      `the number of relevant years that satisfy the first condition` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many years before the one in which the contributor attained pensionable age (or died under that age) were contributions actually paid and the earnings factor at least the qualifying earnings factor? (0 if none)
      `the contributor was entitled to long-term incapacity benefit in that year or the year before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contributor entitled to long-term incapacity benefit at any time in the year of attaining pensionable age (or dying under it) or the year before?
      `the allowance includes a main phase addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contributor's employment and support allowance one whose amount includes an addition under section 2(1)(b) or 4(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007?
      `the contributor was entitled to it in that year or the year before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contributor entitled to it at any time in the year of attaining pensionable age (or dying under it) or the year before?
      `the requisite number of years for a working life of that length` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years does the table for a working life of that length require? (The table is not in this text: ask the Department.)
      `the number of years of the working life that qualify` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many years of the contributor's working life were contributions paid or credited (or earnings credited) and the earnings factor at least the qualifying earnings factor?
      `the number of other years the contributor was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the other years was the contributor precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home?
      `section 23A applies to the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 23A apply to the benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 paragraph 5, are the contribution conditions satisfied for this benefit` IS
    `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied`
        `this paragraph sets out the conditions` `the first condition` `the second condition under (7)` `the second condition under (3)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph 5A applies` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `the benefit` `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA`
        `this paragraph sets out the conditions` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(1) this paragraph sets out the contribution conditions for the benefit` `the benefit` `paragraph 5A applies` `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA`
        `the first condition` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(2) the first condition is satisfied`
                                       `the number of relevant years that satisfy the first condition` `taken under (6)` `taken under (6A)`
        `taken under (6)` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(6) the first condition is taken to be satisfied` `the contributor was entitled to long-term incapacity benefit in that year or the year before`
        `taken under (6A)` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(6A) the first condition is taken to be satisfied`
                                     (`sch 3 pt I para 5(6B) the allowance is main phase employment and support allowance` `the allowance includes a main phase addition`)
                                     `the contributor was entitled to it in that year or the year before`
        `the second condition under (3)` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(3) the second condition is satisfied`
                                                  `the requisite number of years for a working life of that length` `the number of years of the working life that qualify`
        `the second condition under (7)` MEANS `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) the second condition is taken to be satisfied`
                                                  `the requisite number of years for a working life of that length` `the number of years of the working life that qualify`
                                                  `the number of other years the contributor was precluded from regular employment by responsibilities at home` `section 23A status`
        `section 23A status` MEANS IF `section 23A applies to the benefit`
                                   THEN `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A applies to the benefit`
                                   ELSE `sch 3 pt I para 5(7) section 23A does not apply to the benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 5A -- Category A and B retirement pensions: the 30-year condition`

@export Under schedule 3 paragraph 5A, is the 30-year contribution condition satisfied for this retirement pension?
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit @desc Which benefit is it? (Category A retirement pension or Category B retirement pension)
      `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the contributor attain pensionable age?
      `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA (Category B pension)?
      `the number of years of the working life that qualify` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many years of the contributor's working life were contributions paid or credited (or earnings credited) and the earnings factor at least the qualifying earnings factor?
      `regulations under sub-paragraph (4) modify the condition so that it is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations under paragraph 5A(4) modify the condition for you (contributions under the National Insurance Acts 1946 or 1965) so that it is met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 paragraph 5A, is the 30-year contribution condition satisfied for this retirement pension` IS
    `sch 3 pt I para 5A the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied`
        (`sch 3 pt I para 5A(1) this paragraph applies to the benefit` `the benefit` `the day the contributor attains pensionable age` `the case is one provided for by any of sections 48A to 51ZA`)
        (`sch 3 pt I para 5A(2) the contribution condition is satisfied` `the number of years of the working life that qualify`)
        `regulations under sub-paragraph (4) modify the condition so that it is met`

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- child's special allowance`

@export Under schedule 3 paragraph 6, is the contribution condition satisfied for a child's special allowance?
GIVEN `the number of relevant years in which the contributor paid contributions and reached 50 times the lower earnings limit` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many years before the one in which the contributor attained pensionable age (or died under that age) did the contributor actually pay contributions of a relevant class with an earnings factor of at least 50 times that year's lower earnings limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 3 paragraph 6, is the contribution condition satisfied for a child's special allowance` IS
    `sch 3 pt I para 6 the contribution conditions for a child's special allowance are satisfied`
        `the number of relevant years in which the contributor paid contributions and reached 50 times the lower earnings limit`

§ `Schedule 4A -- additional pension: accrual rates for the purposes of section 45(2)(c)`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- the amount of my additional pension`

@export Under schedule 4A paragraph 1, what is the amount for the purposes of section 45(2)(c) of my additional pension?
GIVEN `the total of the amounts for the tax years concerned in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the yearly amounts found for each tax year concerned (paragraphs 2 and 3), in pounds?
      `the number of relevant years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many relevant years are there (as section 44 counts them)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 4A paragraph 1, what is the amount for the purposes of section 45(2)(c) of my additional pension` IS
    `sch 4A para 1 the amount referred to in section 45(2)(c)` (LIST `the total of the amounts for the tax years concerned in pounds`) `the number of relevant years`

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- the amount for a year in which I was not contracted out`

-- The table of bands is omitted from the text: this question takes two bands (the second runs without an upper limit).
@export Under schedule 4A paragraph 2, what is the amount for a tax year in which my earnings factor was above the qualifying earnings factor?
GIVEN `my earnings factor has a surplus for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a surplus in your earnings factor for the year?
      `the weeks in the year in which I was contracted out` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many tax weeks in the year were you contracted out (paragraph 3(2))?
      `the surplus in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the surplus in your earnings factor for the year, in pounds?
      `the upper limit of band 1 in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc Where does the first band of the table end, in pounds of surplus? (The table is not in this text.)
      `the percentage for band 1` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage for the first band?
      `the percentage for band 2` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the percentage for the second band, which has no upper limit?
      `the percentage of the order increase` IS A NUMBER @desc By what percentage does the last order under section 148 direct earnings factors to be increased?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 4A paragraph 2, what is the amount for a tax year in which my earnings factor was above the qualifying earnings factor` IS
    `sch 4A para 2 the amount for the year`
        (`sch 4A para 2(1) Part II applies to the tax year` `my earnings factor has a surplus for the year` `the weeks in the year in which I was contracted out`)
        (`sch 4A para 2(2) the amount for the year found band by band` `the surplus in pounds` `my bands` `the percentage of the order increase`)
    WHERE
        `my bands` MEANS LIST (`sch 4A a band` OF 0, (JUST `the upper limit of band 1 in pounds`), `the percentage for band 1`),
                             (`sch 4A a band` OF `the upper limit of band 1 in pounds`, NOTHING, `the percentage for band 2`)

§ `Schedule 4B -- additional pension: accrual rates for the purposes of section 45(2)(d)`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- the amount of my additional pension`

@export Under schedule 4B paragraph 1, what is the amount for the purposes of section 45(2)(d) of my additional pension?
GIVEN `the total of the amounts for the years to which Part 2 applies in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the appropriate amounts for the relevant years to which Part 2 applies, in pounds?
      `the total of the amounts for the years to which Part 3 applies in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the appropriate amounts for the relevant years to which Part 3 applies, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 4B paragraph 1, what is the amount for the purposes of section 45(2)(d) of my additional pension` IS
    `sch 4B para 1 the amount referred to in section 45(2)(d)`
        `the total of the amounts for the years to which Part 2 applies in pounds` `the total of the amounts for the years to which Part 3 applies in pounds`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions from part ssc9 (merged by the lead on 2026-11-04; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Schedules 5 to 13 (lines 5067-5744 of the converted text).
--
-- SEAT: a person who works, is self-employed, or claims a contributory or non-contributory benefit, statutory pay or Child Benefit in Great Britain, asking, on facts
-- they can state, whether they are entitled to a benefit or to statutory pay, how much, for how long, and what ends or reduces it. In this range that person is: a
-- pensioner who deferred a retirement pension (Schedules 5 and 5A); a person whose disablement is assessed (Schedule 6); someone claiming an industrial injuries
-- benefit, or the widow, widower or child of a person who died of an industrial injury (Schedule 7); a parent or carer claiming Child Benefit (Schedules 9 and 10);
-- and an employee asking about statutory sick pay or statutory maternity pay (Schedules 11 to 13). Nothing here is new law: every question builds the modules' inputs
-- from plain answers and calls the module rules.
--
-- Every question begins "Under schedule N paragraph M," (the Act's own numbering; the converter dropped the paragraph numbers, so each is inferred and says so in the
-- module that holds it). A result of NOTHING means the text, read as the module reads it, does not answer; FALSE means the text says no in its own words. See NOTES.md,
-- "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING". Amounts that the Act leaves to Schedule 4, regulations or an order are asked as numbers the person states.
-- Questions about a person's own death, or the death of the person they depend on, are asked by the survivor, the claimant (the widow, the widower, the carer).
-- Groups that only arise in a situation the person may not be in (a deferred pension, an industrial accident, a death, a child, sick pay) say so in their comments.

§ `Schedule 5 -- pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to a retirement pension is deferred`

-- These questions only arise for someone whose Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred, or whose late spouse or civil partner's was.
-- The choice a person made is asked as a choice from a list; "no choice within the prescribed period" is the third answer and the module's default election applies.

DECLARE `Under schedule 5 My choice` IS ONE OF
    `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension`
    `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum`
    `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period`

-- What the person chose, as the module's own election (NOTHING when no choice was made in time).
GIVEN choice IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice`
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 5 Election`
`Under schedule 5 the election I made within the prescribed period` MEANS
    CONSIDER choice
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` THEN JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` THEN JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` THEN NOTHING

GIVEN choice IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice`
GIVETH A `sch 5 Election`
`Under schedule 5 the election treated as mine` MEANS
    `sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made` (`Under schedule 5 the election I made within the prescribed period` choice)

-- The widowed person's choice (paragraph 3C) has its own pair of elections.
GIVEN choice IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice`
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 5 Widowed election`
`Under schedule 5 the widowed election I made within the prescribed period` MEANS
    CONSIDER choice
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` THEN JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` THEN JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` THEN NOTHING

-- Schedule 5A has the same choice between its own two elections.
GIVEN choice IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice`
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch 5A Election`
`Under schedule 5 the shared additional pension election I made within the prescribed period` MEANS
    CONSIDER choice
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the increase of my pension` THEN JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(a) an election that paragraph 2 (the increase of pension) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I chose the lump sum` THEN JUST `sch 5A para 1(1)(b) an election that paragraph 4 (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN `Under schedule 5 I made no choice within the prescribed period` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph A1 and paragraph 1 -- my own deferred pension`

-- Paragraph A1: a person whose entitlement is deferred for at least 12 months must elect between an increase of the pension and a lump sum.
@export Under schedule 5 paragraph A1, must I choose between an increase of my pension and a lump sum?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred?
      `the first day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment begin?
      `the last day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment end (or what is the latest day you are asking about)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph A1, must I choose between an increase of my pension and a lump sum` IS
    `sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` `my period of deferment`
    WHERE
        `my period of deferment` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my period of deferment`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of my period of deferment`

-- Paragraph 1 with paragraph 2: the weekly increase is the sum of the increments for the complete six-day incremental periods, each a fraction of the weekly rate.
@export Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred?
      `the first day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment begin?
      `the last day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment end (or what is the latest day you are asking about)?
      `my choice` IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice` @desc Which did you choose, within the period the regulations allow: the increase of your pension, the lump sum, or neither?
      `the weekly rate I would have had` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of pension, in pounds, would you have been entitled to for the period if your entitlement had not been deferred?
      `the days of increment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in your period of deferment do the regulations treat as days of increment?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 1, by how much a week is my retirement pension increased because I deferred it` IS
    `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` `my period of deferment` (JUST (`Under schedule 5 the election treated as mine` `my choice`)) `the weekly rate I would have had` `the days of increment`
    WHERE
        `my period of deferment` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my period of deferment`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of my period of deferment`

§§ `Paragraph 3A -- the lump sum for my own deferred pension`

@export Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred?
      `my choice` IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice` @desc Which did you choose, within the period the regulations allow: the increase of your pension, the lump sum, or neither?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3A, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my retirement pension` IS
    `sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` `my entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension is deferred` (JUST (`Under schedule 5 the election treated as mine` `my choice`))

§§ `Paragraphs 3C, 4 and 7A -- my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension`

-- These arise only for a widow, widower or surviving civil partner whose late spouse or civil partner had deferred a Category A or B retirement pension.
@export Under schedule 5 paragraph 3C, do I, as a widowed person, have a choice between an increase and a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension?
      `I was married to or was the civil partner of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to, or the civil partner of, the person when they died?
      `their entitlement was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person's entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred when they died?
      `their pension was a Category B pension by virtue of my contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person's pension a Category B retirement pension to which they were or would have been entitled by virtue of your contributions?
      `the first day of their period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did their period of deferment begin?
      `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 3C, do I, as a widowed person, have a choice between an increase and a lump sum` IS
    `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` `I was married to or was the civil partner of the person who died` `their entitlement was deferred when they died` `their pension was a Category B pension by virtue of my contributions` `the first day of their period of deferment` `the day they died`

@export Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, by how much a week is my pension increased because my late spouse or civil partner deferred theirs?
GIVEN `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your late spouse or civil partner die?
      `they were my civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they your civil partner (not your spouse)?
      `their increase in the basic pension` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly increase in the basic pension, in pounds, were they entitled to (or would they have been) under Schedule 5, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A?
      `their increase in the additional pension` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly increase in the additional pension, in pounds, were they entitled to (or would they have been) under Schedule 5, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 4, by how much a week is my pension increased because my late spouse or civil partner deferred theirs` IS
    `sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `the day they died` `they were my civil partner` `their increase in the basic pension` `their increase in the additional pension`

@export Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension?
GIVEN `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension?
      `I was married to or was the civil partner of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you married to, or the civil partner of, the person when they died?
      `their entitlement was deferred when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person's entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension deferred when they died?
      `their pension was a Category B pension by virtue of my contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person's pension a Category B retirement pension to which they were or would have been entitled by virtue of your contributions?
      `the first day of their period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did their period of deferment begin?
      `the day they died` IS A DATE @desc On what day did they die?
      `my choice` IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice` @desc Which did you choose, within the period the regulations allow: the increase of the pension, the lump sum, or neither?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5 paragraph 7A, am I entitled to a lump sum because my late spouse or civil partner deferred their pension` IS
    `sch 5 para 7A(2) W is entitled to a widowed person’s or surviving civil partner’s lump sum` (`sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` `I was married to or was the civil partner of the person who died` `their entitlement was deferred when they died` `their pension was a Category B pension by virtue of my contributions` `the first day of their period of deferment` `the day they died`) (JUST (`sch 5 para 3C(3) the election that is treated as made` (`Under schedule 5 the widowed election I made within the prescribed period` `my choice`)))

§ `Schedule 5A -- pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred`

-- These arise only for a person whose entitlement to a shared additional pension (a pension shared on divorce or dissolution) is deferred.
@export Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a shared additional pension deferred?
      `the first day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment begin?
      `the last day of my period of deferment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of deferment end (or what is the latest day you are asking about)?
      `my choice` IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice` @desc Which did you choose, within the period the regulations allow: the increase of your pension, the lump sum, or neither?
      `the weekly rate I would have had` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of shared additional pension, in pounds, would you have been entitled to for the period if your entitlement had not been deferred?
      `the days of increment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in your period of deferment do the regulations treat as days of increment?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 5A paragraph 2, by how much a week is my shared additional pension increased because I deferred it` IS
    `sch 5A para 2 the amount by which the shared additional pension is increased for the deferment` `my entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` `my period of deferment` (JUST (`sch 5A para 1(2) the election that is treated as made` (`Under schedule 5 the shared additional pension election I made within the prescribed period` `my choice`))) `the weekly rate I would have had` `the days of increment`
    WHERE
        `my period of deferment` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day of my period of deferment`
            `the last day` IS `the last day of my period of deferment`

@export Under schedule 5A paragraph 4, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my shared additional pension?
GIVEN `my entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement to a shared additional pension deferred?
      `my choice` IS A `Under schedule 5 My choice` @desc Which did you choose, within the period the regulations allow: the increase of your pension, the lump sum, or neither?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 5A paragraph 4, am I entitled to a lump sum for deferring my shared additional pension` IS
    `sch 5A para 4(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` `my entitlement to a shared additional pension is deferred` (JUST (`sch 5A para 1(2) the election that is treated as made` (`Under schedule 5 the shared additional pension election I made within the prescribed period` `my choice`)))

§ `Schedule 6 -- assessment of extent of disablement`

-- These questions only arise for a person whose disablement from an industrial accident or disease is being assessed under section 103.
@export Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, what percentage disablement is assessed for me?
GIVEN `my loss of faculty is one that regulations prescribe as amounting to 100 per cent disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your loss of faculty one that the regulations prescribe as amounting to 100 per cent disablement?
      `the percentage my disabilities amount to` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the disabilities you have as a result of your loss of faculty amount to, compared with a person of your age and sex whose physical and mental condition is normal?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, what percentage disablement is assessed for me` IS
    `sch 6 the extent of the disablement assessed, as a percentage` `my loss of faculty is one that regulations prescribe as amounting to 100 per cent disablement` (JUST `the percentage my disabilities amount to`)

@export Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, may my assessment take a particular circumstance of mine into account?
GIVEN circumstance IS A `sch 6 Circumstance` @desc Which circumstance of yours are you asking about: your age, your sex, your physical condition, your mental condition, being right-handed or left-handed, or some other particular circumstance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 1, may my assessment take a particular circumstance of mine into account` IS
    `sch 6 para 1(c) the assessment may refer to the circumstance` circumstance

@export Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, from what day does the period taken into account by my assessment begin?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your industrial accident happen?
      `the first day I suffered the loss of faculty` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first suffer the loss of faculty?
      `the last day I may be expected to suffer it` IS A DATE @desc On what day may you be expected to stop suffering from the loss of faculty (or, if it is for life, the last day you are asking about)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, from what day does the period taken into account by my assessment begin` IS
    (`sch 6 para 6(1) the period taken into account by the assessment` `the day of my accident` `my period of suffering`)'s `the first day`
    WHERE
        `my period of suffering` MEANS Period WITH
            `the first day` IS `the first day I suffered the loss of faculty`
            `the last day` IS `the last day I may be expected to suffer it`

@export Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment?
GIVEN `my assessed extent of disablement, as a percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage is the extent of your disablement assessed at?
      `my extent is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the extent of your disablement assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period?
      `the percentage assessed for the latest part of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage is assessed for the latest part of the period (the same figure if there is only one)?
      `it seems likely that my assessed extent will be aggregated with a present disablement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it seem likely that your assessed extent will be aggregated with the assessed extent of any present disablement you have?
      `it seems likely that the aggregate will be 14 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it seem likely that the aggregate will amount to 14 per cent or more?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 6 paragraph 6, is my assessment a final assessment` IS
    `sch 6 para 6(3) the assessment is a final assessment` `my assessed extent of disablement, as a percentage` `my extent is assessed at different percentages for different parts of the period` `the percentage assessed for the latest part of the period` `it seems likely that my assessed extent will be aggregated with a present disablement` `it seems likely that the aggregate will be 14 per cent or more`

§ `Schedule 7 Part I -- unemployability supplement`

-- These questions only arise for someone who was in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6 April 1987.
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 1, does the unemployability supplement Part apply to me?
GIVEN `I was in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in receipt of unemployability supplement immediately before 6 April 1987?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 1, does the unemployability supplement Part apply to me` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 1 this Part applies to the person` `I was in receipt of unemployability supplement under section 58 of the 1975 Act immediately before 6 April 1987`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, is my disablement pension increased because I am incapable of work?
GIVEN `I am incapable of work as a result of my loss of faculty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of your loss of faculty, are you incapable of work (work you can reasonably be expected to do)?
      `I am likely to remain so permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you likely to remain incapable of work permanently?
      `my loss of faculty is likely to prevent my earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your loss of faculty likely to prevent your earnings in a year exceeding the amount the regulations prescribe?
      `the prescribed amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What yearly amount, in pounds, do the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, is my disablement pension increased because I am incapable of work` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 2(1) the weekly rate is increased` (JUST `I am incapable of work as a result of my loss of faculty`) `I am likely to remain so permanently` (`sch 7 pt I para 2(3) the beneficiary may be treated as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently` `my loss of faculty is likely to prevent my earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount` `the prescribed amount in pounds`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, by how much a week is my disablement pension increased by the unemployability supplement?
GIVEN `I am incapable of work as a result of my loss of faculty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of your loss of faculty, are you incapable of work (work you can reasonably be expected to do)?
      `I am likely to remain so permanently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you likely to remain incapable of work permanently?
      `my loss of faculty is likely to prevent my earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your loss of faculty likely to prevent your earnings in a year exceeding the amount the regulations prescribe?
      `the prescribed amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What yearly amount, in pounds, do the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
      `the increase for incapacity in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly increase, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 5 give?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 2, by how much a week is my disablement pension increased by the unemployability supplement` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 2(1) the amount of the increase` (`sch 7 pt I para 2(1) the weekly rate is increased` (JUST `I am incapable of work as a result of my loss of faculty`) `I am likely to remain so permanently` (`sch 7 pt I para 2(3) the beneficiary may be treated as incapable of work and likely to remain so permanently` `my loss of faculty is likely to prevent my earnings in a year exceeding the prescribed amount` `the prescribed amount in pounds`)) (JUST `the increase for incapacity in pounds`)

-- Paragraph 3: the age increase, less the relevant amount of any additional pension, subject to section 46(6) and (7).
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions?
GIVEN sex IS A Sex @desc Are you a man or a woman?
      `I was under 60 on the qualifying date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the qualifying date (the beginning of the first week you qualified for the supplement) were you under 60?
      `I was under 55 on the qualifying date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the qualifying date were you under 55?
      `the age increase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly amount, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 6 give as the appropriate increase?
      `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the period, are you entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension?
      `my pension includes an additional pension under section 44(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the weekly rate of your pension include an additional pension of the kind mentioned in section 44(3)(b)?
      `my weekly additional pension after any increase under section 52(3)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly additional pension, in pounds, after any increase under section 52(3)?
      `the part attributable to units of additional pension` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it, in pounds a week, is attributable to units of additional pension?
      `any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly increase, in pounds, do you get under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5?
      `the reduction made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly reduction, in pounds, has been made to your retirement pension by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act?
      `section 46(6) or (7) limits my increase` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do section 46(6) or (7) (guaranteed minimum pensions and increases of unemployability supplement) limit your increase?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 3, by how much a week is my unemployability supplement increased for my age, after the deductions` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 7 pt I para 3(1) the increase before the deductions` (`sch 7 pt I para 3(1) the beneficiary meets the age condition on the qualifying date` sex (JUST `I was under 60 on the qualifying date`) (JUST `I was under 55 on the qualifying date`)) (JUST `the age increase in pounds`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST before THEN `sch 7 pt I para 3(11) the increase subject to section 46(6) and (7)` (JUST (`sch 7 pt I para 3(2) the increase after the deduction` `I am entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` `my pension includes an additional pension under section 44(3)(b)` (`sch 7 pt I para 3(3) the relevant amount` `my weekly additional pension after any increase under section 52(3)` `the part attributable to units of additional pension` `any increase under paragraphs 1 and 2 of Schedule 5` `the reduction made by virtue of section 46 of the Pensions Act`) before)) (JUST `section 46(6) or (7) limits my increase`)

-- Paragraphs 4 to 6: the increases for children and for an adult dependant. Paragraph 4 says "subject to this paragraph and paragraph 5": the 4(1) question answers NOTHING when its own
-- conditions are met, and the paragraph 4(4) and paragraph 5 questions say what cuts it back.
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase?
GIVEN `my partner and I are spouses or civil partners residing together, or living together as if married or civil partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your partner spouses or civil partners residing together, or living together as if you were a married couple or civil partners?
      `my partner had earnings in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your partner have earnings in the week?
      `my partner's earnings in the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc How much, in pounds, did your partner earn in the week?
      `the number of my children and qualifying young persons` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many children and qualifying young persons are you entitled to child benefit?
      `the amount an order has substituted for 215 pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If an order has substituted a larger amount for £215, what is it, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the amount an order has substituted for 28 pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc If an order has substituted a larger amount for £28, what is it, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, for how many of my children does my partner's pay mean I get no increase` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 7 pt I para 4(5) the amount for the time being specified` 215 (IF `the amount an order has substituted for 215 pounds` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the amount an order has substituted for 215 pounds`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST first THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 7 pt I para 4(5) the amount for the time being specified` 28 (IF `the amount an order has substituted for 28 pounds` EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the amount an order has substituted for 28 pounds`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST further THEN JUST (`sch 7 pt I para 4(4) the number of children and qualifying young persons for whom no increase is payable` `my partner and I are spouses or civil partners residing together, or living together as if married or civil partners` `my partner had earnings in the week` `my partner's earnings in the week in pounds` `the number of my children and qualifying young persons` first further)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, is my disablement pension increased for my children and qualifying young persons?
GIVEN `I am entitled to an unemployability supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an unemployability supplement?
      `I am entitled to child benefit for one or more children or qualifying young persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to child benefit for one or more children or qualifying young persons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 4, is my disablement pension increased for my children and qualifying young persons` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 4(1) the weekly rate is increased for children` `I am entitled to an unemployability supplement` `I am entitled to child benefit for one or more children or qualifying young persons`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 5, is the condition on contributions to the cost of providing for my child satisfied?
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the contributions I make` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate, in pounds, do you contribute to the cost of providing for the child?
      `I am one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you one of two spouses or civil partners residing together?
      `the weekly rate of the contributions my spouse or civil partner makes` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate, in pounds, does your spouse or civil partner contribute?
      `the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (1) in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly amount, in pounds, must the contributions reach? (the text names none: give the figure you are told applies)
      `it is a prescribed case in which the contributions need not be over and above those required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is yours a case in which the regulations say the contributions need not be over and above those required for section 143(1)(b)?
      `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the contributions over and above those required for the purposes of satisfying section 143(1)(b)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 5, is the condition on contributions to the cost of providing for my child satisfied` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 5(2) the condition in paragraph (b) of sub-paragraph (1) is satisfied` `the weekly rate of the contributions I make` `I am one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` `the weekly rate of the contributions my spouse or civil partner makes` (JUST `the amount referred to in sub-paragraph (1) in pounds`) `it is a prescribed case in which the contributions need not be over and above those required` (JUST `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant?
GIVEN `I am entitled to an unemployability supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an unemployability supplement?
      `I am residing with my spouse or civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you residing with your spouse or civil partner?
      `my weekly contribution to the maintenance of my spouse or civil partner in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What do you contribute each week, in pounds, to the maintenance of your spouse or civil partner?
      `the increase for an adult dependant in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly amount, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 8 give?
      `someone other than my spouse, civil partner or a child has the care of children I get child benefit for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person who is neither your spouse or civil partner nor a child or qualifying young person have the care of children for whom you are entitled to child benefit?
      `the further conditions prescribed for that person are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the further conditions the regulations prescribe for that person fulfilled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 6, is my disablement pension increased for an adult dependant` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 6(1) the weekly rate is increased for an adult dependant` `I am entitled to an unemployability supplement` `I am residing with my spouse or civil partner` (`sch 7 pt I para 6(2) the beneficiary is contributing at the requisite rate` `my weekly contribution to the maintenance of my spouse or civil partner in pounds` (JUST `the increase for an adult dependant in pounds`)) `someone other than my spouse, civil partner or a child has the care of children I get child benefit for` (JUST `the further conditions prescribed for that person are fulfilled`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up?
GIVEN `I have been awarded an increase under paragraph 4 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been awarded an increase under paragraph 4 or 6?
      `I ceased to be entitled only because the other person's weekly earnings exceeded the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be entitled to the increase only because the weekly earnings of the other person exceeded the amount of the increase (or some specified amount)?
      `I would still be entitled apart from that excess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have continued to be entitled to the increase if that excess of earnings were disregarded?
      `the other person's earnings relevant to the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the other person's earnings relevant to the week, in pounds?
      `the amount of the increase or the specified amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the increase (or the specified amount), in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 8, is my increase still payable for a week when my partner's earnings have gone up` IS
    `sch 7 pt I para 8(1) the increase is payable for the week` `I have been awarded an increase under paragraph 4 or 6` `I ceased to be entitled only because the other person's weekly earnings exceeded the amount` `I would still be entitled apart from that excess` `the other person's earnings relevant to the week in pounds` `the amount of the increase or the specified amount in pounds`

§ `Schedule 7 Parts II and III -- disablement gratuity; hospital treatment`

-- These questions only arise for a person who claimed disablement benefit for an industrial accident or disease (a gratuity: a claim before 1 October 1986).
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 9, am I entitled to a disablement gratuity?
GIVEN `I am an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employed earner?
      `the day I claimed disablement benefit` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you claim disablement benefit?
      `the percentage my disablement is assessed at` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage is the extent of your disablement assessed at under Schedule 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 9, am I entitled to a disablement gratuity` IS
    `sch 7 pt II para 9(1) the employed earner is entitled to a disablement gratuity` `I am an employed earner` `the day I claimed disablement benefit` (JUST `the percentage my disablement is assessed at`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 9, from what day can a disablement gratuity be paid to me?
GIVEN `the day of my accident` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your industrial accident happen?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 9, from what day can a disablement gratuity be paid to me` IS
    `sch 7 pt II para 9(3) the first day after the 90 days` `the day of my accident`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 10, what extent of disablement is treated as assessed for me while I am an in-patient?
GIVEN `the percentage my disablement is assessed at for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage is your disablement assessed at for the period taken into account?
      `I receive in-patient treatment for my injury during that part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you receiving medical treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution for your injury or loss of faculty during that part of the period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 10, what extent of disablement is treated as assessed for me while I am an in-patient` IS
    `sch 7 pt III para 10(2) the extent treated as assessed for the part of the period` `the percentage my disablement is assessed at for the period` `I receive in-patient treatment for my injury during that part of the period`

§ `Schedule 7 Parts IV and V -- reduced earnings allowance; retirement allowance`

-- These questions only arise for an employed earner whose loss of faculty came from an industrial accident (before 1 October 1990) or a prescribed disease.
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 11, am I entitled to reduced earnings allowance?
GIVEN `I am an employed earner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employed earner?
      `I am entitled to a disablement pension, or would be if it were payable where disablement is assessed at 1 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to a disablement pension, or would you be if that pension were payable where disablement is assessed at not less than 1 per cent?
      `I am incapable, and likely to remain incapable, of my regular occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of your loss of faculty, are you incapable, and likely to remain permanently incapable, of following your regular occupation?
      `I am incapable of suitable employment of an equivalent standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of following employment of an equivalent standard that is suitable in your case?
      `I have been incapable of that occupation and any such employment since the 90 days ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, at all times since the end of the 90 days after your accident, been incapable of following that occupation or any such employment?
      `my loss of faculty results from an accident on or after 1 October 1990` IS A `sch 7 pt IV Extent` @desc Does your loss of faculty result from an accident happening on or after 1 October 1990: wholly, partly or not at all?
      `my disease was prescribed on or after 10 October 1994` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim in relation to a disease prescribed on or after 10 October 1994?
      `my disease's prescription was extended on or after 10 October 1994` IS A `sch 7 pt IV Extent` @desc Is your claim in relation to a disease prescribed before 10 October 1994 whose prescription was extended on or after that date: wholly, partly or not at all?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 11, am I entitled to reduced earnings allowance` IS
    `sch 7 pt IV para 11(1) the employed earner is entitled to reduced earnings allowance` `I am an employed earner` `I am entitled to a disablement pension, or would be if it were payable where disablement is assessed at 1 per cent or more` `I am incapable, and likely to remain incapable, of my regular occupation` `I am incapable of suitable employment of an equivalent standard` `I have been incapable of that occupation and any such employment since the 90 days ended` `my loss of faculty results from an accident on or after 1 October 1990` `my disease was prescribed on or after 10 October 1994` `my disease's prescription was extended on or after 10 October 1994`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 11, what is the highest weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance I can be paid?
GIVEN `the maximum rate of a disablement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum weekly rate of a disablement pension, in pounds (Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 1, first entry, without increases)?
      `my weekly disablement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly disablement pension do you get, in pounds, not counting any increases?
      `I retired from regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you retired from regular employment?
      `I was treated under section 27(3) of the 1975 Act as having retired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated under section 27(3) of the Social Security Act 1975 as having retired from regular employment?
      `I was deemed under section 27(5) of the 1975 Act to have retired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you deemed under section 27(5) of the Social Security Act 1975 to have retired from regular employment?
      `I retired before 6 April 1987` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that retirement before 6 April 1987?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 11, what is the highest weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance I can be paid` IS
    `sch 7 pt IV para 11(10) the highest rate of reduced earnings allowance` (JUST `the maximum rate of a disablement pension in pounds`) `my weekly disablement pension in pounds` (`I retired before 6 April 1987` AND `sch 7 pt IV para 11(12A) the person is a person who retired from regular employment` `I retired from regular employment` `I was treated under section 27(3) of the 1975 Act as having retired` `I was deemed under section 27(5) of the 1975 Act to have retired`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 13, am I entitled to retirement allowance?
GIVEN `I have attained pensionable age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you attained pensionable age?
      `the day I gave up regular employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give up regular employment?
      `I was entitled to reduced earnings allowance on the day immediately before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to reduced earnings allowance on the day immediately before you gave up regular employment?
      `my weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance, with all awards, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance (all awards added together) were you entitled to on the day before you ceased to be entitled, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 13, am I entitled to retirement allowance` IS
    `sch 7 pt V para 13(2) the person is entitled to retirement allowance` (`sch 7 pt V para 13(1) the day from which the person ceases to be entitled to reduced earnings allowance` `I have attained pensionable age` `the day I gave up regular employment` `I was entitled to reduced earnings allowance on the day immediately before` EQUALS JUST `the day I gave up regular employment`) `my weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance, with all awards, in pounds`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 13, what weekly rate of retirement allowance do I get?
GIVEN `I retired, or am deemed to have retired, on 10 April 1989` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you retire, or are you deemed to have retired, on 10 April 1989?
      `on 9 April 1989 I was entitled at a rate restricted to 40 per cent of the maximum disablement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On 9 April 1989 were you entitled to reduced earnings allowance at a rate restricted under paragraph 11(10) by reference to 40 per cent of the maximum rate of disablement pension?
      `the weekly rate at which I was last entitled to reduced earnings allowance in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc At what weekly rate, in pounds, were you last entitled to reduced earnings allowance?
      `the maximum rate of a disablement pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum weekly rate of a disablement pension, in pounds (Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 1, first entry, without increases)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 13, what weekly rate of retirement allowance do I get` IS
    CONSIDER `sch 7 pt V para 13(4) the weekly rate of retirement allowance before rounding` (`sch 7 pt V para 13(5) the weekly rate of reduced earnings allowance taken for sub-paragraph (4)` `I retired, or am deemed to have retired, on 10 April 1989` `on 9 April 1989 I was entitled at a rate restricted to 40 per cent of the maximum disablement pension` `the weekly rate at which I was last entitled to reduced earnings allowance in pounds`) (JUST `the maximum rate of a disablement pension in pounds`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST before THEN `sch 7 pt V para 13(6) the weekly rate of retirement allowance after rounding` before

§ `Schedule 7 Part VI -- industrial death benefit`

-- These questions only arise after a death from an industrial injury or disease, and only for a death before 11 April 1988 (paragraph 14). They are asked by the widow, widower or carer who claims.
@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 14, does the industrial death benefit Part apply to the death?
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the person die?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 14, does the industrial death benefit Part apply to the death` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1) this Part has effect in relation to the death` `the day of the death`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 14, may I still claim industrial death benefit?
GIVEN `the day I would claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you make the claim?
      `the day paragraph 14(1A) came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did sub-paragraph (1A) (no claim after it) come into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 14, may I still claim industrial death benefit` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 14(1A) a claim for industrial death benefit may be made` `the day I would claim` (JUST `the day paragraph 14(1A) came into force`)

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 15, am I entitled to death benefit as the widow of a person who died of an industrial injury?
GIVEN `I am the widow of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the widow of the person who died?
      `I was residing with him at his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you residing with him at his death?
      `the payments for my maintenance were provided or procured by him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the periodical payments for your maintenance provided or procured by him (whether paid by him or by another)?
      `I was receiving those payments at his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you receiving those payments at his death?
      `I was entitled to them under a court order, trust or agreement I have taken reasonable steps to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to receive them under an order of a court, a trust or an agreement that you have taken reasonable steps to enforce?
      `but for the accident I would have been receiving or entitled to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the relevant accident, would you have been receiving them or entitled to receive them?
      `the weekly amount of the payments in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly amount of the payments for your maintenance, in pounds?
      `the prescribed amount in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What minimum weekly amount, in pounds, do the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 15, am I entitled to death benefit as the widow of a person who died of an industrial injury` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 15(1) the widow is entitled to death benefit` `I am the widow of the person who died` `I was residing with him at his death` `the payments for my maintenance were provided or procured by him` `I was receiving those payments at his death` `I was entitled to them under a court order, trust or agreement I have taken reasonable steps to enforce` `but for the accident I would have been receiving or entitled to them` `the weekly amount of the payments in pounds` `the prescribed amount in pounds`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 15, is my widow's pension payable on a given day?
GIVEN `I am entitled to death benefit as the widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to death benefit as the widow of the person who died?
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what day did he die?
      `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you remarried or formed a civil partnership?
      `the day I did` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you remarry or form the civil partnership?
      `I am living as a married couple with someone I am not married to or in a civil partnership with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living as a married couple with a person you are not married to or in a civil partnership with?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking whether the pension is payable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 15, is my widow's pension payable on a given day` IS
    IF `sch 7 pt VI para 15(3) the pension may be payable for the period` `I am living as a married couple with someone I am not married to or in a civil partnership with` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `sch 7 pt VI para 15(2) the pension is payable on the day` (JUST `I am entitled to death benefit as the widow`) `the day of the death` (IF `I have remarried or formed a civil partnership` THEN JUST `the day I did` ELSE NOTHING) NOTHING `the day I am asking about`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 16, what weekly rate of widow's pension do I get on a given day?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc On what day did he die?
      `the initial rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly initial rate, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 10 give?
      `the higher permanent rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly higher permanent rate, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 10 give?
      `the lower permanent rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly lower permanent rate, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 10 give?
      `I am entitled to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 for the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For that day, are you entitled (or treated by regulations as entitled) to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18?
      `I was over 50 at his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you over 50 at his death?
      `I was entitled to such an allowance for some period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to such an allowance for some period?
      `I was over 40 at the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you over 40 at the end of the period for which you were entitled to such an allowance?
      `I was permanently incapable of self-support at his death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At his death, were you permanently incapable of self-support?
      `I am pregnant by him` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant by him?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 16, what weekly rate of widow's pension do I get on a given day` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 16 the weekly rate of the widow's pension on the day` `the day I am asking about` `the day of the death` (JUST `the initial rate in pounds`) (JUST `the higher permanent rate in pounds`) (JUST `the lower permanent rate in pounds`) `I am entitled to an allowance for children or qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 for the day` (`sch 7 pt VI para 16(2)(b) the widow's age brings the higher permanent rate` (JUST `I was over 50 at his death`) `I was entitled to such an allowance for some period` (JUST `I was over 40 at the end of that period`)) `I was permanently incapable of self-support at his death` `I am pregnant by him`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 17, am I entitled to death benefit as the widower of a person who died of an industrial injury?
GIVEN `I am the widower of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the widower of the person who died?
      `at her death I was wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would but for the accident have been` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At her death, were you being wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would you but for the relevant accident have been so maintained?
      `at her death I was permanently incapable of self-support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At her death, were you permanently incapable of self-support?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 17, am I entitled to death benefit as the widower of a person who died of an industrial injury` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 17(1) the widower is entitled to death benefit` `I am the widower of the person who died` `at her death I was wholly or mainly maintained by her, or would but for the accident have been` `at her death I was permanently incapable of self-support`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, do I meet the conditions for an allowance for a child of the person who died?
GIVEN `at his death he was entitled to child benefit for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At his death, was the person who died entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person?
      `I am his widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you his widow?
      `I am entitled to death benefit other than a gratuity under paragraphs 15 and 16` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the period, are you entitled to death benefit other than a gratuity as his widow?
      `I am entitled to child benefit for the child for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the period, are you entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person?
      `I am a person prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 18, do I meet the conditions for an allowance for a child of the person who died` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 18(1) the person satisfies the conditions for an allowance for the child` `at his death he was entitled to child benefit for the child` `I am his widow` (JUST `I am entitled to death benefit other than a gratuity under paragraphs 15 and 16`) `I am entitled to child benefit for the child for the period` `I am a person prescribed for this purpose`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 19, if two people claim the allowance for the same child, am I the one entitled?
GIVEN `two or more of us satisfy the conditions for the allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do two or more people satisfy the conditions for an allowance under paragraph 18 for the same child for the period?
      `I am the widow or widower, entitled to death benefit as such, and meet the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the widow or widower of the person who died, entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and do you satisfy the conditions for the allowance?
      `another claimant is the widow or widower, entitled as such, and meets the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another claimant the widow or widower of the person who died, entitled to death benefit as such for the period, and satisfying the conditions for the allowance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 19, if two people claim the allowance for the same child, am I the one entitled` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 19 the person is the one entitled to the allowance for the child` `two or more of us satisfy the conditions for the allowance` `I am the widow or widower, entitled to death benefit as such, and meet the conditions` `another claimant is the widow or widower, entitled as such, and meets the conditions`

@export Under schedule 7 paragraph 20, is the death of a person with constant attendance allowance regarded as caused by the injury?
