      `at death the person was entitled to a section 104 increase of a disablement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the person died, were they entitled to an increase of a disablement pension under section 104 (constant attendance), paid as an increase of that pension (not for constant attendance under paragraph 7(2)(b) of Schedule 8)?
      `the amount of the increase in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the weekly amount of that increase, in pounds?
      `the amount specified in Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 2(a) in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What weekly amount, in pounds, does Schedule 4 Part V paragraph 2(a) specify?
      `they would have been so entitled but for in-patient treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would they have been so entitled but for having received medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
