      `the percentage their disablement was assessed at` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage was their disablement assessed at for such a period?
      `the percentage it would have been assessed at if their condition had been normal apart from those diseases` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage would it have been assessed at had their physical condition at the time of the assessment been normal, apart from those diseases?
      `regulations provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations provide otherwise for the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 7 paragraph 21, is the death of a person with a pulmonary disease treated as caused by that disease` IS
    `sch 7 pt VI para 21 the death is treated as caused by the disease for which the benefit was payable` `the day of the death` `they died as a result of a pulmonary disease` `they were entitled to disablement benefit for pneumoconiosis, byssinosis or both with tuberculosis` (JUST `the percentage their disablement was assessed at`) (JUST `the percentage it would have been assessed at if their condition had been normal apart from those diseases`) `regulations provide otherwise`

§ `Schedule 9 -- exclusions from entitlement to child benefit`

-- These questions only arise for a person claiming child benefit for a child or qualifying young person.
