      `the child is under a compulsory supervision order and residing in a residential establishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that week is the child subject to a compulsory supervision order (Children's Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011, section 83) and residing in a residential establishment (section 202(1) of that Act)?
      `the child is in the care of a local authority in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In that week is the child in the care of a local authority in circumstances the regulations prescribe?
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations otherwise provide for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 9 paragraph 1, can I get child benefit for a week when the child is detained or in care` IS
    `sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` `the child is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` `the child is under a compulsory supervision order and residing in a residential establishment` `the child is in the care of a local authority in prescribed circumstances` `regulations otherwise provide`

@export Under schedule 9 paragraph 3, can I get child benefit for a child who is married or a civil partner?
GIVEN `the child is married or is a civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child or qualifying young person married or a civil partner?
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations otherwise provide for your case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 9 paragraph 3, can I get child benefit for a child who is married or a civil partner` IS
    `sch 9 para 3 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person` `the child is married or is a civil partner` `regulations otherwise provide`

§ `Schedule 10 -- priority between persons entitled to child benefit`

-- These questions only arise when two people are entitled to, or claim, child benefit for the same child in the same week.
DECLARE `Under schedule 10 My place in the claim` IS ONE OF
    `Under schedule 10 I have already been awarded child benefit for that week when the other person claimed`
    `Under schedule 10 I am the one claiming and the other person has already been awarded it`
    `Under schedule 10 neither of us has been awarded it yet`

DECLARE `Under schedule 10 Our election` IS ONE OF
    `Under schedule 10 we have jointly elected me`
    `Under schedule 10 we have jointly elected the other person`
    `Under schedule 10 we have not jointly elected`

DECLARE `Under schedule 10 The Secretary of State's decision` IS ONE OF
    `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has decided in my favour`
    `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has decided in the other person's favour`
    `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has not decided`

@export Under schedule 10 paragraphs 1 to 5, as between me and the other person, am I the one entitled to child benefit for the child?
GIVEN `my place in the claim` IS A `Under schedule 10 My place in the claim` @desc Has child benefit for that child and week already been awarded to you when the other person claimed, are you the one claiming when it has already been awarded to them, or has neither of you been awarded it yet?
      `the weeks by which the week claimed for is after the week of the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many weeks does the week the claim relates to fall after the week in which the claim was made?
      `I am entitled by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the week, are you entitled to child benefit because the child is living with you (section 143(1)(a))?
      `I am entitled by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the week, are you entitled because you contribute to the child's cost at the required rate (section 143(1)(b))?
      `the other person is entitled by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person entitled because the child is living with them (section 143(1)(a))?
      `the other person is entitled by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person entitled because they contribute to the child's cost at the required rate (section 143(1)(b))?
      `I am a woman or a man` IS A Sex @desc Are you a man or a woman?
      `we are a man and a woman, married or civil partners, residing together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person a man and a woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and residing together?
      `I am a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent of the child or qualifying young person?
      `the other person is a parent of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a parent of the child or qualifying young person?
      `we are residing together and both parents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and the other person residing together, and both parents of the child?
      `I am the mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the child's mother?
      `the other person is the mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person the child's mother?
      `our election` IS A `Under schedule 10 Our election` @desc Have you and the other person jointly elected who is to be entitled, and if so which of you?
      `the election was made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the election made in the prescribed manner?
      `the Secretary of State's decision` IS A `Under schedule 10 The Secretary of State's decision` @desc If you did not elect, has the Secretary of State decided who is to be entitled, and if so whom?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 10 paragraphs 1 to 5, as between me and the other person, am I the one entitled to child benefit for the child` IS
    BRANCH
        IF known para1 THEN para1
        IF known para2 THEN para2
        IF known para3 THEN para3
        IF known para4a THEN para4a
        IF known para4b THEN para4b
        OTHERWISE para5
    WHERE
        known result MEANS NOT (result EQUALS NOTHING)
        para1 MEANS
            CONSIDER `my place in the claim`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 I have already been awarded child benefit for that week when the other person claimed` THEN `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims` `the weeks by which the week claimed for is after the week of the claim`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 I am the one claiming and the other person has already been awarded it` THEN `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming` `the weeks by which the week claimed for is after the week of the claim`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 neither of us has been awarded it yet` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 speaks of a person to whom child benefit "has already been awarded"
        decided1 MEANS known para1
        para2 MEANS `sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` decided1 `I am entitled by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)` `I am entitled by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)` `the other person is entitled by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)` `the other person is entitled by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)`
        decided2 MEANS decided1 OR known para2
        para3 MEANS `sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` decided2 `we are a man and a woman, married or civil partners, residing together` `I am a woman or a man`
        decided3 MEANS decided2 OR known para3
        para4a MEANS `sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` decided3 `I am a parent of the child` `the other person is a parent of the child`
        para4b MEANS `sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` decided3 `we are residing together and both parents` `I am the mother` `the other person is the mother`
        decided4 MEANS decided3 OR known para4a OR known para4b
        theElection MEANS
            CONSIDER `our election`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 we have jointly elected me` THEN `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 we have jointly elected the other person` THEN `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the other person`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 we have not jointly elected` THEN `sch 10 para 5 the persons have not jointly elected`
        theDecision MEANS
            CONSIDER `the Secretary of State's decision`
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has decided in my favour` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has decided in the other person's favour` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `Under schedule 10 the Secretary of State has not decided` THEN NOTHING
        para5 MEANS `sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` decided4 theElection `the election was made in the prescribed manner` theDecision

§ `Schedule 11 -- circumstances in which periods of entitlement to statutory sick pay do not arise`

-- These questions only arise for an employee asking about statutory sick pay for a period of incapacity for work.
@export Under schedule 11 paragraph 1, does the Schedule stop a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay from arising for my sickness?
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE @desc On what date would your period of entitlement to statutory sick pay begin under section 153 if Schedule 11 did not stop it?
      `I had a day in the 57 days before the relevant date when I was entitled to incapacity benefit (or would have been)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the 57 days ending immediately before that date, did you have at least one day on which you were entitled to incapacity benefit (or would have been, had you satisfied the contribution conditions in section 30A(2)(a))?
      `the day I attain pensionable age` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you (or did you) attain pensionable age?
      `I am entitled to incapacity benefit at the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the relevant date, are you entitled to incapacity benefit?
      `after the relevant date there was a day I was not entitled to incapacity benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the relevant date, was there a day on which you were not entitled to incapacity benefit?
      `the first such day` IS A DATE @desc What was the first such day?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `I had a day in the 85 days before the relevant date when I was entitled to employment and support allowance (or would have been)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the 85 days ending immediately before the relevant date, did you have at least one day on which you were entitled to an employment and support allowance (or would have been, had you satisfied the requirements in section 1(2) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007)?
      `I have done no work for my employer under my new contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you done no work for your employer under your contract of service?
      `I have done no work under my previous contract with the same employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you had a previous contract of service with the same employer, have you done no work under it?
      `I had a previous contract with the same employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a previous contract of service with the same employer?
      `the day my previous contract ceased to have effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the previous contract cease to have effect?
      `the day my new contract is to take effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your new contract to take effect?
      `there is a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at my place of employment on the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the relevant date, is there a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at your place of employment?
      `I prove that I never had a direct interest in the trade dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that at no time on or before the relevant date did you have a direct interest in the trade dispute?
      `I am or have been pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, pregnant?
      `the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the relevant date fall within the disqualifying period (within the meaning of section 153(12))?
      `my pregnancy terminated before the disqualifying period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your pregnancy terminate before the beginning of the disqualifying period?
      `my pregnancy terminated otherwise than by confinement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your pregnancy terminate otherwise than by confinement (as defined for statutory maternity pay in section 171(1))?
      `another circumstance the regulations prescribe applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another circumstance that the regulations prescribe apply to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 11 paragraph 1, does the Schedule stop a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay from arising for my sickness` IS
    `sch 11 para 1 a period of entitlement may arise`
        (`sch 11 para 2(d)(i) applies on the day` (`sch 11 para 2(d)(i) the employee had such a day in the 57 days` `the relevant date` incapacityBenefitDays) `the relevant date` `the day I attain pensionable age` `I am entitled to incapacity benefit at the relevant date` laterNonEntitlementDays `the day I am asking about`)
        (`sch 11 para 2(dd) the circumstance applies` `the relevant date` employmentAndSupportDays)
        (`sch 11 para 2(f) the circumstance applies` (`sch 11 para 2(f) the employee has done no work for the employer under the contract of service` `I have done no work for my employer under my new contract` `I have done no work under my previous contract with the same employer` previousCeased `the day my new contract is to take effect`))
        (`sch 11 para 2(g) the circumstance applies` `there is a stoppage of work due to a trade dispute at my place of employment on the relevant date` `I prove that I never had a direct interest in the trade dispute`)
        (`sch 11 para 2(h) the circumstance applies` `I am or have been pregnant` `the relevant date falls within the disqualifying period` `my pregnancy terminated before the disqualifying period began` `my pregnancy terminated otherwise than by confinement`)
        `another circumstance the regulations prescribe applies`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder days: paragraph 2(d)(i) and 2(dd) read only WHETHER there is a qualifying day in the window, so the day before the relevant date stands for it.
        incapacityBenefitDays MEANS IF `I had a day in the 57 days before the relevant date when I was entitled to incapacity benefit (or would have been)` THEN LIST (`the relevant date` MINUS 1) ELSE EMPTY
        employmentAndSupportDays MEANS IF `I had a day in the 85 days before the relevant date when I was entitled to employment and support allowance (or would have been)` THEN LIST (`the relevant date` MINUS 1) ELSE EMPTY
        laterNonEntitlementDays MEANS IF `after the relevant date there was a day I was not entitled to incapacity benefit` THEN LIST `the first such day` ELSE EMPTY
        previousCeased MEANS IF `I had a previous contract with the same employer` THEN JUST `the day my previous contract ceased to have effect` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Schedules 12 and 13 -- statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay with benefits and other payments`

-- Schedule 12 only arises for an employee who had statutory sick pay, and Schedule 13 only for a woman who had statutory maternity pay.
@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 1, does a day I got statutory sick pay for count as a day of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a day of incapacity for work in relation to a contract of service?
      `the day falls within a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day fall within a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay (whether or not it is also a qualifying day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 1, does a day I got statutory sick pay for count as a day of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit` IS
    `sch 12 para 1 the day counts as a day of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit` `the day is a day of incapacity for work in relation to a contract of service` `the day falls within a period of entitlement to statutory sick pay`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 2, how much contractual pay is still owed to me for a day after statutory sick pay was paid?
GIVEN `my employer's liability to pay me contractual remuneration for the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How much contractual remuneration, in pounds, does your employer owe you for the day?
      `the statutory sick pay paid for the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How much statutory sick pay, in pounds, did your employer pay for the day?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 2, how much contractual pay is still owed to me for a day after statutory sick pay was paid` IS
    `sch 12 para 2(2)(b) the contractual remuneration still owed for the day` `my employer's liability to pay me contractual remuneration for the day` `the statutory sick pay paid for the day`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 2, how much statutory sick pay is still owed to me for a day after contractual pay was paid?
GIVEN `my employer's liability to pay me statutory sick pay for the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How much statutory sick pay, in pounds, does your employer owe you for the day?
      `the contractual remuneration paid for the day` IS A NUMBER @desc How much contractual remuneration, in pounds, did your employer pay you for the day?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 2, how much statutory sick pay is still owed to me for a day after contractual pay was paid` IS
    `sch 12 para 2(2)(a) the statutory sick pay still owed for the day` `my employer's liability to pay me statutory sick pay for the day` `the contractual remuneration paid for the day`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 3, after my statutory sick pay ended, is the day part of a period of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `the number of the day counted from the day after my period of entitlement ended` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the day after your period of entitlement ended as day 1, which day are you asking about?
      `every day from the first to this one is a day of incapacity for work and not covered by another employer's statutory sick pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every day from the first to that day a day of incapacity for work in relation to you, and not a day to which paragraph 1 applies by reason of an entitlement as between you and another employer?
      `it is a prescribed case in which the paragraph does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is yours a prescribed case in which the paragraph does not apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 3, after my statutory sick pay ended, is the day part of a period of incapacity for work for incapacity benefit` IS
    `sch 12 para 3(2) the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` `the number of the day counted from the day after my period of entitlement ended` `every day from the first to this one is a day of incapacity for work and not covered by another employer's statutory sick pay` `it is a prescribed case in which the paragraph does not apply`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 4, is incapacity benefit payable for a day within 57 days after my statutory sick pay ended without the first three days being left out?
GIVEN `the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day, or does it form part of, a period of incapacity for work?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the day my period of entitlement ended` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your period of entitlement to statutory sick pay end?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 4, is incapacity benefit payable for a day within 57 days after my statutory sick pay ended without the first three days being left out` IS
    `sch 12 para 4(1) section 30A(3) does not apply to the day` `the day is or forms part of a period of incapacity for work` `the day I am asking about` `the day my period of entitlement ended`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 5, does the rule about statutory sick pay days apply to the conditions for widows' and widowers' incapacity benefit?
GIVEN `I am asking about the conditions in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking whether the conditions specified in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3) are satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 5, does the rule about statutory sick pay days apply to the conditions for widows' and widowers' incapacity benefit` IS
    `sch 12 para 5 paragraph 1 applies` `I am asking about the conditions in section 40(3) or (4) or section 41(2) or (3)`

@export Under schedule 12 paragraph 6, does the rule about statutory sick pay days apply to my unemployability supplement?
GIVEN `I am asking about paragraph 3 of Schedule 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking about paragraph 3 of Schedule 7 (the qualifying date for unemployability supplement)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 12 paragraph 6, does the rule about statutory sick pay days apply to my unemployability supplement` IS
    `sch 12 para 6 paragraph 1 applies` `I am asking about paragraph 3 of Schedule 7`

